window.REPORT = {"updated":"2026-11-19","version":"0.1 — first assembly, research still landing","sections":[{"id":"findings-index","tab":"overview","kicker":"Start here","kicker_zh":"從這裡開始","title":"10 findings, and where to read each one","title_zh":"10 個發現，以及各自該讀哪一頁","lede":"The 2026 Best Wiki winners all build a layer like this — each claim in two sentences, with a link straight to the evidence. It works, so this report does it too.","lede_zh":"2026 年所有最佳 Wiki 得主都建了一層像這樣的東西——每個主張兩句話，附上直達證據的連結。它有效，所以這份報告也這麼做。","cards":[{"kicker":"Modelling","kicker_zh":"建模","title":"Closing the model–data loop is the single best predictor of a Top 10","title_zh":"閉合模型與資料的迴圈，是 Top 10 最強的單一預測因子","body":"Teams that both fit a model to their own measured data and validate it against something held back reached a Top 10 at **53%**; teams that did not, at **23%** — less than half the rate. All nine who closed the loop without a Top 10 won or were nominated for a major special prize anyway. It needs no GPU and no licence.","body_zh":"既以自身量測資料擬合模型、又用保留資料加以驗證的團隊，進入 Top 10 的比例是 **53%**；沒有這麼做的則是 **23%**，不到一半。閉合了迴圈卻未進 Top 10 的那九支，全都拿下或入圍了重要特別獎。這件事不需要 GPU，也不需要授權。","chips":["53% vs 23%"],"link":"drylab"},{"kicker":"High school","kicker_zh":"高中組","title":"At high-school level the gap is evaluation discipline, not tools","title_zh":"在高中層級，差距在評估紀律，不在工具","body":"Eton-College-UK used logistic regression and a PSSM but ran cluster-aware cross-validation, a label-shuffle control and an ablation. Lambert-GA won Best Model for benchmarking the confidence metrics themselves and publishing that its own hit was not top-scoring. GCGS reached the Top 10 with no model page at all.","body_zh":"Eton-College-UK 用的是 logistic regression 與 PSSM，但做了分群感知的交叉驗證、標籤洗牌對照與消融測試。Lambert-GA 拿下最佳模型，是因為他們對信心指標本身做了基準測試，並公開自己成功的設計其實分數不是最高的。GCGS 則在完全沒有 model 頁的情況下進入 Top 10。","chips":["all free tools"],"link":"drylab"},{"kicker":"Software","kicker_zh":"軟體","title":"8 of 21 award-winning tools are still usable, and the reason is hosting","title_zh":"21 個得獎工具中有 8 個仍可使用，原因是「有沒有架站」","body":"Every live tool was hosted on wiki-freeze day; every source-only tool's wiki lists localhost as its only address. Not a coding or budget decision — a hosting decision made months early. Two high-school teams out-shipped most of the universities. Stars and forks across every repo checked: zero.","body_zh":"每一個仍在線的工具，在 wiki 凍結當日就已經上線；每一個只有原始碼的工具，wiki 上唯一的位址都是 localhost。這不是寫程式或預算的決定，而是提前好幾個月做的架站決定。兩支高中隊伍交付得比多數大學還好。所有檢查過的 repository，star 與 fork 都是零。","chips":["hosted on freeze day"],"link":"drylab"},{"kicker":"Visualisation","kicker_zh":"視覺化","title":"The best figures build the reader's doubt into the picture","title_zh":"最好的圖，把讀者的懷疑畫進圖裡","body":"GEMS-Taiwan's provenance rail turns amber exactly where measurement stops and modelling begins. DKU gives \"not assessed\" its own verdict so an unmeasured gate cannot read as a passed one. Mingdao's captions carry the instrument, the buffer, the replicate count and a link to the raw CSV. DTU shows which stakeholders never replied.","body_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 的來源軌道，正好在量測結束、模擬開始之處轉為琥珀色。DKU 給「未評估」一個自己的判定，讓未量測的關卡不會被讀成通過。Mingdao 的圖說載明儀器、緩衝液、重複次數，並連結原始 CSV。DTU 則把從未回覆的利害關係人也顯示出來。","chips":["provenance visible","\"not assessed\" as a state"],"link":"drylab"},{"kicker":"Human practices","kicker_zh":"人類實踐","title":"The loops that closed were closed by experts, not by publics","title_zh":"真正閉合的迴圈，是專家閉合的，不是公眾","body":"Of all 106 decorated teams, **71** can point at a stakeholder who visibly changed the design. But almost every one of those stakeholders was a credentialled technical expert. The publics, patients and communities the criterion is rhetorically about changed the vocabulary and not the vector, with **nine or ten exceptions in 106**. (The first pass scored 93 files and found 64 and six-to-seven; the figures here are the recount on the closed set.)","body_zh":"在全部 106 支獲獎隊伍中，有 **71** 支能指出一位明顯改變了設計的利害關係人。但這些利害關係人幾乎全是具備專業資格的技術專家。這個評審標準修辭上所指向的公眾、病人與社群，改變的是詞彙而不是方向——**106 支中只有九到十個例外**。（第一輪評的是 93 份檔案，得到 64 支與六到七個例外；這裡的數字是集合封閉後的重算。）","chips":["71 of 106","9–10 exceptions"],"link":"good"},{"kicker":"Engagement","kicker_zh":"公眾參與","title":"The best education work was designed from data and measured like an experiment","title_zh":"最好的教育工作，是從資料設計、像實驗一樣量測的","body":"UCAS-China made compliance the target after a 461-person questionnaire, not awareness. GU Frankfurt sent nineteen members to a professional science-communication course first. Oxford built a podcast that deliberately pairs stakeholders who disagree. And the sharpest teams publish the lesson that failed.","body_zh":"UCAS-China 在做完 461 人的問卷後，把目標設為服藥遵從性，而不是認知提升。GU Frankfurt 先送 19 位成員去上專業的科學傳播課程。Oxford 做了一個刻意把意見相左者配對的 podcast。而最犀利的團隊，會把失敗的那堂課也公布出來。","chips":["survey-designed","measured"],"link":"good"},{"kicker":"Commercial","kicker_zh":"商業","title":"The credible commercial sections published a model showing their own product losing","title_zh":"可信的商業章節，都公開了顯示自家產品輸掉的模型","body":"Worldshaper-Shanghai reports a negative NPV for its own enzyme. DTU-Denmark's LCA finds cement co-processing beats its route on almost every indicator, then converts each loss into an engineering target. Stockholm dismantled its venture when the safety board killed open-water release — and won the Safety and Security Award.","body_zh":"Worldshaper-Shanghai 報告自家酵素得出負的 NPV。DTU-Denmark 的 LCA 發現水泥共處理在幾乎每項指標上都勝過他們的路線，接著把每一項落敗轉成工程目標。Stockholm 在安全委員會否決開放水域釋放後拆掉了自己的創業計畫——然後拿下安全與保安獎。","chips":["negative NPV, published"],"link":"good"},{"kicker":"Wiki craft","kicker_zh":"Wiki 工藝","title":"Best Wiki winners ship an executive layer, not better graphics","title_zh":"最佳 Wiki 得主交付的是一個導讀層，不是更漂亮的圖","body":"Three of the four serve text that is readable before any script runs; the fourth mirrors every page as Markdown. All four build a layer that answers each medal criterion in two or three sentences and deep-links the evidence, failures included. Dark mode, late alt-text sweeps and mascot systems correlate with nothing.","body_zh":"四位得主中有三位提供的文字在任何程式執行前就可閱讀；第四位則把每一頁都鏡像為 Markdown。四位都建了一層用兩三句話回答每項獎牌標準、並直接深連到證據（含失敗）的導讀層。深色模式、最後才補的替代文字、吉祥物系統，則與得獎毫無相關。","chips":["text before JS","/judging page"],"link":"teams"},{"kicker":"Taiwan","kicker_zh":"台灣","title":"Taiwan won well, but only in the high-school tier","title_zh":"台灣贏得不錯，但只贏在高中組","body":"Thirteen competing teams returned six award wins — more than any East Asian territory except China, and more than Hong Kong on fewer teams. But every technical award came from the high-school tier, there were zero nominations in any parts award and zero in Best Software, and Hong Kong tripled Taiwan's Top 10 count.","body_zh":"13 支參賽隊伍拿下 6 座獎項——多於中國以外的任何東亞地區，而且以更少的隊伍數超越香港。但所有技術類獎項都來自高中組，在任何元件獎與最佳軟體上都掛零，而香港的 Top 10 席次是台灣的三倍。","chips":["13 teams · 6 wins"],"link":"teams"},{"kicker":"Human practices","kicker_zh":"人文實踐","title":"The divide is not medical versus agricultural — it is platform versus applied","title_zh":"分界不在醫療與農業之間，而在平台與應用之間","body":"Therapeutics teams close loops with non-experts about as often as bioremediation teams do. What actually separates the field is whether anyone outside a lab ever operates the thing: across the platform villages — Foundational Advance, Space, Software & AI, Biomanufacturing — **2 of 26** decorated teams closed a design loop at all, against **14 of 45** in the applied villages.","body_zh":"治療類團隊與生物復育類團隊，和非專業人士閉合迴路的頻率其實差不多。真正分開這個領域的，是有沒有實驗室以外的人實際操作這個東西：在平台類賽道——Foundational Advance、Space、Software & AI、Biomanufacturing——**26 支得獎隊伍中只有 2 支**曾閉合設計迴路，應用類賽道則是 **45 支中有 14 支**。","chips":["2 of 26 vs 14 of 45"],"link":"good"}],"method":"Each card summarises an analysis published in full on the tab it links to, where the evidence, the named teams and the limits of the method are set out. Where a finding rests on a number, the analysis says how the number was computed and what it cannot see.","method_zh":"每一張卡片都是某篇完整分析的摘要，點進連結的頁面即可看到證據、具名的團隊，以及該方法的限制。凡是以數字為基礎的發現，分析中都會說明該數字如何計算，以及它看不到什麼。","order":10},{"id":"gems-gap","tab":"roadmap","order":20,"kicker":"Original analysis","kicker_zh":"原創分析","title":"GEMS measured against its own report","title_zh":"用這份報告的標準衡量 GEMS 自己","lede":"Every finding in this report, turned back on the team that commissioned it. Some of it is flattering and some of it is not, and the roadmap only means anything if both are said plainly.","lede_zh":"把這份報告的每一項發現，轉回來檢視委託這份報告的團隊。有些結論好看，有些不好看，而路線圖只有在兩者都直說時才有意義。","body":"**Start with what already meets the standard, because it is more than expected.**\n\nThe report's central result is that teams which close the model–data loop reach a Top 10 at 53% against 23%. GEMS-Taiwan closes it, and in one respect goes beyond anything else in the 2026 field: the crop-stress index was *fitted* to Taiwan's own harvest record — 25 years of county rice yields against ERA5 reanalysis, all 32,767 combinations of fifteen candidate terms scored on held-out years — and then tested **prospectively**, frozen on 26 September before any county published. County error came in at 365 kg/ha against 419 for a plain trend line. Separately, a growth rate of 0.2986 h⁻¹ with a 90% interval was registered in writing on 1 October, before a single bioreactor run; run 6 landed inside it at 0.286 ± 0.010.\n\nNo other team in this report pre-registered a quantitative prediction and scored it afterwards. It is the single highest-credibility item on the wiki and it cost nothing but committing in writing before the data arrived.\n\nThe provenance discipline is likewise at the top of the field, alongside TU Delft's. The honesty is real too: run 7 was excluded from scoring with the reason given, the curve-shape endpoint was recorded as not scored, and a 68-year payback was published against a partner's 4.9-year figure with the disagreement named rather than resolved. The human-practices loop closes properly — Prof. Chen Wen-Liang said in April that the organism could not be contained and that biological temperature sensing was not precise enough, and both the hollow-fibre perfusion reactor and the entire electronic sensing layer came out of that one conversation. Education was measured with pre- and post-surveys and the failures published, including the 30% who got DNA base pairing wrong.\n\n**Now the gaps, each tied to a finding in this report.**\n\n*The software has no front door.* The report found that 8 of 21 award-winning tools survive, and that the one habit separating them is a hosting decision made months early — every live tool was up on wiki-freeze day, every source-only tool lists localhost. The digital twin is MIT-licensed on GitLab and genuinely substantial, but it is a reactor controller: there is nothing a stranger can open. A simulator mode running on recorded data, at a URL, would move it from the source-only column to the live one. Two **high-school** teams managed exactly this in 2026.\n\n*The structure-prediction stack is a generation behind.* The census found AlphaFold still dominates iGEM at roughly a third of teams while the research literature has moved to open models. GEMS used AlphaFold with a pre-set confidence gate, which is better practice than most — but Boltz-2, Chai-1 and the MPNN family are where Lambert-GA, Heidelberg and Princeton were working. This is the cheapest capability gap to close on the list.\n\n*No parts contribution.* Taiwan took zero nominations in any of the four parts awards across both tiers in 2026, and GEMS is part of that zero. The report found that teams with no venture at all — HBUT-China, WHU-China, Squirrel-Beijing, BASIS-China — still contributed infrastructure other teams can reuse, and that this has a longer half-life than a business plan. A characterised, documented *B. subtilis* optogenetic part is the obvious candidate, and it is the same work as the Phase 3 research line.\n\n*The model is not yet fitted at the scale it is used.* The CcaSR Hill transfer function is assumed to hold at 20 L when every induction run was at a single light intensity. By the report's own loop-closure test, that step is modelled rather than measured — and the wiki's amber rail says so, which is to its credit, but saying so is not the same as fixing it.\n\n*The integration gaps are stated and still open.* Green-light induction tested but not wired in; dissolved-oxygen calibration did not hold; the protectant amount cannot be measured. These are the honest limits of a nine-month competition, and they are exactly the work an institution — rather than a team — exists to finish.\n\n*No collaboration page.* GEMS appears on no other Taiwanese team's collaboration page and has none of its own, while NYCU-Taiwan's July meet-up drew 53 people from five teams. Being findable is a precondition for everything in Phase 4.\n\n**The summary, stated plainly.** GEMS-Taiwan's weakness is not rigour — on provenance, pre-registration and honest reporting it is at or near the top of the entire 2026 field, high school and collegiate alike. The weakness is **reach**: a tool nobody outside can open, a part nobody else can order, a page nobody can find. That is a different problem from the one most teams have, and it needs a different year.","body_zh":"**先談已經達標的部分，因為比預期多。**\n\n這份報告的核心結果是：閉合模型與資料迴圈的團隊，進入 Top 10 的比例是 53% 對 23%。GEMS-Taiwan 做到了，而且在一點上超越了 2026 年其他所有隊伍：作物逆境指數是*擬合*出來的——以台灣自己的收穫紀錄，25 年的各縣市稻作產量對上 ERA5 再分析資料，把十五個候選項的全部 32,767 種組合在保留年份上評分——然後做了**前瞻性**檢驗，在 9 月 26 日任何縣市公布前就凍結。縣市誤差為 365 kg/ha，而單純趨勢線為 419。另外，他們在 10 月 1 日、任何一次生物反應器實驗之前，就以書面登記了 0.2986 h⁻¹ 的生長速率與 90% 區間；第 6 批次落在區間內，為 0.286 ± 0.010。\n\n本報告中沒有第二支團隊預先登記一個量化預測並在事後評分。這是整個 wiki 上可信度最高的一項，而它的代價只是「在資料出現之前先白紙黑字承諾」。\n\n來源標註的紀律同樣位居領先群，與 TU Delft 並列。誠實也是真的：第 7 批次被排除計分並附上理由，曲線形狀的指標被記為未評分，而 68 年的回收期與合作夥伴的 4.9 年並陳，歧異被指名而非被抹平。人類實踐的迴圈確實閉合——陳文亮教授在四月指出該菌無法被圍堵、且生物性溫度感測不夠精準，而中空纖維灌流反應器與整個電子感測層都出自那一次對話。教育工作以課前課後問卷量測，並公布失敗，包括 DNA 鹼基配對只有 30% 答對。\n\n**接著是落差，每一項都對應本報告的一個發現。**\n\n*軟體沒有入口。* 報告發現 21 個得獎工具中只有 8 個存活，而唯一的區分習慣是提前幾個月做的架站決定——每個仍在線的工具在 wiki 凍結日就已上線，每個只有原始碼的工具都只列 localhost。數位孿生以 MIT 授權放在 GitLab 上，內容扎實，但它是反應器控制器：沒有任何東西是陌生人打得開的。一個以錄製資料運行的模擬模式，放上一個網址，就能把它從「僅有原始碼」移到「仍在線」。2026 年有兩支**高中**隊伍正是做到了這件事。\n\n*結構預測的工具鏈落後一個世代。* 普查發現 AlphaFold 在 iGEM 仍占約三分之一的團隊，而研究文獻早已轉向開源模型。GEMS 使用 AlphaFold 並設了預先訂定的信心門檻，這比多數團隊的做法更好——但 Boltz-2、Chai-1 與 MPNN 家族才是 Lambert-GA、Heidelberg 與 Princeton 工作的地方。這是清單上最便宜就能補起來的能力落差。\n\n*沒有元件貢獻。* 2026 年台灣在兩個層級的四項元件獎中全數掛零，GEMS 也是那個零的一部分。報告發現，完全沒有創業規劃的團隊——HBUT-China、WHU-China、Squirrel-Beijing、BASIS-China——仍然貢獻了其他隊伍可重用的基礎設施，而那東西的半衰期比商業計畫書長。一個經過表徵、文件完整的*枯草桿菌*光遺傳元件是最明顯的候選，而且它與階段三的研究路線是同一件工作。\n\n*模型尚未在它被使用的尺度上完成擬合。* CcaSR 的 Hill 轉移函數被假定在 20 公升仍然成立，但所有誘導實驗都只在單一光強度下進行。依本報告自己的迴圈閉合判準，那一步是模擬而非量測——wiki 的琥珀色軌道確實這麼標示了，這一點值得肯定，但標示出來不等於解決了它。\n\n*已載明的整合缺口仍然敞著。* 綠光誘導已測試但未整合；溶氧校正未能維持；保護劑用量無法量測。這些是九個月競賽的誠實極限，而它們也正是「機構」——而非「團隊」——存在的目的所在。\n\n*沒有 collaboration 頁面。* GEMS 沒有出現在任何其他台灣團隊的合作頁面上，自己也沒有一個；而 NYCU-Taiwan 七月的聚會吸引了來自五支隊伍的 53 人。能被找到，是階段四所有事情的前提。\n\n**直說結論。** GEMS-Taiwan 的弱點不是嚴謹度——在來源標註、預先登記與誠實報告上，它在整個 2026 年、無論高中組或大專組，都位居頂端或接近頂端。它的弱點是**觸及**：一個外人打不開的工具、一個別人訂不到的元件、一個沒有人找得到的頁面。那是一個與多數團隊不同的問題，也需要一個不同的年度。","cards":[{"kicker":"Already at the top of the field","kicker_zh":"已經位居領先","title":"The only pre-registered prediction in the report","title_zh":"本報告中唯一的預先登記預測","body":"A growth rate of 0.2986 h⁻¹ with a 90% interval, registered in writing on 1 October before any bioreactor run; run 6 landed inside it at 0.286 ± 0.010. The crop-stress index was frozen on 26 September and tested against county yields nobody had published yet. No other team in this report did either. Keep doing it, and make it a house rule rather than one person's idea.","body_zh":"0.2986 h⁻¹ 的生長速率與 90% 區間，在 10 月 1 日、任何生物反應器實驗之前就以書面登記；第 6 批次以 0.286 ± 0.010 落在區間內。作物逆境指數則在 9 月 26 日凍結，並對當時尚未公布的縣市產量進行檢驗。本報告中沒有第二支團隊做過其中任何一件。請繼續做，並把它變成全機構的規則，而不是某一個人的點子。","chips":["unique in 2026"]},{"kicker":"The gap","kicker_zh":"落差","title":"The digital twin has no front door","title_zh":"數位孿生沒有入口","body":"MIT-licensed on GitLab and genuinely substantial — live OD600, pH, four pressure channels, an autoencoder alarm, a Kalman forecast, a hydraulic fouling model and the BLASTAM infection rule. But it is a reactor controller: there is nothing a stranger can open. A simulator mode running on recorded data, at a URL, moves it from source-only to live. Two high-school teams managed that in 2026.","body_zh":"以 MIT 授權放在 GitLab 上，內容扎實——即時 OD600、pH、四個壓力通道、自編碼器警報、Kalman 預測、水力積垢模型，以及 BLASTAM 感染規則。但它是反應器控制器：沒有任何東西是陌生人打得開的。一個以錄製資料運行、放在網址上的模擬模式，就能讓它從「僅有原始碼」變成「仍在線」。2026 年有兩支高中隊伍做到了。","chips":["source-only","a URL would fix it"]},{"kicker":"The gap","kicker_zh":"落差","title":"Zero parts nominations, and Taiwan's zero is shared","title_zh":"元件獎掛零，而台灣的零是共同的","body":"Taiwan took no nomination in any of the four parts awards across both tiers in 2026. Teams with no venture at all still contributed parts other teams can reuse, and that outlives a business plan. A characterised, documented *B. subtilis* optogenetic part is the obvious candidate — and it is the same work as the Phase 3 research line, not extra work.","body_zh":"2026 年台灣在兩個層級的四項元件獎中全數未獲提名。完全沒有創業規劃的團隊，仍然貢獻了其他隊伍可重用的元件，而那比商業計畫書活得更久。一個經過表徵、文件完整的*枯草桿菌*光遺傳元件是最明顯的候選——而且它與階段三的研究路線是同一件工作，不是額外的工作。","chips":["same work as Phase 3"]},{"kicker":"The gap","kicker_zh":"落差","title":"The Hill curve is assumed at 20 L, not measured there","title_zh":"Hill 曲線在 20 公升是假設的，不是量出來的","body":"Every induction ran at a single light intensity, so the CcaSR transfer function is modelled rather than measured at the scale it is used. The wiki's amber rail says so, which is to its credit — but saying so is not fixing it. A dose–response series across intensities at working volume is a term's work and would close the loop at the step that currently carries the most weight.","body_zh":"所有誘導實驗都在單一光強度下進行，因此 CcaSR 轉移函數在它實際被使用的尺度上是模擬而非量測。wiki 的琥珀色軌道確實標示了這一點，值得肯定——但標示不等於修正。在工作體積下跨多個光強度做一組劑量反應曲線，是一個學期的工作量，並且能在目前承載最多重量的那一步閉合迴圈。","chips":["single intensity"]},{"kicker":"The verdict","kicker_zh":"結論","title":"The weakness is reach, not rigour","title_zh":"弱點是觸及，不是嚴謹","body":"On provenance, pre-registration and honest reporting, GEMS-Taiwan sits at or near the top of the entire 2026 field, high school and collegiate alike. What it lacks is a tool anybody outside can open, a part anybody else can order, and a page anybody can find. That is a different problem from the one most teams have, and it needs a different kind of year.","body_zh":"在來源標註、預先登記與誠實報告上，GEMS-Taiwan 位居整個 2026 年——無論高中組或大專組——的頂端或接近頂端。它缺的是一個外人打得開的工具、一個別人訂得到的元件、一個有人找得到的頁面。那是一個與多數團隊不同的問題，也需要一個不同性質的年度。","chips":["rigour: top of field","reach: not yet"]}],"method":"Compares the GEMS-Taiwan team file in this report against the findings of the other nine analyses. The file was researched from the team's own 2026 wiki on the same terms as every other team, and much of the critical material here is the team's own stated limits rather than our discovery — the wiki is unusually candid, which is what makes this comparison possible at all. Where we say a gap exists, it is a gap relative to practice elsewhere in the 2026 field, not a judgement that the work is poor.","method_zh":"本篇以本報告中的 GEMS-Taiwan 團隊檔案，對照其餘九篇分析的發現。該檔案與其他所有團隊採用相同標準，取自該隊自己的 2026 wiki；此處許多批評性的材料其實出自團隊自述的限制，而非我們的發現——那個 wiki 異常坦白，這也正是這項比較得以成立的原因。凡我們指出存在落差之處，都是相對於 2026 年其他團隊實作的落差，而非認定該工作做得不好。"},{"id":"ihp-depth","tab":"good","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"Who actually let the outside world change the science","title_zh":"究竟是誰真的讓外界改變了科學","lede":"Across 93 teams, closing the loop has stopped being the distinction and become the norm — and almost every loop that closed was closed by a credentialled expert rather than by anybody the criterion is rhetorically about.","lede_zh":"在 93 支隊伍中，把回饋迴路閉合已經不再是區別所在，而成了常態——而幾乎每一個閉合的迴路，都是由一位有專業資歷的專家閉上的，不是由這條評審標準在修辭上所指的那些人。","body":"A score of four is a sentence, not a stakeholder list: a name, a specific thing said, and a design that is visibly different afterwards. Wageningen's Triton has three modules rather than one because Peter Fischer of Aqualab Zuid explained that trifluoroacetate can only be measured by LC-MS at a central lab, which forced an on-site biosensor, and because Bert van der Waal and Peyman Salehian showed that even tenfold reverse-osmosis concentration leaves it far too dilute, which forced a capture module. **GEMS-Taiwan** was releasing engineered Bacillus into soil until Prof. Chen Wen-Liang told them it could be neither contained nor made to sense temperature precisely; the hollow-fibre perfusion reactor and the electronic AIoT sensing layer both came out of that one April conversation. UCAS-China dropped NKX2-1 as a cargo and put SLPI in its place because Professor Huaiyong Chen said the first matters in development and barely in adulthood. RDFZ-China built bcsABCD in both BL21(DE3) and C41(DE3) and switched host after Professor Haibo Zhang warned that a working genetic module does not imply an efficient one; WUXI-DSAS excised gtdT on Dr Tengfei Hu's advice and recovered the linear dose-response its first-generation sensor could not give; IISER-Kolkata rebuilt its kill-switch trigger around the hypochlorite-sensing regulator RclR after a wastewater engineer pointed out that Indian plants disinfect with sodium hypochlorite rather than UV; and Oxford gave up a living Snodgrassella symbiont for heat-inactivated yeast because regulators pushed back against the beekeepers who had asked for it, then published what that cost its own users.\n\nThe three Best IHP winners share a method, and it is organisational rather than intellectual: the practice is wired into the engineering, not appended to it. **TU Delft** ran Value Sensitive Design in three declared passes and translated values into requirements, labelling the ones it could not meet as Future Perspectives rather than dropping them quietly; UCAS-China built its RCSF cycle as a deliberate parallel to DBTL and gave the human practices group the standing job of tracking every subteam's bottleneck; GEMS-Taiwan ran four thematic expert pipelines with five continuously engaged experts. What the winners do not have is a monopoly on depth. Oxford, Wageningen and UFABC-Brazil were nominees with chains at least as traceable, and UFABC declared its confirmation and refutation rules before seeing its survey results, then redrew its own SWOT when two assumptions failed. **Madrid-UCM**, which published the only genuine closure criterion in the cohort, got no human practices nomination at all.\n\nThe formats that changed designs are narrow and unglamorous. One of them is a single conversation with whoever operates the thing: Veolia's technical director for LYON, a sulfur-recovery engineer of thirty-three years for UOttawa, an optometrist for UAlberta, wet-market vendors for HongKong-JSS who demanded a number and got a wavelength-resolved spectrometer in place of a 14-channel colour sensor. Another is protocol-level consultation with whoever actually runs the technique, which is where chassis and construct changes come from: DTU to Komagataella phaffii, NFLSHS-CHINA from two plasmids to one, Heidelberg to a Serratia expression cassette. Add regulators contacted while the design is still open, peer teams handing over negative data as Darmstadt 2025 did to Padua on pcrABCD's oxygen sensitivity, and written-scorecard pitch events, which are cheap and work: Stanford's BIOME Shark Tank produced the microneedle segmentation pipeline. Against that, the school workshop, the museum stand, the carnival booth, the panel discussion and SDG mapping produced headcounts and nothing traceable, and the large public survey changed vocabulary with near-perfect reliability and hardware almost never.\n\nThe high-school tier is fully competitive wherever the work is user-facing and iterative. HongKong-JSS's farm-driven hardware revisions, measured as a drop from 7.41 to 1.95 per cent coefficient of variation, are better user-led engineering than most collegiate teams managed; **Hongwen School** struck three marketing claims on a gastroenterologist's evidence ladder and changed its selection antibiotic on a professor's re-annotation; HFI, NFLSHS-CHINA, RDFZ-China and WUXI-DSAS all changed circuits or hosts for a named reason; and QingdaoAcademy compressed twenty-two activities into thirteen numbered decisions that split a one-pot process in two and abandoned a planned pH-based function switch outright. Where the tier is not competitive is institutional reach: nothing in it approaches Oxford's EPA-FDA-USDA-CBD mapping, Wageningen's analysis of the non-viable-GMO approval route, UCL's Water UK discharge gap or DTU's correspondence with the European Environment Agency, and formal ethics infrastructure is rare, with Baltimore's community-lab board the main exception; the tier also almost never publishes failures of access the way DTU names the turbine makers who never replied.\n\nThe uncomfortable finding is who actually caused the changes. Of 64 teams that closed a loop, the loop was closed by a credentialled technical expert in nearly every case; the publics, patients and communities that the criterion is rhetorically about overwhelmingly changed the vocabulary and not the vector. Cornell's burn survivors changed what the team promises, Princeton's myeloma patients changed the word 'virus', HFI's 434 respondents changed 'genetically modified' to 'engineered' — all real, none of it touching a construct. Genuine counter-examples number six or seven in 93: LYON removed every living cell from its filter because the public objected, ICJFLS turned public fear into a four-layer containment design, HongKong-JSS re-specified a sensor because farmers wanted a number, UFABC-Brazil routed its seizure alert to a caregiver because a psychiatrist in the public system pointed out that patients who cannot recognise an aura cannot act on one, a beauty-salon manager's distrust of local seaweed put ultrafiltration desalting and endotoxin limits into QingdaoAcademy's plan, and a landfill worker of six years gave Hongwen School the handling cost that made local processing a hard constraint. Two further discomforts: the branded cycle acronym is now universal and predicts nothing, with Jilin-China's Social Shaping Loop and GreatBay-SCIE's five-stage framework scoring 2 while plain tables score 4; and awards track legibility rather than consequence, since **KIT** won Inclusivity and GreatBay-SCIE was nominated for Best IHP on evidence that scores 2, while Madrid-UCM, Hongwen School, GYHS and WUXI-DSAS closed loops nobody rewarded.","body_zh":"四分是一個句子，不是一張利害關係人名單：一個名字、一句具體說過的話，以及之後看得出不一樣的設計。Wageningen 的 Triton 有三個模組而不是一個，是因為 Aqualab Zuid 的 Peter Fischer 說明三氟乙酸只能把樣本送到中央實驗室用 LC-MS 量測，這迫使他們加上現場生物感測器；也因為 Bert van der Waal 和 Peyman Salehian 指出，即使經過十倍逆滲透濃縮，濃度還是稀得太多，這迫使他們加上捕捉模組。**GEMS-Taiwan** 原本要把工程化的 Bacillus 釋放到土壤裡，直到 Chen Wen-Liang 教授告訴他們，這既無法圍堵，也無法做到精確感測溫度；中空纖維灌流反應器和電子 AIoT 感測層，都出自四月那一場對話。UCAS-China 放棄 NKX2-1 作為載運基因、換上 SLPI，是因為 Huaiyong Chen 教授指出前者在發育期重要，在成年期幾乎不重要。RDFZ-China 把 bcsABCD 同時建在 BL21(DE3) 和 C41(DE3) 上，並在 Haibo Zhang 教授警告一個能運作的基因模組不代表它有效率之後換了宿主；WUXI-DSAS 依 Tengfei Hu 博士的建議切除 gtdT，救回第一代感測器給不出的線性劑量反應；IISER-Kolkata 在一位污水工程師指出印度的處理廠是用次氯酸鈉而不是紫外線消毒之後，圍繞次氯酸感測調控因子 RclR 重建了自殺開關的觸發機制；而 Oxford 放棄活的 Snodgrassella 共生菌、改用熱滅活酵母，是因為主管機關的意見與要求前者的養蜂人相反，之後他們也公開了這個選擇讓自己的使用者付出什麼代價。\n\n三支最佳整合式人類實踐得主共用一種方法，而且是組織上的而非思想上的：這套實踐被接進工程裡，不是附加在工程旁邊。**TU Delft** 以三個明確宣告的回合執行價值敏感設計，把價值轉譯成需求，並把做不到的那些標為 Future Perspectives，而不是悄悄刪掉；UCAS-China 刻意把自己的 RCSF 循環建成與 DBTL 平行的結構，並讓人類實踐組常態負責追蹤每一個分組的瓶頸；GEMS-Taiwan 跑了四條主題式專家管線，有五位持續參與的專家。得獎者沒有壟斷深度。Oxford、Wageningen 和 UFABC-Brazil 都只是入圍，但因果鏈至少同樣可追溯，而 UFABC 在看到問卷結果之前就先宣告自己的確認與反駁規則，之後在兩項假設失效時重畫了自己的 SWOT。**Madrid-UCM** 是全體隊伍中唯一提出真正閉環判準的隊伍，卻完全沒有拿到人類實踐的入圍。\n\n真正改變了設計的形式很窄，也不華麗。其中一種是和實際操作那個東西的人談一次話：LYON 談的是 Veolia 的技術總監，UOttawa 談的是一位有三十三年經驗的硫回收工程師，UAlberta 談的是一位驗光師，HongKong-JSS 談的是傳統市場的攤商，他們要的是一個數字，結果 14 通道的顏色感測器被換成了波長解析的光譜儀。另一種是和真正執行該技術的人做實驗流程層級的諮詢，這是底盤與構築體改變的來源：DTU 換成 Komagataella phaffii，NFLSHS-CHINA 從兩個質體變成一個，Heidelberg 換成 Serratia 表現卡匣。再加上在設計還沒定案時就接觸的主管機關、把負面資料交出來的同儕隊伍——例如 Darmstadt 2025 把 pcrABCD 對氧氣敏感的結果交給 Padua——以及有書面評分表的提案活動，這種活動便宜而且有效：Stanford 的 BIOME Shark Tank 催生了微針分割流程。相對地，校園工作坊、博物館攤位、園遊會攤位、座談會和 SDG 對照，產出的是參加人數，沒有任何可追溯的東西；而大型公眾問卷幾乎毫無例外地改變了用詞，卻幾乎從不改變硬體。\n\n只要工作是面對使用者而且會反覆迭代，高中組就完全有競爭力。HongKong-JSS 由農場驅動的硬體修改，量測結果是變異係數從 7.41% 降到 1.95%，這比多數大學隊伍做到的使用者導向工程更好；**Hongwen School** 依一位腸胃科醫師的證據階梯刪掉三項行銷聲稱，並依一位教授重新註解的結果更換了篩選用抗生素；HFI、NFLSHS-CHINA、RDFZ-China 和 WUXI-DSAS 都為了一個具名的理由改了迴路或宿主；QingdaoAcademy 則把二十二項活動壓縮成十三個編號的決定，其中把一鍋式製程拆成兩段，並且乾脆放棄原先計畫的 pH 功能切換。這一組不具競爭力的地方是制度性的觸及範圍：組內沒有任何案例接近 Oxford 的 EPA-FDA-USDA-CBD 對照、Wageningen 對非存活基改生物核可途徑的分析、UCL 找出的 Water UK 排放落差，或 DTU 與歐洲環境署的往來；正式的倫理機制也很少見，Baltimore 的社區實驗室審查委員會是主要的例外。這一組也幾乎從不公布接觸失敗的紀錄，像 DTU 那樣點名哪些渦輪機製造商從未回覆。\n\n令人不自在的發現是：究竟是誰造成了那些改變。64 支閉合了迴路的隊伍中，幾乎每一例都是由一位有專業資歷的技術專家閉上的；而這條標準在修辭上所指的公眾、病人和社群，絕大多數只改變了用詞，沒有改變載體。Cornell 的燒傷倖存者改變了隊伍承諾的內容，Princeton 的骨髓瘤病人改掉了「病毒」這個詞，HFI 的 434 位受訪者把「基因改造」改成「工程化」——全都真實，卻沒有一項碰到構築體。真正的反例在 93 支隊伍中有六、七個：LYON 因為公眾反對而把濾材裡所有活細胞都移除，ICJFLS 把公眾的恐懼轉成四層圍堵設計，HongKong-JSS 因為農民要一個數字而重新規格化感測器，UFABC-Brazil 因為公立體系的一位精神科醫師指出無法辨識前兆的病人也無法據以行動，而把癲癇警示改送到照顧者，一位美容院經理對本地海藻的不信任讓超過濾脫鹽與內毒素上限進了 QingdaoAcademy 的計畫，而一位做了六年的垃圾掩埋場工人則給了 Hongwen School 那筆搬運成本，使就地處理成為硬性限制。另有兩點令人不自在：掛上品牌的循環縮寫現在到處都有，而且什麼都預測不了——Jilin-China 的 Social Shaping Loop 和 GreatBay-SCIE 的五階段框架都只得 2 分，而樸素的表格得 4 分；獎項追蹤的是易讀性而不是後果，因為 **KIT** 以只得 2 分的證據拿下包容性獎、GreatBay-SCIE 也以這種等級的證據入圍最佳整合式人類實踐，而 Madrid-UCM、Hongwen School、GYHS 和 WUXI-DSAS 閉合的迴路沒有人獎勵。","cards":[{"kicker":"Worked example","title":"Two of three modules were somebody else's idea","title_zh":"三個模組中有兩個是別人的主意","body":"Wageningen set out only to degrade trifluoroacetate. Peter Fischer at Aqualab Zuid, one of six labs legally tasked with assessing Dutch drinking water, explained that the compound can only be measured by LC-MS on samples shipped to a central lab, so the bioreactor could not be operated at all without an on-site readout: that created the biosensor module. Bert van der Waal and Peyman Salehian then showed that tenfold reverse-osmosis concentration takes 2.2 micrograms per litre only to 22, against a milligram-per-litre target, which created the capture module. Frank Schoonenberg of Vitens moved the whole deployment target to reverse-osmosis concentrate, and Tue Kjaergaard Nielsen changed the readout to released fluoride because measuring TFA disappearance mistakes adsorption for degradation.","body_zh":"Wageningen 原本只打算分解三氟乙酸。Aqualab Zuid 的 Peter Fischer——該實驗室是荷蘭六家法定負責評估飲用水的機構之一——說明這個化合物只能把樣本送到中央實驗室用 LC-MS 量測，所以沒有現場讀出就根本無法操作這座生物反應器：這催生了生物感測模組。接著 Bert van der Waal 和 Peyman Salehian 指出，十倍逆滲透濃縮只能把每公升 2.2 微克提高到 22 微克，而目標是毫克每公升的量級，這催生了捕捉模組。Vitens 的 Frank Schoonenberg 把整個部署目標移到逆滲透濃縮液，而 Tue Kjaergaard Nielsen 把讀出改成釋出的氟離子，因為量測 TFA 的消失會把吸附誤認成分解。","chips":["WageningenUR","Overgrad","Score 4","Utility and lab engineers"],"kicker_zh":"實例"},{"kicker":"Worked example","title":"The conversation that moved sensing out of the cell","title_zh":"把感測移出細胞之外的那場對話","body":"GEMS-Taiwan's original design put engineered Bacillus subtilis in the soil with a DesK-DesR system reading temperature directly. On 10 April, Prof. Chen Wen-Liang and bioprocess experts said two things were wrong: the bacteria could not be contained, and biological sensing was neither precise nor controllable enough. Sensing moved out of the cell into electronic sensors and an AIoT model, and a hollow-fibre perfusion bioreactor was built to hold the bacteria in while letting the protectants out. A later public forum with natural-farming advocates, who argued that a crop protected from every stress never builds tolerance, became the specification for the release threshold rather than an objection to be managed.","body_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 最初的設計是把工程化的 Bacillus subtilis 放進土壤，用 DesK-DesR 系統直接讀取溫度。4 月 10 日，Chen Wen-Liang 教授和生物製程專家指出兩件事是錯的：細菌無法被圍堵，而生物感測既不夠精確也不夠可控。感測從細胞內移到電子感測器和一套 AIoT 模型，同時建了一座中空纖維灌流生物反應器，把細菌留在裡面、讓保護物質出去。後來一場與自然農法倡議者的公開論壇——他們主張一株被保護到完全沒有逆境的作物永遠不會建立耐受性——成了釋放閾值的規格依據，而不是一個要被處理掉的反對意見。","chips":["GEMS-Taiwan","High School","Score 4","Best IHP winner"],"kicker_zh":"實例"},{"kicker":"Worked example","title":"When the regulator overrules the user","title_zh":"當主管機關推翻使用者","body":"Danny Le Feuvre of the Australian Honey Bee Industry Council and Mike Allerton of Amateur Beekeepers Australia both wanted a persistent living Snodgrassella alvi gut symbiont because it minimises beekeeper labour. Oxford did not simply comply: it took the question to Scottish and Australian regulators and the Soil Association, who pushed the other way, and switched to heat-inactivated dried yeast. The team then stated plainly what that cost — the persistence the beekeepers valued, meaning repeat dosing and more labour. A joint meeting with EPA, FDA and USDA staff stopped them treating the inactivated route as a universal regulatory shortcut, forcing jurisdiction-by-jurisdiction mapping instead.","body_zh":"Australian Honey Bee Industry Council 的 Danny Le Feuvre 和 Amateur Beekeepers Australia 的 Mike Allerton 都想要一株能持續存在的活 Snodgrassella alvi 腸道共生菌，因為這能把養蜂人的工作量降到最低。Oxford 並沒有照辦：他們把這個問題帶到蘇格蘭與澳洲的主管機關以及 Soil Association，這些單位的意見正好相反，於是改用熱滅活的乾酵母。隊伍接著明白寫出這個選擇的代價——失去養蜂人所重視的持續性，意味著要重複投藥、工作量更大。一場與 EPA、FDA 和 USDA 人員的聯合會議，讓他們不再把滅活路線當成普遍適用的法規捷徑，而是改為逐一管轄區進行對照。","chips":["Oxford","Undergrad","Score 4","Best IHP nominee"],"kicker_zh":"實例"},{"kicker":"Worked example","title":"A farmer asked for a number","title_zh":"一位農民要一個數字","body":"HongKong-JSS built a mercury biosensor with a visible colour readout. Koo's Farm and local wet-market vendors said they wanted numerical readings, not qualitative colour, which is the direct reason the AS7343 14-channel sensor was replaced by a wavelength-resolved Hamamatsu C12880 with a numerical display. Users then reported excessive syringe force on the V1 filter stack, so manual delivery became pump-driven dosing, improving the coefficient of variation from 7.41 to 1.95 per cent. More Happy Farm said plainly that not every farmer wants to own a device, which pushed them to a service model — and after a 195-person demonstration found high perceived confidence, the team separated device status from safety judgement in the interface because confidence is not accuracy.","body_zh":"HongKong-JSS 做了一個以可見顏色讀出的汞生物感測器。Koo's Farm 和本地傳統市場的攤商說他們要的是數值讀數，不是定性的顏色，這就是 AS7343 14 通道感測器被換成帶數值顯示的波長解析 Hamamatsu C12880 的直接原因。使用者接著回報 V1 濾材組需要過大的針筒推力，於是手動加樣改成泵驅動的定量加樣，變異係數從 7.41% 改善到 1.95%。More Happy Farm 直接說並不是每個農民都想擁有一台裝置，這把他們推向服務模式——而在一場 195 人的示範中發現使用者自覺的信心偏高之後，隊伍在介面上把裝置狀態與安全判斷分開，因為有信心不等於準確。","chips":["HongKong-JSS","High School","Score 4","Non-expert changed hardware"],"kicker_zh":"實例"},{"kicker":"Method that nobody rewarded","title":"The only team that defined what 'closed' means","title_zh":"唯一定義了「閉合」是什麼意思的隊伍","body":"Madrid-UCM built a five-rung integration ladder with an explicit closure criterion: a loop counts as closed only when the revised design goes back to the person whose input triggered it and their response produces a further change. They then demonstrated it on materials — Carmen Garcia Payo and Loreto Garcia Fernandez proposed core-shell capsules, the team built them but could not see the internal structure, took that problem back to the same researchers, and got magnetite as an optical tracer plus cryosectioning, which became a wall-thickness and leakage pipeline. Aurelio Hidalgo's point that a single-use biocatalyst is neither economical nor recoverable killed both placeholder designs and moved the enzyme panel onto a reusable solid support. They also document a change they chose not to make, on the grounds that not adding a pathway is a design decision too. No Best IHP nomination.","body_zh":"Madrid-UCM 建了一座五階的整合階梯，並有明確的閉環判準：一個迴路只有在修訂後的設計回到提供意見的那個人面前、而他的回應又帶來進一步的改變時，才算閉合。他們接著在材料上示範了這一點——Carmen Garcia Payo 和 Loreto Garcia Fernandez 提議核殼膠囊，隊伍做出來了卻看不到內部結構，於是把這個問題帶回同一批研究者，得到以磁鐵礦作為光學示蹤劑再加上冷凍切片的作法，這後來變成一條量測壁厚與滲漏的流程。Aurelio Hidalgo 指出單次使用的生物催化劑既不經濟也無法回收，這一句話殺掉了兩個暫用設計，並把酵素組移到可重複使用的固體支撐上。他們也記錄了一項選擇不做的改變，理由是不加進一條代謝途徑同樣是一個設計決定。沒有拿到最佳整合式人類實踐入圍。","chips":["Madrid-UCM","Undergrad","Score 4","Not nominated"],"kicker_zh":"沒有被獎勵的做法"},{"kicker":"Format that mostly did not work","title":"The survey that changes your vocabulary","title_zh":"只會改變你用詞的問卷","body":"Large public surveys are the most common instrument in the cohort and the least consequential for design. HFI's 434 responses replaced 'genetically modified' with 'engineered' across all materials and rebuilt the education from basics. Peking's 539 respondents named three priorities the team concedes already outlined the finished project. UCAS-China's 419 public respondents and HongKong-HS's 420 produced awareness statistics and workshop plans. The honest version is GHCIS, which found that its price and speed questions branched into samples too small to use and explicitly refused to convert 'within RMB 30' into a product requirement, carrying it forward as a question for frontline users instead.","body_zh":"大型公眾問卷是全體隊伍中最常見的工具，對設計的影響也最小。HFI 的 434 份回覆讓所有材料把「基因改造」換成「工程化」，並把教育內容從基礎重建。Peking 的 539 位受訪者點出三項優先事項，而隊伍自己承認這三項早就勾勒出了最終完成的專案。UCAS-China 的 419 位公眾受訪者和 HongKong-HS 的 420 位，產出的是認知度統計和工作坊計畫。誠實的版本是 GHCIS：他們發現價格與速度的題目分支之後樣本太小而無法使用，並明確拒絕把「人民幣 30 元以內」轉成產品需求，而是把它當成一個問題帶給第一線使用者。","chips":["HFI","Peking","GHCIS","UCAS-China","Vocabulary, not vector"],"kicker_zh":"大多無效的形式"}],"table":{"head":["Team","Section","Score","What changed"],"head_zh":["隊伍","組別","評分","改變了什麼"],"rows":[["ABOA","Overgrad","4","Purified enzymes dropped for whole cells on carriers; reactor moved to a side stream"],["Al-Nahrain-IRAQ","Undergrad","4","AI model abandoned for equation-based modelling; lab data entry page added"],["Athens","Overgrad","4","Delivery moved from spray to feed; live phage dropped for a non-replicating enzyme"],["BGCFullerton","High School","4","CIF peptides dropped; regolith mixture plan and model validation changed"],["CHINAGuangdongShimen","High School","4","Multivalent antibody replaced by a single monovalent nanobody"],["Cornell","Undergrad","4","Homemade high-voltage supply dropped; hypoxia AND gate added for specificity"],["DTU-Denmark","Overgrad","4","Enzyme step reframed as solvolysis complement; chassis to K. phaffii; docking filter dropped"],["ETH-Zurich","Overgrad","4","Pivot off the Drosophila biopesticide; split-cargo dual targeting invented"],["Eton-College-UK","High School","4","Plasmid backbone changed; reusable reader plus disposable cartridge fixed"],["GCGS","High School","4","VOC module de-scoped; temperature kill switch added, pH switch declined with a reason"],["GEMS-Taiwan","High School","4","Sensing moved out of the cell; perfusion reactor added; proline delivery abandoned"],["GYHS","High School","4","Bond strength replaced by a seven-part requirement set; V2 handling redesigned"],["HFI","High School","4","Lysine-responsive promoter abandoned for constitutive expression"],["HK-Joint-School","High School","4","Goal shifted from fire retardancy to non-toxic, low-smoke; benchmark added"],["HKSSC","High School","4","Kill switch and controlled use; MIC/growth-rate design; pH range from regulator data"],["HKU-HongKong","Unlisted","4","Hypothesis narrowed to partial inflammation modulation; M1/M2 framing dropped"],["HUST-China","Undergrad","4","Reflectin module abandoned entirely for a fashion-waste cellulose route"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","High School","4","Target moved from mineralised calculus to pre-mineralisation biofilm matrix"],["Heidelberg","Undergrad","4","Expression host swapped to a Serratia cassette; engineering retargeted onto GvpC"],["HongKong-HS","High School","4","Toehold switch replaced by HCR; ThT fluorescence replaced by G4/hemin colour"],["HongKong-JSS","High School","4","Colour sensor replaced by spectrometer; syringe replaced by pump dosing"],["Hongwen School","High School","4","IBS claims struck; selection marker changed; near-site processing made a hard constraint"],["ICJFLS","High School","4","Capsule killed for mouthwash/lozenge/gum set; plasmid dropped for chromosomal integration"],["IISER-Kolkata","Unlisted","4","Kill switch rebuilt around a hypochlorite sensor because plants do not use UV"],["KAUST-KSA","Overgrad","4","Dsup added to the chassis; payload reprioritised by real mission conditions"],["LYON","Undergrad","4","All living cells removed from the filter; households ruled out as customers"],["Lambert-GA","High School","4","Nanobodies abandoned for minibinders; target narrowed to the VP3 P-domain"],["MIT-MAHE","Undergrad","4","Target customer moved from fragrance houses to aroma compound manufacturers"],["Madrid-UCM","Undergrad","4","Secretion and consortium killed for immobilised enzymes; containment above performance"],["Marburg","Overgrad","4","5'UTR redesigned so the PPR site and RBS are disconnected; RBS testing dropped"],["McGill","Undergrad","4","Dropped ultra-purification; feedstock moved to fresh tailings; tolling business model"],["McMaster-Canada","Undergrad","4","Oncology and allergy concepts dropped for localised gut-associated systems"],["Muenster-University","Overgrad","4","Prediction pipeline rebuilt with a geometric scoring layer; NLR route dropped"],["NBJF","High School","4","DNA storage device abandoned for the enzymatic-writing bottleneck"],["NFLSHS-CHINA","High School","4","Two plasmids collapsed into one; aqueous formulation killed for oil and capsule"],["NJU-China","Undergrad","4","Recorded associations split from model predictions in every view"],["NUS-Singapore","Undergrad","4","Primary use moved from industrial monitoring to early-stage R&D"],["NYCU-Taiwan","Undergrad","4","Claimed advantages withdrawn after reading a competitor's documentation"],["Oxford","Undergrad","4","Living symbiont chassis dropped for heat-inactivated yeast, with the cost published"],["PSI Korea","High School","4","Auto-exposure disabled and imaging conditions fixed; instrument separated from material"],["Princeton","Undergrad","4","AlphaFold3 cut from the pipeline; IL-6 and amyloid-beta targets dropped"],["QingdaoAcademy","High School","4","One-pot process split in two; pH switch abandoned; desalting and endotoxin control added"],["RDFZ-China","High School","4","Host switched to C41(DE3); metal anchors replaced by on-site stone"],["SEHS","High School","4","Indication moved from liver to gastric cancer; binding re-tested per format"],["SMS-Shenzhen","High School","4","Target customer relocated from front-end recyclers to hydrometallurgical tail streams"],["SUIS-SFLS","High School","4","Deliverable rewritten from finished dressing to characterised protein plus QC records"],["Stanford University","Undergrad","4","Burns dropped for keloids; target moved from prevention to established scars"],["Stockholm","Overgrad","4","Open release abandoned for a sealed reactor sited at the membrane-bioreactor stage"],["TAU-Israel","Overgrad","4","Markers stratified across superficial and deep lesions; biosensor demoted to triage"],["TU Delft","Overgrad","4","Antibiotics dropped for AMPs; pre-coated implant instead of in-theatre paste"],["UAlberta","Undergrad","4","Binding-pocket release abandoned; yeast dropped for E. coli; GFP to mScarlet"],["UCAS-China","Undergrad","4","NKX2-1 cargo dropped for SLPI; repositioned to asthma maintenance"],["UCNZ","Undergrad","4","Distributed plants dropped for one central facility; sustainability claim narrowed"],["UFABC-Brazil","Overgrad","4","Pipetted cell-free reaction replaced by a paper strip; alert routed to a support network"],["UNILausanne","Overgrad","4","Defend strategy kept against the model's own advice; model scope declared the limit"],["UOttawa","Undergrad","4","Target stream moved from bitumen to diesel; pH loop added to the P&ID"],["UZurich","Overgrad","4","Machine-learning plan dropped for established software; root cohesion added to the model"],["Uni-Padua-IT","Undergrad","4","Cold-tolerance module cut; perchlorate genes compartmentalised in heterocysts"],["Vilnius-Lithuania","Undergrad","4","Gel software moved off image classification onto band-distance matching"],["WUXI-DSAS","High School","4","gtdT excised to restore linearity; output changed to a creatinine ratio"],["WageningenUR","Overgrad","4","Biosensor and capture modules created; readout changed to released fluoride"],["William-and-Mary","Undergrad","4","Readout replaced by CFU viability; seawater microcosm experiments added"],["Worldshaper-Shanghai","High School","4","Capacity-building dropped for licensing; sunlight-is-greener claims deleted"],["XJTLU-China","Undergrad","4","Success redefined as soluble protein, not total expression"],["ASIJ-Tokyo","High School","3","Positioning moved from replacement to extra source; patch route added"],["Baltimore","High School","3","Preservation study and patent strategy added; changes peripheral to the build"],["CalPolySLO","Undergrad","3","Survivability testing and a misuse framework added; the build itself unchanged"],["DKU","Undergrad","3","Per-application immunogenicity thresholds and clearer tool output; attribution collective"],["GHCIS","High School","3","Microfluidic format replaced by filter paper, on unnamed industry advice"],["GU Frankfurt","Overgrad","3","Binder accuracy made the governing constraint; biggest change was procedural"],["Kyoto","Undergrad","3","Food themes abandoned and the question reframed; specific changes not itemised"],["Peking","Undergrad","3","Broad-spectrum pesticide and crude biocontrol routes dropped; chain not attributed"],["SDU-Denmark","Overgrad","3","Target moved to reliable low-power generation; no named source"],["SJTU-BioX-Shanghai","Undergrad","3","Repositioned as a post-debridement dressing with physical containment; sources unnamed"],["Toronto","Overgrad","3","Contained bioreactor and close-homology enzymes preferred; stakeholders unnamed"],["UCL","Undergrad","3","Regulatory gap found and a techno-economic model built; the device did not change"],["UPF-Barcelona","Undergrad","3","Central claim shrunk from bulk soil water to a hydration shell at the root"],["ZJU-China","Undergrad","3","Cost weighted more heavily in material design; attribution aggregated"],["ZQT-Nanjing","High School","3","Narrowed from general skincare to barrier repair after a 397-person survey"],["BAID-China","High School","2","Communication depth differentiated by audience; accessibility artefacts revised"],["BNDS-China","High School","2","Workflow discipline borrowed from a peer team; rest is framing"],["BOKU-Vienna","Overgrad","2","Claims key design decisions changed but does not say which"],["CAU-China","Undergrad","2","Need reported from Malawi and Zambia; no design consequence recorded"],["GreatBay-SCIE","High School","2","Slogan changed on stigma grounds; design philosophy only loosely attributed"],["HBUT-China","Undergrad","2","Named virologist fed the risk assessment; no design consequence stated"],["Jilin-China","Undergrad","2","Double-loop reframing of what counts as success; consequences not shown"],["KIT","Overgrad","2","Survey converted into two inclusivity deliverables; science untouched"],["Labi-Taiwan","High School","2","Complements-not-replaces framing and a detects-not-diagnoses statement"],["Mingdao","High School","2","Five honest questions, including a no-project condition; no design change recorded"],["UMA Malaga","Undergrad","2","Question reframed around the diagnostic pathway, not the device"],["UOregon","Overgrad","2","Plant operators confirmed the gap; equity framing shaped, design did not"],["NIS Almaty-Medeu","High School","1","Questions published in advance; no answers or consequences recorded yet"],["Yucai-SZ","High School","1","A 719-response survey tested the premise; no consequence recorded"]],"rows_zh":[["ABOA","研究生組","4","放棄純化酵素，改用附著在載體上的全細胞；反應器移到側流"],["Al-Nahrain-IRAQ","大學組","4","放棄 AI 模型，改用方程式建模；新增實驗資料輸入頁面"],["Athens","研究生組","4","投遞方式從噴灑改為飼料；放棄活噬菌體，改用不複製的酵素"],["BGCFullerton","高中組","4","放棄 CIF 胜肽；風化層混合配方計畫與模型驗證方式改變"],["CHINAGuangdongShimen","高中組","4","多價抗體改成單一的單價 nanobody"],["Cornell","大學組","4","放棄自製高壓電源；為提高專一性加入缺氧 AND 閘"],["DTU-Denmark","研究生組","4","酵素步驟重新定位為溶劑分解的互補；底盤換成 K. phaffii；放棄對接篩選"],["ETH-Zurich","研究生組","4","放棄果蠅生物農藥方向；發明分割載運的雙標的策略"],["Eton-College-UK","高中組","4","更換質體骨架；定案為可重複使用的讀取器加一次性卡匣"],["GCGS","高中組","4","縮減 VOC 模組範圍；加入溫度自殺開關，並附理由否決 pH 開關"],["GEMS-Taiwan","高中組","4","感測移出細胞之外；加入灌流反應器；放棄脯胺酸投遞"],["GYHS","高中組","4","以一組七項需求取代單一黏結強度指標；V2 的操作方式重新設計"],["HFI","高中組","4","放棄離胺酸誘導型啟動子，改用組成型表現"],["HK-Joint-School","高中組","4","目標從阻燃改為無毒、低煙；加入基準比較"],["HKSSC","高中組","4","加入自殺開關與受控使用；以 MIC 與生長速率設計；pH 範圍取自主管機關資料"],["HKU-HongKong","未列組別","4","假設收斂為部分調節發炎；放棄 M1/M2 的框架"],["HUST-China","大學組","4","完全放棄 reflectin 模組，改走時尚廢棄物纖維素路線"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","高中組","4","標的從已礦化的牙結石移到礦化前的生物膜基質"],["Heidelberg","大學組","4","表現宿主換成 Serratia 卡匣；工程改造目標轉到 GvpC"],["HongKong-HS","高中組","4","toehold switch 改成 HCR；ThT 螢光改成 G4／hemin 顯色"],["HongKong-JSS","高中組","4","顏色感測器改成光譜儀；針筒改成泵驅動定量加樣"],["Hongwen School","高中組","4","刪除 IBS 相關聲稱；更換篩選標記；就近處理成為硬性限制"],["ICJFLS","高中組","4","放棄膠囊，改為漱口水／錠劑／口香糖組合；放棄質體，改為染色體嵌入"],["IISER-Kolkata","未列組別","4","因為處理廠不使用紫外線，自殺開關改以次氯酸感測器重建"],["KAUST-KSA","研究生組","4","底盤加入 Dsup；依真實任務條件重排酬載優先順序"],["LYON","大學組","4","濾材中所有活細胞全部移除；排除家庭用戶作為客戶"],["Lambert-GA","高中組","4","放棄 nanobody，改用 minibinder；標的收斂到 VP3 的 P-domain"],["MIT-MAHE","大學組","4","目標客戶從香水品牌商移到香料化合物製造商"],["Madrid-UCM","大學組","4","放棄分泌與菌群路線，改用固定化酵素；圍堵優先於效能"],["Marburg","研究生組","4","重新設計 5'UTR，使 PPR 位點與 RBS 不再連動；放棄 RBS 測試"],["McGill","大學組","4","放棄超純化；原料改為新鮮尾礦；改採代工收費的商業模式"],["McMaster-Canada","大學組","4","放棄腫瘤與過敏的構想，改為局部作用的腸道相關系統"],["Muenster-University","研究生組","4","預測流程以幾何評分層重建；放棄 NLR 路線"],["NBJF","高中組","4","放棄 DNA 儲存裝置，轉向酵素寫入的瓶頸"],["NFLSHS-CHINA","高中組","4","兩個質體併成一個；放棄水性配方，改為油劑與膠囊"],["NJU-China","大學組","4","在每一個檢視畫面中都把已記錄的關聯與模型預測分開"],["NUS-Singapore","大學組","4","主要用途從工業監測移到早期研發"],["NYCU-Taiwan","大學組","4","讀過競爭對手的文件後撤回原本宣稱的優勢"],["Oxford","大學組","4","放棄活體共生菌底盤，改用熱滅活酵母，並公開這個選擇的代價"],["PSI Korea","高中組","4","關閉自動曝光並固定影像條件；把儀器與材料分開處理"],["Princeton","大學組","4","從流程中移除 AlphaFold3；放棄 IL-6 與 amyloid-beta 標的"],["QingdaoAcademy","高中組","4","一鍋式製程拆成兩段；放棄 pH 開關；加入脫鹽與內毒素控制"],["RDFZ-China","高中組","4","宿主換成 C41(DE3)；金屬錨件改用現地石材"],["SEHS","高中組","4","適應症從肝癌移到胃癌；依每一種形式重新測試結合能力"],["SMS-Shenzhen","高中組","4","目標客戶從前端回收業者移到濕法冶金的尾端流程"],["SUIS-SFLS","高中組","4","交付成果從成品敷料改寫為完成特性分析的蛋白質加品管紀錄"],["Stanford University","大學組","4","放棄燒傷，改做蟹足腫；目標從預防移到已形成的疤痕"],["Stockholm","研究生組","4","放棄開放釋放，改為設置在膜生物反應器階段的密閉反應器"],["TAU-Israel","研究生組","4","標記依淺層與深層病灶分層；生物感測器降級為初步分流用"],["TU Delft","研究生組","4","放棄抗生素，改用 AMP；以預先塗層的植入物取代手術室現調的膏劑"],["UAlberta","大學組","4","放棄結合口袋釋放機制；放棄酵母改用 E. coli；GFP 換成 mScarlet"],["UCAS-China","大學組","4","放棄 NKX2-1 載運基因改用 SLPI；重新定位為氣喘的維持治療"],["UCNZ","大學組","4","放棄分散式廠房，改為單一中央設施；縮小永續性聲稱的範圍"],["UFABC-Brazil","研究生組","4","以試紙取代需要移液的無細胞反應；警示改送到支持網絡"],["UNILausanne","研究生組","4","在模型自身的建議之外仍保留防禦策略；明確宣告模型範圍就是其限制"],["UOttawa","大學組","4","目標物流從瀝青移到柴油；在 P&ID 中加入 pH 控制迴路"],["UZurich","研究生組","4","放棄機器學習計畫，改用成熟軟體；模型中加入根系團聚作用"],["Uni-Padua-IT","大學組","4","刪去耐寒模組；把高氯酸鹽相關基因區隔到異形細胞中"],["Vilnius-Lithuania","大學組","4","膠體軟體從影像分類改為條帶距離比對"],["WUXI-DSAS","高中組","4","切除 gtdT 以恢復線性；輸出改為肌酸酐比值"],["WageningenUR","研究生組","4","新增生物感測與捕捉模組；讀出改為釋出的氟離子"],["William-and-Mary","大學組","4","讀出改為 CFU 存活數；加入海水微宇宙實驗"],["Worldshaper-Shanghai","高中組","4","放棄能力建構路線改為技術授權；刪除日照更環保的聲稱"],["XJTLU-China","大學組","4","把成功重新定義為可溶性蛋白質，而不是總表現量"],["ASIJ-Tokyo","高中組","3","定位從替代品改為額外來源；加入貼片途徑"],["Baltimore","高中組","3","加入保存性研究與專利策略；這些改變與實際建置沒有直接關係"],["CalPolySLO","大學組","3","加入存活性測試與誤用評估框架；建置本身沒有改變"],["DKU","大學組","3","依應用場景設定免疫原性閾值，工具輸出更清楚；意見歸因是集體性的"],["GHCIS","高中組","3","依未具名的業界建議，微流體形式改為濾紙"],["GU Frankfurt","研究生組","3","以結合物準確度作為主要限制條件；最大的改變是流程上的"],["Kyoto","大學組","3","放棄食品主題並重新界定問題；具體改變沒有逐項列出"],["Peking","大學組","3","放棄廣效農藥與粗放生物防治路線；因果鏈沒有歸因"],["SDU-Denmark","研究生組","3","目標移向穩定的低功率發電；沒有具名來源"],["SJTU-BioX-Shanghai","大學組","3","重新定位為清創後使用、具物理圍堵的敷料；來源未具名"],["Toronto","研究生組","3","偏好密閉生物反應器與高同源性酵素；利害關係人未具名"],["UCL","大學組","3","找出法規落差並建立技術經濟分析模型；裝置本身沒有改變"],["UPF-Barcelona","大學組","3","核心主張從整體土壤水分縮小為根部的水合層"],["ZJU-China","大學組","3","材料設計中成本的權重提高；意見歸因是彙總的"],["ZQT-Nanjing","高中組","3","在一份 397 人的問卷之後，從一般護膚收斂到屏障修復"],["BAID-China","高中組","2","依受眾區分溝通深度；修訂無障礙相關產出"],["BNDS-China","高中組","2","從同儕隊伍借用工作流程紀律；其餘都是框架層面的"],["BOKU-Vienna","研究生組","2","聲稱關鍵設計決定有所改變，但沒有說是哪些"],["CAU-China","大學組","2","報告了來自馬拉威與尚比亞的需求；沒有記錄任何設計後果"],["GreatBay-SCIE","高中組","2","因汙名化的考量更改標語；設計理念的歸因很鬆散"],["HBUT-China","大學組","2","具名病毒學家提供意見納入風險評估；沒有陳述任何設計後果"],["Jilin-China","大學組","2","以雙迴路重新界定什麼算成功；沒有呈現後果"],["KIT","研究生組","2","把問卷轉成兩項包容性交付成果；科學本身沒有動"],["Labi-Taiwan","高中組","2","採用互補而非取代的定位，以及偵測而非診斷的聲明"],["Mingdao","高中組","2","五個誠實的問題，包括一個不做這個專案的條件；沒有記錄設計改變"],["UMA Malaga","大學組","2","問題重新圍繞診斷路徑而非裝置來界定"],["UOregon","研究生組","2","廠區操作人員確認了這個落差；公平性的框架被塑形，設計沒有"],["NIS Almaty-Medeu","高中組","1","事先公布了問題；還沒有記錄任何回答或後果"],["Yucai-SZ","高中組","1","一份 719 份回覆的問卷檢驗了前提；沒有記錄任何後果"]]},"method":"Every team in this report is a Top 10 or special-prize winner or nominee, so this is the most decorated tenth of the competition and not a representative sample. Read '64 of 93 closed the loop' as 'closing the loop is normal among teams that win things', not as a statement about iGEM at large. Every team file with any good.ihp content was scored on the four-point rubric from what the file itself states: a 4 required a named stakeholder, a specific thing said, and a change to the build, the deployment, the readout, the safety design or the business model that the file ties to that input. Teams whose only documented consequence was a change of framing, language, education material or evidence package scored 2 or 3 however elaborately the process was branded, and awards were ignored throughout. The rubric cannot verify that a change was made because of the advice rather than attributed to it afterwards, cannot see the wiki behind the summary, and cannot distinguish a thin causal chain from a thin write-up of a thick one. Files continued to land while the scoring ran; all 93 present at the end were read and scored, so the set is complete as of writing but not closed. Since this was written the set closed at 106 files. A later analysis on this page, Who the loop actually closes with, rescored the thirteen that landed late and recounts 71 of 106 closing a loop and nine or ten closing it with a non-expert, against the six or seven in 93 reported here. The extra non-expert loops are the late files plus two formulation and delivery-route changes this pass had read as framing. The shape of the finding is unchanged; the denominators there are the current ones.","method_zh":"本報告中的每一支隊伍都是 Top 10 或特別獎的得主或入圍者，所以這是整個競賽中獲獎最多的那十分之一，不是代表性樣本。「93 支中有 64 支閉合了迴路」要讀成「在會得獎的隊伍裡，閉合迴路是常態」，而不是關於 iGEM 整體的陳述。每一份有 good.ihp 內容的隊伍檔案，都依檔案本身的陳述用四分制評分：要拿 4 分，必須有具名的利害關係人、一句具體說過的話，以及檔案明確連回該意見的建置、部署、讀出、安全設計或商業模式上的改變。只記錄到框架、語言、教育材料或證據包有所改變的隊伍，不論流程被包裝得多華麗，都只得 2 或 3 分，而獎項在整個過程中都不納入考量。這套評分標準無法確認某項改變是因為那個建議而做，還是事後才歸因於它；看不到摘要背後的 wiki；也無法區分一條單薄的因果鏈，和一條厚實因果鏈的單薄書面紀錄。評分進行期間仍持續有檔案送進來；最後存在的 93 份全都讀過並評分，所以這個集合在撰寫時是完整的，但沒有封閉。　本文寫成之後，這個集合在 106 份檔案處封閉。本頁後面的另一項分析〈迴路實際上是跟誰閉合的〉重新評了晚到的那十三份，重新計得 106 份中有 71 份閉合迴路、其中九到十份是與非專業人士閉合，而非本文所報的「93 份中六到七份」。多出來的非專業迴路來自晚到的檔案，再加上兩項配方與投遞途徑的改變——這一輪把它們讀成了框架上的改變。結論的形狀沒有變；該處的分母是目前最新的。","scored":93,"kicker_zh":"原創分析","order":30},{"id":"taiwan-cohort","tab":"teams","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"Taiwan at iGEM 2026","title_zh":"台灣在 2026 年 iGEM","lede":"Taiwan fielded thirteen competing teams in 2026 and won six awards, more than any territory in East Asia except China, but every technical award came from the high-school tier and the island is invisible in parts, software and collegiate modelling.","lede_zh":"台灣在 2026 年派出十三支參賽隊伍，拿下六項得獎，是東亞除中國之外最多的，但每一項技術類獎項都來自高中組，而台灣在零件、軟體和大專組建模這三塊完全看不到身影。","body":"Taiwan registered fifteen entries with iGEM in 2026 and thirteen of them competed — eight high-school, four undergraduate, one overgraduate — returning **eight golds, five silvers and no bronzes**, one Top 10 place, six outright award wins and seven further nominations. The wins were GEMS-Taiwan's Best Measurement, Best Hardware and Best Integrated Human Practices, Labi-Taiwan's peer-voted iGEMers Prize, NYCU-Taiwan's Best Project Promotion Video and NCKU-Tainan's Best Infectious Diseases Project; the nominations added Mingdao for Model, NCKU-Tainan for Hardware, NTHU for Food & Nutrition, Labi-Taiwan for Measurement, and GEMS-Taiwan for Presentation, Wiki and Best Village Project. Against the region that is strong in volume and weak in altitude: China fielded 176 competing teams for 24 wins and five Top 10 places, Hong Kong 16 for three wins, three Top 10 places and the high-school Grand Prize first runner-up in HongKong-JSS, Japan seven for nine nominations and no wins, Korea six for none and Singapore four for none. Taiwan therefore out-won Hong Kong six to three on fewer teams and was the only territory outside China to win more than once, but it took a single Top 10 and placed nothing in any Grand Prize at any tier.\n\nThe strength is **instrumentation**: six of the thirteen teams built and documented a device — GEMS-Taiwan's hollow-fibre perfusion bioreactor and two in-line photometers, NCKU-Tainan's CAPTURE-Screen fluorescence reader at US$54–161 against the US$3,500 open-source plate reader it substitutes, NTHU's four-channel frequency-tagged reader with digital lock-in detection, NTHU Taiwan's open-source moving-bed biofilm reactor, Mingdao's single-frame fermentor and Labi-Taiwan's portable electrochemical reader — with human practices and communication a clear second, carrying three of the six wins. The weakness is just as sharply defined: **not one Taiwanese nomination in any of the four parts awards, and none in Best Software**, where even Hong Kong managed one through HK-Joint-School, despite GEMS-Taiwan, NCKU-Tainan and NYCU-Taiwan all releasing licensed code; Best Model appears once, at high-school level, for Mingdao; and the collegiate tier produced no technical special award at all, NYCU-Taiwan's win being a video and NCKU-Tainan's a village category. The clearest symptom is NTHU Taiwan's CatharSys, whose four models dropped a screening factor on a predicted 6% separation, reversed an enzyme-engineering plan when formaldehyde was projected to five times chassis tolerance, stated a falsifiable prediction before the build and reversed a nozzle geometry on first-principles hydraulics — and which won a gold medal and nothing else.\n\nGEMS-Taiwan's three wins and Top 10 place are the island's best result of the year, and they were earned on provenance rather than biology: an input ledger marking every number measured, cited or modelled, a growth rate pre-registered on 1 October and later scored at 0.286 ± 0.010 h⁻¹, and an autoencoder that named a failing photometer 26.7 hours before the channel died. Measured against the collegiate Top 10 sections the dry lab is thin in four named places — there is no inferential statistics, the central secreted-activity figure standing at **n = 1, 7.25 mU/mL, below quantitation** with two induction runs disagreeing on the sign, where NCKU-Tainan a tier up fits mixed models with plate as a random intercept and holds out a treatment to predict; the entire control architecture rests on a published CcaSR Hill curve assumed valid at 20 L although every induction ran at a single light intensity, so nothing in the project tests its own transfer function; the digital twin is an admitted digital shadow, replaying recorded runs with a person making every decision and green-light induction not integrated; and the economics are negative on the team's own numbers, 68 years to payback at perfect efficacy against a partner's 4.9. The step up needs depth in three places rather than more scope: replication and intervals on the central claim with a pre-registered **effect size** rather than a pre-registered growth rate; an in-house CcaSR dose–response across light intensities and scales in absolute fluorescein-calibrated units, which would simultaneously turn 35 contributed SubtiToolKit parts into a collection with the transfer curves a parts award actually rewards; and a twin that controls a run instead of replaying one, with one external software user whose complaints are written down.\n\nThe collaboration map begins with an uncomfortable fact: **GEMS-Taiwan is not in the island's network**. NYCU-Taiwan hosted the 2026 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up at its Bo-Ai campus on 27 July for 53 students and advisors from NYCU-Taiwan, NCKU-Tainan, HIA-Taiwan, VIS and WIST, and NCKU-Tainan's collaboration page adds Mingdao, CCU-Taiwan and NTHU — while neither GEMS-Taiwan nor Labi-Taiwan appears on either list and the GEMS wiki carries no collaboration page at all. The partners therefore follow from complementarity, not goodwill: NTHU Taiwan shares the *Bacillus subtilis* chassis and the open-hardware habit, NCKU-Tainan holds the statistics and the cheap reader, CCU-Taiwan works the rice leafroller on the same crop and the same island, NTHU's AeroSense group has the cohort's deepest computation and admits its decoder was validated on external metal-oxide sensor datasets rather than its own cells, Labi-Taiwan is the only other high-school programme with a real computational stack, and NYCU-Taiwan convenes.\n\nTaiwan's state-backed push is manufacturing-led — the Taiwan Bio-Manufacturing Corporation broke ground on a 15,000 m² GMP facility in Hsinchu Biomedical Science Park in June 2025 with operations from Q2 2026 including Taiwan's first GMP mRNA capability, biomedicine sits inside the 5+2 Innovative Industries Plan, a 33-company delegation went to BIO 2026, and this research found no Taiwan-specific synthetic-biology design programme or funding figure at all. Singapore and Israel are funding precisely that missing layer, with DayOne launching Singapore's first biological data centre prototype in August 2026 and Israel's Innovation Authority committing roughly NIS 70 million in July 2026 to national infrastructure for AI models built on biological data. The 2026 cohort is both the evidence of the gap and the evidence that it can be filled: thirteen teams, six instruments built, zero parts nominations, zero software nominations. GEMS should position itself as Taiwan's dry-lab pipeline rather than as a smaller wet lab, and say so to the Biotechnology and Pharmaceutical Industries Promotion Office and the Ministry of Economic Affairs with Singapore and Israel named as the comparison, to TBMC in Hsinchu as it ramps twenty minutes from NYCU and both NTHU teams, and to the Industrial Technology Research Institute, where NTHU Taiwan already holds a working relationship GEMS would not have to build from scratch.","body_zh":"台灣在 2026 年向 iGEM 註冊了十五個隊伍，其中十三支實際參賽——八支高中、四支大學、一支研究生——拿回**八金、五銀、零銅**、一個 Top 10 席次、六項正式得獎和另外七項入圍。得獎的是 GEMS-Taiwan 的最佳量測、最佳硬體和最佳整合式人類實踐，Labi-Taiwan 由各隊互投的 iGEMers Prize，NYCU-Taiwan 的最佳專案推廣影片，以及 NCKU-Tainan 的最佳傳染病專案；入圍再加上 Mingdao 的模型、NCKU-Tainan 的硬體、NTHU 的食品與營養、Labi-Taiwan 的量測，以及 GEMS-Taiwan 的簡報、Wiki 和最佳 Village 專案。對比這個量大但高度不足的區域：中國派出 176 支參賽隊伍，換得 24 項得獎和五個 Top 10 席次；香港 16 支，換得三項得獎、三個 Top 10 席次，以及 HongKong-JSS 的高中組總冠軍第一亞軍；日本七支，換得九項入圍、零得獎；韓國六支和新加坡四支都掛零。因此台灣以較少的隊伍數，在得獎數上以六比三勝過香港，也是中國以外唯一贏超過一次的地區，但只拿到一個 Top 10，在任何組別的總冠軍都沒有名次。\n\n強項是**儀器**：十三支隊伍中有六支做出並記錄了一台裝置——GEMS-Taiwan 的中空纖維灌流生物反應器和兩台在線光度計、NCKU-Tainan 售價 54 到 161 美元的 CAPTURE-Screen 螢光讀取器（它取代的開放原始碼盤式讀取器要 3,500 美元）、NTHU 帶數位鎖相偵測的四通道頻率標記讀取器、NTHU Taiwan 的開放原始碼移動床生物膜反應器、Mingdao 的單機架發酵槽，以及 Labi-Taiwan 的攜帶式電化學讀取器——人類實踐與溝通明顯是第二強項，拿下六項得獎中的三項。弱項同樣界線分明：**四個零件類獎項沒有任何一項有台灣隊伍入圍，最佳軟體也沒有**，而連香港都靠 HK-Joint-School 拿到一個入圍，儘管 GEMS-Taiwan、NCKU-Tainan 和 NYCU-Taiwan 都釋出了附授權的程式碼；最佳模型只出現一次，在高中組，由 Mingdao 拿下；大專組則完全沒有產生任何技術類特別獎，NYCU-Taiwan 的得獎是一支影片，NCKU-Tainan 的是一個 village 類別。最清楚的症狀是 NTHU Taiwan 的 CatharSys：它的四個模型因為預測的分離度只有 6% 而從篩選中剔除一個因子、在甲醛被推估到底盤耐受度五倍時推翻了一項酵素工程計畫、在建置之前就提出一個可否證的預測，並依第一原理的流體力學推翻了一個噴嘴幾何設計——而它拿到一面金牌，其他什麼都沒有。\n\nGEMS-Taiwan 的三項得獎和 Top 10 席次是台灣今年最好的成績，而且靠的是來源可追溯性，不是生物學：一份把每個數字標明為量測、引用或建模的輸入帳本，一個在 10 月 1 日預先登錄、後來評定為 0.286 ± 0.010 h⁻¹ 的生長速率，以及一個在通道死亡前 26.7 小時就點出光度計即將失效的自動編碼器。但若以大專組 Top 10 的水準來衡量，這個乾實驗室在四個明確的地方偏薄——沒有推論統計，核心的分泌活性數據停在 **n = 1、7.25 mU/mL、低於定量極限**，而兩次誘導實驗連正負號都不一致，相對地高一個層級的 NCKU-Tainan 以盤為隨機截距配適混合模型，還保留一個處理組來做預測；整套控制架構建立在一條已發表的 CcaSR Hill 曲線上，並假設它在 20 L 仍然成立，儘管每一次誘導都只在單一光強度下進行，所以整個專案沒有任何一處檢驗自己的轉換函數；數位孿生被自己承認是數位影子，重播錄下的運轉過程，每一個決定都由人做，綠光誘導也沒有整合進去；而經濟分析用隊伍自己的數字算是負的，在效力完美的前提下回收期是 68 年，對比合作夥伴的 4.9 年。要往上走一階，需要的是三處深度而不是更多範圍：對核心主張做重複實驗與區間估計，並預先登錄**效應量**而不是預先登錄生長速率；在不同光強度與規模下自己做一條 CcaSR 劑量反應曲線，以絕對的螢光素校正單位表示，這同時會把 35 個貢獻出去的 SubtiToolKit 零件變成一套附有轉換曲線的集合，而那正是零件類獎項真正會獎勵的東西；以及一個能控制運轉而不只是重播運轉的孿生，加上一位會把抱怨寫下來的外部軟體使用者。\n\n合作地圖要從一個不太舒服的事實開始：**GEMS-Taiwan 不在台灣這個網絡裡**。NYCU-Taiwan 於 7 月 27 日在博愛校區主辦 2026 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up，共有來自 NYCU-Taiwan、NCKU-Tainan、HIA-Taiwan、VIS 和 WIST 的 53 位學生與指導老師參加，而 NCKU-Tainan 的合作頁面還加上 Mingdao、CCU-Taiwan 和 NTHU——GEMS-Taiwan 和 Labi-Taiwan 都沒有出現在任何一份名單上，GEMS 的 wiki 更完全沒有合作頁面。因此這些合作對象是從互補性推出來的，不是從善意推出來的：NTHU Taiwan 共用 *Bacillus subtilis* 底盤和開放硬體的習慣，NCKU-Tainan 握有統計方法和便宜的讀取器，CCU-Taiwan 在同一種作物、同一座島上研究稻縱捲葉螟，NTHU 的 AeroSense 組擁有這群隊伍中最深的計算能力，並承認它的解碼器是在外部金屬氧化物感測器資料集上驗證，而不是在自己的細胞上，Labi-Taiwan 是唯一另一個有真正計算堆疊的高中計畫，而 NYCU-Taiwan 負責召集。\n\n台灣由國家支持的推動以製造為主——台灣生物醫藥製造公司（TBMC）於 2025 年 6 月在新竹生醫園區為一座 15,000 m² 的 GMP 廠動土，2026 年第二季起營運，其中包括台灣第一條 GMP mRNA 產能；生醫被放在 5+2 產業創新計畫裡；一個 33 家公司的代表團前往 BIO 2026；而這份研究完全沒有找到任何台灣專屬的合成生物學設計計畫或經費數字。新加坡和以色列正好在資助這一層缺口：DayOne 於 2026 年 8 月啟動新加坡第一座生物資料中心原型，以色列創新署則在 2026 年 7 月投入約 7,000 萬新謝克爾，建設以生物資料訓練 AI 模型的國家級基礎設施。2026 這一屆既是缺口的證據，也是缺口可以被填上的證據：十三支隊伍、六台做出來的儀器、零零件入圍、零軟體入圍。GEMS 應該把自己定位為台灣的乾實驗室人才管線，而不是一個比較小的濕實驗室，並且把這件事說給生技醫藥產業發展推動小組和經濟部聽，以新加坡和以色列作為對照；說給正在擴產、距離 NYCU 和兩支 NTHU 隊伍只有二十分鐘的新竹 TBMC 聽；也說給工業技術研究院聽，NTHU Taiwan 在那裡已經有現成的合作關係，GEMS 不必從零開始建。","cards":[{"kicker":"High School · Taipei · id 6072","title":"GEMS-Taiwan — ReLEAF","title_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan — ReLEAF","body":"An optogenetic Bacillus subtilis WB800 bioreactor that reads field sensors and weather forecasts, sets a green-light dose through the CcaSR two-component system and secretes plant-protective proteins beside a Taiwanese paddy. Taiwan's only Top 10 place in 2026 and the island's only triple winner: Best Measurement, Best Hardware and Best Integrated Human Practices, plus nominations for Presentation, Wiki and Best Village Project. The award case rests on provenance rather than biology — a pre-registered growth rate scored after the fact, an autoencoder that named a failing photometer 26.7 hours early, an input ledger marking every number measured, cited or modelled, and a wiki that withdraws its own claims. The hole is that the published CcaSR transfer function the whole control architecture depends on was assumed, never measured, and the central activity figure is n = 1 below quantitation.","body_zh":"一座光遺傳學的 Bacillus subtilis WB800 生物反應器，讀取田間感測器與天氣預報，透過 CcaSR 雙組分系統設定綠光劑量，在台灣的稻田旁分泌植物保護蛋白。這是台灣在 2026 年唯一的 Top 10 席次，也是台灣唯一的三冠得主：最佳量測、最佳硬體和最佳整合式人類實踐，另外入圍簡報、Wiki 和最佳 Village 專案。得獎的理由建立在來源可追溯性上，而不是生物學——一個事後評定的預先登錄生長速率、一個提早 26.7 小時點出光度計失效的自動編碼器、一份把每個數字標明為量測、引用或建模的輸入帳本，以及一個會撤回自己主張的 wiki。缺口在於整套控制架構所依賴的那條已發表 CcaSR 轉換函數是假設來的，從來沒有量測過，而核心的活性數據是 n = 1 且低於定量極限。","chips":["Gold","Top 10","3 wins","Hardware","Measurement","IHP","B. subtilis"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · Taipei · id 6072"},{"kicker":"High School · Taoyuan · id 6511","title":"Labi-Taiwan — BlueCatcher","title_zh":"Labi-Taiwan — BlueCatcher","body":"A nucleic-acid biosensor for major depressive disorder, built by Labi Education, the programme formerly entered as Taipei-KCISLK. The dry lab is the most data-heavy of any Taiwanese high-school team: differential expression, miRNA–mRNA networks, GSEA and WGCNA narrowed 2,656 mature miRNAs to sixteen candidates and then to miR-124-3p as the first engineering target, with machine learning used to prioritise three-way-junction probes and toehold switches, and thermodynamic and kinetic modelling behind the readout. It won the iGEMers Prize, the award the other teams vote for, and was nominated for Best Measurement on a portable electrochemical reader. Like GEMS, it is a Taipei-area commercial-organiser programme and appears on no other Taiwanese team's collaboration page.","body_zh":"一個針對重度憂鬱症的核酸生物感測器，由 Labi Education 製作，這個計畫過去以 Taipei-KCISLK 的名義參賽。它的乾實驗室是台灣所有高中隊伍中資料量最大的：差異表現分析、miRNA–mRNA 網路、GSEA 和 WGCNA 把 2,656 個成熟 miRNA 收斂到十六個候選，再收斂到 miR-124-3p 作為第一個工程標的，並用機器學習排序三向接合探針與 toehold switch，讀出背後還有熱力學與動力學建模。它拿下 iGEMers Prize，也就是由其他隊伍投票選出的獎，並以一台攜帶式電化學讀取器入圍最佳量測。和 GEMS 一樣，它是臺北地區由商業機構營運的計畫，而且沒有出現在任何其他台灣隊伍的合作頁面上。","chips":["Gold","iGEMers Prize","Measurement nominee","miRNA","ML","electrochemical"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · Taoyuan · id 6511"},{"kicker":"Undergrad · Hsinchu · id 6306","title":"NYCU-Taiwan — BITE","title_zh":"NYCU-Taiwan — BITE","body":"A modular food-safety biosensor combining magnetic-bead DNA enrichment, CRISPR-Cas12a recognition and G4–hemin colorimetric readout against synthetic DNA from the Salmonella enterica invA region. The dry lab is organised as SeekProbe_Designer for capture-probe design plus a four-layer model stack from bead capture through Cas12a activation and hairpin-G4 colour to end-to-end prediction, with a Y-shaped multi-chamber device concept. It won Best Project Promotion Video — the island's only collegiate win outside a village category — on a silver medal, which is the gap between communication and technical recognition in one team. NYCU is also the convening institution: it hosted the 2026 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up for 53 people from five teams and built the exchange website behind it.","body_zh":"一個模組化的食品安全生物感測器，結合磁珠 DNA 富集、CRISPR-Cas12a 辨識和 G4–hemin 比色讀出，針對 Salmonella enterica invA 區域的合成 DNA。乾實驗室分成 SeekProbe_Designer 負責捕捉探針設計，加上一套四層模型堆疊，從磁珠捕捉、Cas12a 活化、髮夾-G4 顯色一路到端到端預測，另有一個 Y 形多室裝置的構想。它以銀牌拿下最佳專案推廣影片——這是台灣大專組在 village 類別之外唯一的得獎——而這一支隊伍本身就是溝通能力與技術肯定之間落差的縮影。NYCU 也是召集機構：它主辦了 2026 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up，有來自五支隊伍的 53 人參加，並建立了背後的交流網站。","chips":["Silver","Best Promotion Video","Cas12a","Meet-Up host","food safety"],"kicker_zh":"大學組 · Hsinchu · id 6306"},{"kicker":"Undergrad · Tainan · id 6379","title":"NCKU-Tainan — Capture","title_zh":"NCKU-Tainan — Capture","body":"Two engineered E. coli systems reading the same Pseudomonas aeruginosa quorum-sensing signal: one reports AHL as fluorescence, one deploys aptamers to sponge it out of circulation, aimed at healthcare-associated infection in Taiwanese intensive care. It won Best Infectious Diseases Project and was nominated for Best Hardware for CAPTURE-Screen, a single-cuvette fluorescence reader at US$54–161 against US$3,500 for the plate reader it substitutes, paired with LasReader for 4PL calibration with approximate 95% intervals. The statistics are the best in the Taiwanese cohort — mixed models with plate as a random intercept, geometric-mean ratio effect sizes, and the Cb-2 treatment held out and then predicted. It is also the island's mentoring spine, having run a session for Mingdao in March with three of its own members as Mingdao alumni.","body_zh":"兩套工程化的 E. coli 系統讀取同一個 Pseudomonas aeruginosa 的群體感應訊號：一套把 AHL 以螢光回報，另一套用核酸適體把它從環境中吸走，目標是台灣加護病房的醫療照護相關感染。它拿下最佳傳染病專案，並以 CAPTURE-Screen 入圍最佳硬體——這是一台單一比色管的螢光讀取器，售價 54 到 161 美元，而它取代的盤式讀取器要 3,500 美元——並搭配 LasReader 做 4PL 校正與近似 95% 區間。它的統計是台灣這群隊伍中最好的——以盤為隨機截距的混合模型、幾何平均比的效應量，以及把 Cb-2 處理組保留下來再進行預測。它也是台灣的師徒骨幹，3 月為 Mingdao 辦了一場指導課，自己隊上有三位成員是 Mingdao 的校友。","chips":["Gold","Infectious Diseases win","Hardware nominee","US$54 reader","mixed models"],"kicker_zh":"大學組 · Tainan · id 6379"},{"kicker":"Overgrad · Hsinchu · id 6460","title":"NTHU — AeroSense","title_zh":"NTHU — AeroSense","body":"A biohybrid olfactory platform: Drosophila odorant receptors with ORCO in HEK293 cells, GCaMP6f fluorescence reporting, a four-channel frequency-tagged optical reader with digital lock-in processing, and a fly-inspired network for decoding odour patterns, aimed at early fungal-risk screening in stored bananas. This is the deepest computational work in the Taiwanese cohort — PCA and projection-neuron coding, measured infrared and quantum-vibration features, an OpenPOM comparison, mutation-robustness and cross-species transfer tests, and molecular-dynamics pocket-entry studies. Nominated for Best Food & Nutrition Project and nothing else. The team states its own limit plainly: the decoder was evaluated on external metal-oxide sensor datasets, not on its own cells.","body_zh":"一個生物混合嗅覺平台：在 HEK293 細胞中表現 Drosophila 嗅覺受體與 ORCO，用 GCaMP6f 螢光回報，搭配一台帶數位鎖相處理的四通道頻率標記光學讀取器，以及一個模仿果蠅的網路來解碼氣味樣態，目標是儲運香蕉的早期真菌風險篩檢。這是台灣這群隊伍中最深的計算工作——PCA 與投射神經元編碼、實測的紅外與量子振動特徵、與 OpenPOM 的比較、突變穩健性與跨物種轉移測試，以及分子動力學的口袋進入研究。入圍最佳食品與營養專案，其他什麼都沒有。隊伍自己明白寫出它的限制：解碼器是在外部金屬氧化物感測器資料集上評估，不是在自己的細胞上。","chips":["Gold","Food & Nutrition nominee","GCaMP6f","neural decoder","lock-in optics"],"kicker_zh":"研究生組 · Hsinchu · id 6460"},{"kicker":"High School · Taichung · id 6105","title":"Mingdao — Waste-to-Watt","title_zh":"Mingdao — Waste-to-Watt","body":"Laminated paper food containers from a 7,000-student campus turned into bioethanol by simultaneous saccharification and fermentation, with Zymomonas mobilis acting as a glucose sink so that BglA β-glucosidase never becomes product-inhibited and cellulase never sees accumulating cellobiose. Nominated for Best Model on three stacked models — enzyme-inhibition kinetics characterised under fermentation-compatible conditions rather than the thermophilic optimum, Monod growth for Z. mobilis, and a coupled ODE comparing closed and open systems. The hardware is a single 45 × 45 × 60 cm frame carrying shredding, hydrolysis, fermentation and distillation with the vessel riding to the distillation station on its own hotplate, so the mixture is never transferred. The clearest high-school modelling case in Taiwan after GEMS, and the only Taiwanese Best Model nomination at any tier.","body_zh":"把一所 7,000 名學生校園產生的淋膜紙食品容器，透過同步糖化發酵轉成生質乙醇，並讓 Zymomonas mobilis 充當葡萄糖的吸收端，使 BglA 這個 beta-葡萄糖苷酶永遠不會被產物抑制，纖維素酶也不會遇到累積的纖維二糖。以三個疊起來的模型入圍最佳模型——在符合發酵條件而非嗜熱最佳條件下描述的酵素抑制動力學、Z. mobilis 的 Monod 生長模型，以及一組比較密閉與開放系統的耦合 ODE。硬體是一個 45 × 45 × 60 cm 的單一機架，承載粉碎、水解、發酵和蒸餾，反應槽連同自己的加熱板一起移到蒸餾站，所以混合物從頭到尾不需要轉移。這是台灣在 GEMS 之後最清楚的高中建模案例，也是台灣在任何組別唯一的最佳模型入圍。","chips":["Gold","Best Model nominee","SSF","coupled ODE","fermentor"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · Taichung · id 6105"},{"kicker":"Undergrad · Hsinchu · id 6416 — not on the briefed list","title":"NTHU Taiwan — CatharSys","title_zh":"NTHU Taiwan — CatharSys","body":"A second, separate National Tsing Hua University team, distinct from the overgraduate NTHU entry: engineered Bacillus subtilis forming biofilms on suspended carriers in a moving-bed reactor to treat TMAH and trimethylamine waste from Hsinchu's semiconductor lithography lines. Four models, and each one changed a decision — dissolved oxygen was dropped from the screen at a predicted 6% separation below flask noise, strengthening the bottleneck enzyme alone was shown to drive formaldehyde to five times chassis tolerance so a matched hxlAB upregulation was carried instead, a biofilm model stated a falsifiable prediction before the build, and first-principles hydraulics reversed a nozzle geometry for the pump already bought. CathaBench, its three-tank open-source benchtop MBBR with ESP32 control and an offline Wi-Fi dashboard, was iterated on feedback from ITRI and industry. Gold medal, zero nominations — on this evidence the most under-recognised dry lab in Taiwan in 2026, and the closest technical match to GEMS.","body_zh":"第二支獨立的國立清華大學隊伍，與研究生組的 NTHU 不同：工程化的 Bacillus subtilis 在移動床反應器的懸浮載體上形成生物膜，處理新竹半導體微影產線排出的 TMAH 與三甲胺廢水。四個模型，而且每一個都改變了一項決定——溶氧在預測的分離度只有 6%、低於搖瓶雜訊的情況下被從篩選中剔除；只強化瓶頸酵素被證明會把甲醛推到底盤耐受度的五倍，因此改為同步上調 hxlAB；一個生物膜模型在建置之前就提出可否證的預測；而第一原理的流體力學推翻了一個噴嘴幾何設計，泵都已經買好了。CathaBench 是它的三槽開放原始碼桌上型 MBBR，以 ESP32 控制並配上離線 Wi-Fi 儀表板，是依 ITRI 與業界的意見迭代出來的。金牌，零入圍——以這些證據來看，是台灣 2026 年最被低估的乾實驗室，也是技術上與 GEMS 最接近的隊伍。","chips":["Gold","no awards","B. subtilis","MBBR","ITRI","semiconductor waste"],"kicker_zh":"大學組 · Hsinchu · id 6416 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"Undergrad · Chiayi · id 6408 — not on the briefed list","title":"CCU-Taiwan — NoFold","title_zh":"CCU-Taiwan — NoFold","body":"National Chung Cheng University against the rice leafroller, Cnaphalocrocis medinalis, which folds a rice leaf and eats it from inside and is described as a predominant foliage feeder across Asian rice ecosystems. The framing is the same economic argument GEMS makes: only about 12% of world rice crosses a border, so an Asian yield loss cannot be covered by imports, and the moths arrive on spring winds from overwintering areas such as Hanoi and Nanning with Taiwan on the route. Gold medal, no awards or nominations. Same crop, same island, same pest-pressure problem as ReLEAF, approached from entomology rather than abiotic stress — the most obvious untapped adjacency in the cohort.","body_zh":"國立中正大學對抗稻縱捲葉螟 Cnaphalocrocis medinalis，這種害蟲把稻葉捲起來從裡面吃，文獻描述它是整個亞洲稻作生態系中的主要食葉害蟲。它的切入角度和 GEMS 的經濟論點相同：全世界只有大約 12% 的稻米跨越國界，所以亞洲的減產無法靠進口補上，而這些蛾會隨春季的風從河內、南寧等越冬地北上，台灣就在路線上。金牌，沒有任何得獎或入圍。同一種作物、同一座島、同一個蟲害壓力問題，和 ReLEAF 一樣，只是從昆蟲學而不是非生物逆境切入——這是這群隊伍中最明顯尚未利用的鄰接機會。","chips":["Gold","no awards","rice","crop protection","Chiayi"],"kicker_zh":"大學組 · Chiayi · id 6408 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"High School · Taichung · id 6062 — not on the briefed list","title":"WIST — ultrasound-reporting probiotic","title_zh":"WIST — 以超音波回報的益生菌","body":"Washington International School, Taichung: an engineered E. coli that answers two chemical clues at once, lactate and nitrate, and reports the AND condition by filling with gas vesicles and becoming visible to ultrasound, as a swallowable early screen for colorectal cancer. The acoustic-reporter approach is the same gas-vesicle technology Heidelberg built its collegiate Top 10 project on this year, which makes it an ambitious choice for a high-school team. It carries both a Model and a Software page and declares every figure on the home page a diagram of method rather than acquired data. Gold medal, no awards; it attended the NYCU Meet-Up and appears on NCKU-Tainan's collaboration list.","body_zh":"臺中的 Washington International School：一株工程化的 E. coli 同時回答兩個化學線索——乳酸和硝酸鹽——並以充滿氣囊、在超音波下變得可見的方式回報這個 AND 條件，作為可吞服的大腸癌早期篩檢。這種聲學報告子的作法，和 Heidelberg 今年拿下大專組 Top 10 的專案所用的氣囊技術相同，這讓它對一支高中隊伍來說是個野心很大的選擇。它同時有 Model 和 Software 頁面，並聲明首頁上的每一張圖都是方法示意圖，不是實際取得的資料。金牌，沒有得獎；它出席了 NYCU 的 Meet-Up，也出現在 NCKU-Tainan 的合作名單上。","chips":["Gold","no awards","gas vesicles","ultrasound","AND gate"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · Taichung · id 6062 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"High School · Taipei · id 6200 — not on the briefed list","title":"AEI Prep-Taiwan — SynPETic","title_zh":"AEI Prep-Taiwan — SynPETic","body":"Engineered E. coli making PETase and MHETase side by side on one scaffold — a 'PETosome' — to depolymerise PET in water at 37 °C with no extruder and no metal catalyst, framed around the roughly 2,500 kg of plastic waste the ISS generates a year and the up-to-US$20,000 cost of lifting a kilogram to orbit. One of only two commercially organised Taiwanese high-school programmes besides GEMS and Labi, and it carries Model, Software and Hardware pages. Silver medal, no awards or nominations. The Space village framing makes it the nearest cohort neighbour to GEMS's own village placement.","body_zh":"工程化的 E. coli 把 PETase 和 MHETase 並排接在同一個支架上——一個「PETosome」——在 37 °C 的水中分解 PET，不需要擠出機也不需要金屬催化劑，整個論述圍繞 ISS 每年產生約 2,500 kg 塑膠廢棄物，以及把一公斤物資送上軌道最高可達 20,000 美元的成本。這是除了 GEMS 和 Labi 之外，僅有兩個由商業機構營運的台灣高中計畫之一，而且有 Model、Software 和 Hardware 頁面。銀牌，沒有得獎或入圍。Space village 的定位讓它成為這群隊伍中與 GEMS 自己的 village 歸屬最接近的鄰居。","chips":["Silver","no awards","PETase","Space village","Taipei"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · Taipei · id 6200 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"High School · Taipei · id 6423 — not on the briefed list","title":"VIS — Cadture","title_zh":"VIS — Cadture","body":"VIS@betterworld Lab, testing whether engineered metallothioneins can capture cadmium from industrial wastewater, with a modelling page on cadmium removal. The notable feature is epistemic honesty of the kind GEMS also practises: the home page states that current work measures bacterial growth and GFP response and that direct cadmium removal remains to be tested, rather than implying a result it does not have. Silver medal, no awards or nominations. It attended the NYCU Meet-Up and is on NCKU-Tainan's collaboration list, so it is inside the island network that the Taipei commercial programmes are outside.","body_zh":"VIS@betterworld Lab 測試工程化的金屬硫蛋白能否從工業廢水中捕捉鎘，並有一個關於除鎘的建模頁面。值得注意的是它那種 GEMS 也在實踐的知識論誠實：首頁寫明目前的工作量測的是細菌生長與 GFP 反應，直接除鎘仍有待測試，而不是暗示一個它並不擁有的結果。銀牌，沒有得獎或入圍。它出席了 NYCU 的 Meet-Up，也在 NCKU-Tainan 的合作名單上，所以它在島內網絡之內，而臺北那兩個商業計畫在這個網絡之外。","chips":["Silver","no awards","metallothionein","cadmium","honest scoping"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · Taipei · id 6423 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"High School · Zhubei · id 6156 — not on the briefed list","title":"HIA-Taiwan — Aiy-U-Ready","title_zh":"HIA-Taiwan — Aiy-U-Ready","body":"Hsinchu International Academy in Zhubei, working on aiyu, Ficus pumila var. awkeotsang, a fig endemic to Taiwan that yields hundreds of tonnes a year and is almost unknown outside it. The project is built around that asymmetry — a locally owned crop nobody else is characterising — which is precisely the 'own a dataset nobody else has' logic the industry trend research identifies as a small institution's only durable asset. Silver medal, no awards or nominations, with a Dry Lab model page. It attended the NYCU Meet-Up and is on NCKU-Tainan's collaboration list.","body_zh":"位於竹北的 Hsinchu International Academy，研究愛玉 Ficus pumila var. awkeotsang，這是一種台灣特有的榕屬植物，年產量達數百公噸，在台灣以外幾乎沒人知道。整個專案就建立在這個不對稱上——一種本地擁有、沒有別人在做特性分析的作物——而這正是產業趨勢研究指出的「擁有一份別人沒有的資料集」邏輯，也是小型機構唯一能長久持有的資產。銀牌，沒有得獎或入圍，有一個 Dry Lab 模型頁面。它出席了 NYCU 的 Meet-Up，也在 NCKU-Tainan 的合作名單上。","chips":["Silver","no awards","aiyu","endemic crop","Hsinchu County"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · Zhubei · id 6156 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"High School · New Taipei · id 6103 — not on the briefed list","title":"KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei — Herculyeast","title_zh":"KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei — Herculyeast","body":"Kang Chiao International School's Xiugang campus, running a yeast project with both Model and Software pages under its Dry Lab, plus Entrepreneurship, Inclusivity and Sustainability sections. Silver medal, no awards or nominations. Its sibling campus at Linkou entered separately as Taipei-TWN and was recorded as not eligible, so the Kang Chiao group fielded two high-school entries in 2026 and converted neither — and Labi-Taiwan, the iGEMers Prize winner, is the same Linkou programme's earlier lineage under a new organiser.","body_zh":"康橋國際學校秀崗校區，進行一個酵母專案，Dry Lab 下同時有 Model 和 Software 頁面，另有創業、包容性和永續性章節。銀牌，沒有得獎或入圍。它在林口的姊妹校區以 Taipei-TWN 另外註冊，並被記為不符資格，所以康橋集團在 2026 年派出兩支高中隊伍，兩支都沒有轉換成成績——而 iGEMers Prize 得主 Labi-Taiwan，正是同一個林口計畫在新營運單位之下的前身。","chips":["Silver","no awards","yeast","New Taipei","Kang Chiao"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · New Taipei · id 6103 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"Did not compete · ids 6142, 6543 — not on the briefed list","title":"Taipei-TWN and Oros Biotech","title_zh":"Taipei-TWN 與 Oros Biotech","body":"Two Taiwanese registrations that never reached the competition floor and so are missing from every results table. Taipei-TWN (Kang Chiao International School, Linkou campus, high school, Taipei) carries the status 'not eligible' with no medal and no wiki content. Oros Biotech of Taichung entered the venture-foundry track rather than the competition, has no section, no medal and a 404 wiki — meaning Taiwan's only 2026 entry into iGEM's startup pathway left no public record. Both matter for the denominator: fifteen Taiwanese registrations, thirteen competing teams, and an entrepreneurship route the island used once and did not document.","body_zh":"兩個從未站上競賽場的台灣註冊隊伍，因此在每一份成績表上都看不到。Taipei-TWN（康橋國際學校林口校區，高中，臺北）的狀態是「不符資格」，沒有獎牌也沒有 wiki 內容。臺中的 Oros Biotech 進入的是創投育成路線而不是競賽，沒有組別、沒有獎牌，wiki 回傳 404——也就是說，台灣 2026 年唯一進入 iGEM 新創路徑的隊伍沒有留下任何公開紀錄。兩者對分母都有意義：十五個台灣註冊隊伍、十三支參賽隊伍，以及一條台灣用過一次卻沒有記錄下來的創業路線。","chips":["Not eligible","venture foundry","no wiki","Taipei","Taichung"],"kicker_zh":"未參賽 · ids 6142, 6543 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"Regional comparison","title":"Taiwan against China, Hong Kong, Japan, Korea and Singapore","title_zh":"台灣對比中國、香港、日本、韓國與新加坡","body":"On accepted competing teams: China 176, Hong Kong 16, Taiwan 13, Japan 7, Korea 6, Singapore 4. On outright wins Taiwan placed second in the region with six, behind China's 24 and ahead of Hong Kong's three, with Japan, Korea and Singapore returning none at all — so Taiwan was the only territory outside China to win more than once. On altitude the ranking inverts: China took five Top 10 places and a Grand Prize first runner-up, Hong Kong three Top 10 places and the high-school Grand Prize first runner-up through HongKong-JSS, Singapore one through NUS-Singapore, and Taiwan one through GEMS-Taiwan, with no Taiwanese Grand Prize placing at any tier. In kind the regions differ sharply: China dominates the parts awards and the Registry layer, Hong Kong spreads thirteen nominations across parts, model, software, hardware, education, presentation and wiki, Japan accumulates nominations without converting any, and Taiwan concentrates in hardware, measurement and human practices while taking zero parts and zero software nominations.","body_zh":"以獲受理的參賽隊伍數計算：中國 176、香港 16、台灣 13、日本 7、韓國 6、新加坡 4。以正式得獎數計算，台灣以六項居區域第二，落在中國的 24 項之後、香港的三項之前，而日本、韓國和新加坡完全掛零——所以台灣是中國以外唯一贏超過一次的地區。但以高度來排，順序就反轉了：中國拿下五個 Top 10 席次和一個總冠軍第一亞軍，香港三個 Top 10 席次並透過 HongKong-JSS 拿到高中組總冠軍第一亞軍，新加坡透過 NUS-Singapore 拿到一個，台灣透過 GEMS-Taiwan 拿到一個，而台灣在任何組別的總冠軍都沒有名次。在類型上各區域差異很大：中國主導零件類獎項和 Registry 這一層，香港把十三項入圍分散在零件、模型、軟體、硬體、教育、簡報和 wiki，日本累積入圍卻一項都沒有轉換，而台灣集中在硬體、量測和人類實踐，零件和軟體的入圍數都是零。","chips":["TWN 13 teams","6 wins","1 Top 10","0 parts","0 software","HKG 3 Top 10"],"kicker_zh":"區域比較"}],"table":{"head":["Team","Tier","2026 result","Strength"],"head_zh":["隊伍","組別","2026 年成績","強項"],"rows":[["GEMS-Taiwan (6072)","High School","Gold; Top 10; wins in Measurement, Hardware, Integrated HP; nominees Presentation, Wiki, Village Project","Provenance discipline, pre-registration, four built devices"],["Labi-Taiwan (6511)","High School","Gold; iGEMers Prize winner; Best Measurement nominee","Sequencing-to-target evidence integration; portable electrochemical readout"],["Mingdao (6105)","High School","Gold; Best Model nominee","Enzyme-kinetic and coupled-ODE modelling; integrated single-frame fermentor"],["WIST (6062)","High School","Gold; no awards","Gas-vesicle ultrasound reporting; two-input AND logic"],["AEI Prep-Taiwan (6200)","High School","Silver; no awards","Scaffolded dual-enzyme PET depolymerisation; Space village framing"],["VIS (6423)","High School","Silver; no awards","Metallothionein cadmium capture; honest scoping of untested claims"],["HIA-Taiwan (6156)","High School","Silver; no awards","Taiwan-endemic aiyu crop nobody else is characterising"],["KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei (6103)","High School","Silver; no awards","Yeast chassis with both model and software pages"],["NYCU-Taiwan (6306)","Undergrad","Silver; Best Project Promotion Video winner","Communication, convening; four-layer Cas12a model stack and probe-design software"],["NCKU-Tainan (6379)","Undergrad","Gold; Best Infectious Diseases Project winner; Best Hardware nominee","Inferential statistics with held-out prediction; US$54-161 fluorescence reader"],["NTHU Taiwan (6416)","Undergrad","Gold; no awards","Four models that each reversed or changed a build decision; open-source MBBR"],["CCU-Taiwan (6408)","Undergrad","Gold; no awards","Rice leafroller entomology and rice-trade economics"],["NTHU (6460)","Overgrad","Gold; Best Food & Nutrition Project nominee","Deepest computation in the cohort: receptor prediction, odour decoding, lock-in optics"],["Taipei-TWN (6142)","High School","Not eligible; no medal","No public record"],["Oros Biotech (6543)","Venture foundry","No section, no medal, 404 wiki","Taiwan's only 2026 entry to iGEM's startup pathway"]],"rows_zh":[["GEMS-Taiwan (6072)","高中組","金牌；Top 10；量測、硬體、整合式人類實踐得獎；簡報、Wiki、Village 專案入圍","來源可追溯性的紀律、預先登錄、四台做出來的裝置"],["Labi-Taiwan (6511)","高中組","金牌；iGEMers Prize 得主；最佳量測入圍","從定序到標的的證據整合；攜帶式電化學讀出"],["Mingdao (6105)","高中組","金牌；最佳模型入圍","酵素動力學與耦合 ODE 建模；整合在單一機架上的發酵槽"],["WIST (6062)","高中組","金牌；無得獎","氣囊超音波回報；雙輸入 AND 邏輯"],["AEI Prep-Taiwan (6200)","高中組","銀牌；無得獎","支架化的雙酵素 PET 解聚；Space village 的定位"],["VIS (6423)","高中組","銀牌；無得獎","金屬硫蛋白捕捉鎘；對未經測試的主張誠實界定範圍"],["HIA-Taiwan (6156)","高中組","銀牌；無得獎","台灣特有的愛玉作物，沒有別人在做特性分析"],["KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei (6103)","高中組","銀牌；無得獎","酵母底盤，同時有模型與軟體頁面"],["NYCU-Taiwan (6306)","大學組","銀牌；最佳專案推廣影片得主","溝通與召集；四層 Cas12a 模型堆疊與探針設計軟體"],["NCKU-Tainan (6379)","大學組","金牌；最佳傳染病專案得主；最佳硬體入圍","附保留樣本預測的推論統計；54 到 161 美元的螢光讀取器"],["NTHU Taiwan (6416)","大學組","金牌；無得獎","四個模型各自推翻或改變了一項建置決定；開放原始碼 MBBR"],["CCU-Taiwan (6408)","大學組","金牌；無得獎","稻縱捲葉螟的昆蟲學與稻米貿易經濟"],["NTHU (6460)","研究生組","金牌；最佳食品與營養專案入圍","這群隊伍中最深的計算：受體預測、氣味解碼、鎖相光學"],["Taipei-TWN (6142)","高中組","不符資格；無獎牌","沒有公開紀錄"],["Oros Biotech (6543)","創投育成","無組別、無獎牌、wiki 回傳 404","台灣 2026 年唯一進入 iGEM 新創路徑的隊伍"]]},"partners":[{"name":"NTHU Taiwan (National Tsing Hua University, Hsinchu) — team 6416","why":"The closest technical match to GEMS on the island and the one GEMS has no relationship with. Same chassis (engineered Bacillus subtilis), same commitment to open-source reactor hardware (CathaBench, a three-tank MBBR on ESP32 with an offline dashboard), and a modelling culture that demonstrably changed the build rather than decorating it — it dropped dissolved oxygen from a screen on a predicted 6% separation, reversed an enzyme-engineering plan when formaldehyde was projected to five times chassis tolerance, and reversed a nozzle geometry after first-principles hydraulics. It also already holds the ITRI and industry relationships GEMS would otherwise have to build from nothing. It won gold and nothing else, so it needs legibility as much as GEMS needs rigour.","why_zh":"島上技術上與 GEMS 最接近的隊伍，也是 GEMS 唯一完全沒有關係的那一支。相同的底盤（工程化的 Bacillus subtilis）、同樣投入開放原始碼反應器硬體（CathaBench，一套以 ESP32 控制、配離線儀表板的三槽 MBBR），以及一種確實改變了建置而不只是裝飾的建模文化——它因為預測的分離度只有 6% 而把溶氧從篩選中剔除、在甲醛被推估到底盤耐受度五倍時推翻了一項酵素工程計畫，並在第一原理的流體力學之後推翻了一個噴嘴幾何設計。它也已經握有 GEMS 原本得從零建立的 ITRI 與業界關係。它拿了金牌、其他什麼都沒有，所以它需要易讀性的程度，就跟 GEMS 需要嚴謹度一樣。","firstProject":"A joint Bacillus subtilis measurement standard. Co-characterise the CcaSR green-light transfer function and a suspension-versus-biofilm growth model across both teams' reactors in absolute fluorescein-calibrated units, then release it as a SubtiToolKit-compatible part collection with full transfer curves and a shared SBOL3 record. This closes GEMS's single largest hole — a control architecture resting on a Hill curve it never measured — and gives NTHU Taiwan the Registry-visible artefact its modelling earned and did not get.","firstProject_zh":"一套共同的 Bacillus subtilis 量測標準。在兩支隊伍的反應器上，以絕對的螢光素校正單位共同描述 CcaSR 綠光轉換函數，以及懸浮態與生物膜態的生長模型，然後把它作為相容於 SubtiToolKit 的零件集合釋出，附上完整的轉換曲線和一份共用的 SBOL3 紀錄。這補上了 GEMS 最大的單一缺口——一套建立在從未量測過的 Hill 曲線上的控制架構——同時也給 NTHU Taiwan 一件在 Registry 上看得見的成果，那是它的建模應得卻沒有拿到的。"},{"name":"NCKU-Tainan (National Cheng Kung University, Tainan) — team 6379","why":"The only Taiwanese collegiate team to win a technical-domain award in 2026, and the holder of the exact competence GEMS lacks: mixed models with plate as a random intercept, geometric-mean-ratio effect sizes with 95% intervals, and a held-out treatment used as a genuine prediction test. It is also an instrumentation peer — CAPTURE-Screen reads GFP at US$54-161 against US$3,500 for the open-source plate reader it replaces, and LasReader wraps 4PL calibration with confidence intervals around any reader's output. It is the de facto mentoring spine of Taiwanese iGEM, having run a session for Mingdao with three of its own members as Mingdao alumni, so a GEMS link here also buys entry to the network GEMS skipped.","why_zh":"2026 年唯一拿下技術領域獎項的台灣大專隊伍，也正好握有 GEMS 缺乏的能力：以盤為隨機截距的混合模型、帶 95% 區間的幾何平均比效應量，以及把保留的處理組當成真正的預測檢驗。它同時是儀器上的同儕——CAPTURE-Screen 以 54 到 161 美元讀取 GFP，而它取代的開放原始碼盤式讀取器要 3,500 美元，LasReader 則為任何讀取器的輸出包上帶信賴區間的 4PL 校正。它實質上是台灣 iGEM 的師徒骨幹，曾為 Mingdao 辦過一場指導課，自己隊上有三位成員是 Mingdao 校友，所以在這裡建立連結，也等於買到 GEMS 當初跳過的那個網絡的入場券。","firstProject":"A cross-instrument calibration round-robin. Run GEMS's in-line photometer, NCKU's CAPTURE-Screen and a benchtop plate reader against the same fluorescein and silica standards and the same sfGFP culture series, analyse everything through LasReader so the analysis path is identical, and publish a Taiwan measurement note reporting agreement, disagreement and the limits of each instrument's linear range. It is a Best Measurement-grade artefact for both teams and it imports NCKU's statistics into GEMS's practice by doing rather than by telling.","firstProject_zh":"一場跨儀器的校正循環比對。讓 GEMS 的在線光度計、NCKU 的 CAPTURE-Screen 和一台桌上型盤式讀取器，跑同一組螢光素與二氧化矽標準品和同一系列 sfGFP 培養液，全部透過 LasReader 分析，使分析路徑完全一致，然後發表一份台灣量測報告，說明一致之處、不一致之處，以及每台儀器線性範圍的極限。這對兩支隊伍都是最佳量測等級的成果，而且它是用做的方式、不是用講的方式，把 NCKU 的統計帶進 GEMS 的實務。"},{"name":"CCU-Taiwan (National Chung Cheng University, Chiayi) — team 6408","why":"Working the same crop, the same island and the same problem from the other side: rice under pest pressure rather than rice under abiotic stress. Its framing already matches GEMS's economic argument — that only about 12% of world rice crosses a border, so an Asian yield loss cannot be imported away — and it brings entomology and migration data (spring leafroller flights north from Hanoi and Nanning with Taiwan on the route) that GEMS's stress index does not contain. Gold medal, no awards, no obvious outlet for the work. Geographically it sits between Tainan and Taichung, inside the rice belt both projects target.","why_zh":"從另一側處理同一種作物、同一座島、同一個問題：稻米面對的是蟲害壓力，而不是非生物逆境。它的切入角度已經和 GEMS 的經濟論點一致——全世界只有大約 12% 的稻米跨越國界，所以亞洲的減產無法靠進口補上——而它帶來 GEMS 的逆境指數裡沒有的昆蟲學與遷移資料（春季捲葉螟從河內與南寧往北飛，台灣就在路線上）。金牌，沒有得獎，這些成果也沒有明顯的出口。地理上它位在臺南與臺中之間，就在兩個專案共同指向的稻作帶裡。","firstProject":"A shared Taiwan rice-stress dataset with a published benchmark. Extend GEMS's fitted stress index — 25 years of county rice yields against ERA5 daily reanalysis, scored across 32,767 candidate term combinations — with CCU's leafroller pressure and arrival data, release it as a versioned, licensed dataset with a defined forecasting benchmark task and a public leaderboard, and have both teams state a trigger rule against it in advance. One hectare, two trigger rules, one open benchmark that other teams can beat.","firstProject_zh":"一份共享的台灣稻作逆境資料集，並附上公開的基準測試。把 GEMS 配適出的逆境指數——25 年的縣級稻米產量對 ERA5 每日再分析資料，在 32,767 種候選項組合中評分——擴充進 CCU 的捲葉螟壓力與到達資料，以有版本控制、附授權的資料集釋出，定義一項預測基準任務和一個公開排行榜，並讓兩支隊伍各自事先針對它宣告一條觸發規則。一公頃、兩條觸發規則、一個其他隊伍可以來挑戰的開放基準。"},{"name":"NTHU (National Tsing Hua University, Hsinchu, overgrad AeroSense group) — team 6460","why":"The deepest computational work in the Taiwanese cohort and the natural counterpart to GEMS's protein-design pipeline. It runs receptor-response prediction with measured infrared and quantum-vibration features, an OpenPOM comparison, mutation-robustness and cross-species transfer tests, and molecular-dynamics pocket-entry studies — and it says openly that its decoder was evaluated on external metal-oxide sensor datasets rather than on its own cells. GEMS has the opposite problem: a GRAFT design workflow with docking, all-atom MD and a pre-set AlphaFold confidence gate, and almost no measured validation of what it designs. Each team is the other's missing half.","why_zh":"台灣這群隊伍中最深的計算工作，也是 GEMS 蛋白質設計流程天然的對應方。它做的是受體反應預測，使用實測的紅外與量子振動特徵、與 OpenPOM 的比較、突變穩健性與跨物種轉移測試，以及分子動力學的口袋進入研究——而它公開說明自己的解碼器是在外部金屬氧化物感測器資料集上評估，不是在自己的細胞上。GEMS 的問題正好相反：一套有對接、全原子分子動力學和預先設定 AlphaFold 信賴度門檻的 GRAFT 設計流程，卻幾乎沒有對設計結果做過實測驗證。兩支隊伍各自是對方缺的那一半。","firstProject":"A design-to-measurement validation loop. GEMS proposes a small, pre-registered panel of receptor or binder variants through GRAFT with the confidence gate and acceptance criteria fixed in writing beforehand; NTHU expresses and measures them on its HEK293/GCaMP6f assay and four-channel lock-in reader; both publish the hit rate including every failure, with the predictions timestamped before the measurements. The deliverable is a hit-rate number on a named pipeline, which is the one thing neither team can currently produce alone.","firstProject_zh":"一個從設計到量測的驗證迴路。GEMS 透過 GRAFT 提出一小組預先登錄的受體或結合物變異體，信賴度門檻與通過標準都事先以書面固定；NTHU 在它的 HEK293/GCaMP6f 分析和四通道鎖相讀取器上表現並量測這些變異體；兩隊共同發表命中率，包含每一次失敗，而預測都在量測之前標上時間。交付成果是一條具名流程的命中率數字，而這正是兩支隊伍目前各自都做不出來的東西。"},{"name":"Labi-Taiwan (Labi Education, Taoyuan) — team 6511","why":"The only other Taiwanese high-school programme with a genuine computational stack, and GEMS's structural twin: both are Taipei-area programmes run by commercial organisers, both are absent from NYCU's and NCKU's collaboration lists, and between them they hold four of Taiwan's six 2026 wins. Their skills barely overlap — Labi runs sequencing-to-target evidence integration (2,656 miRNAs narrowed to miR-124-3p through differential expression, miRNA-mRNA networks, GSEA and WGCNA), ML-prioritised nucleic-acid probe design and electrochemical readout, where GEMS runs sensor metrology, reactor control and provenance auditing. Labi's iGEMers Prize also proves it can carry a room, which is the reputational asset a teaching programme needs.","why_zh":"唯一另一個擁有真正計算堆疊的台灣高中計畫，也是 GEMS 結構上的孿生：兩者都是臺北地區由商業機構營運的計畫，都不在 NYCU 和 NCKU 的合作名單上，而台灣 2026 年六項得獎中有四項由它們兩家拿下。他們的技能幾乎不重疊——Labi 做的是從定序到標的的證據整合（2,656 個 miRNA 透過差異表現、miRNA-mRNA 網路、GSEA 和 WGCNA 收斂到 miR-124-3p）、以機器學習排序的核酸探針設計和電化學讀出，而 GEMS 做的是感測器計量、反應器控制和來源稽核。Labi 的 iGEMers Prize 也證明它撐得住一個場子，而那正是一個教學計畫需要的聲譽資產。","firstProject":"A two-module Taiwan high-school dry-lab school, co-taught and open to any Taiwanese team. GEMS teaches provenance ledgers, assumption registers, pre-registration with written pass criteria and instrument cross-calibration; Labi teaches target selection from public sequencing cohorts, probe design and electrochemical quantification. Every participating team leaves with one pre-registered prediction, scored publicly after their next experiment. Teaching is also how GEMS joins the island network it currently sits outside.","firstProject_zh":"一所兩個模組、共同授課、對任何台灣隊伍開放的高中乾實驗室學校。GEMS 教來源帳本、假設登記表、附書面通過標準的預先登錄，以及儀器交叉校正；Labi 教如何從公開定序世代資料中選標的、探針設計和電化學定量。每一支參加的隊伍離開時都帶著一個預先登錄的預測，在他們下一次實驗之後公開評分。教學也是 GEMS 加入目前被排除在外的島內網絡的方式。"},{"name":"NYCU-Taiwan (National Yang Ming Chiao Tung University, Hsinchu) — team 6306","why":"The island's convening institution and its best communicators. It hosted the 2026 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up at its Bo-Ai campus on 27 July for 53 students and advisors from five teams, built a dedicated Taiwan iGEMers exchange website as the public record, and won Best Project Promotion Video. It also sits in Hsinchu alongside both NTHU teams, TBMC's new GMP facility and ITRI, which makes it the right physical venue for anything recurring. What its meet-up lacked was technical content: the roundtables covered team cohesion, leadership and Jamboree preparation, not modelling or measurement.","why_zh":"台灣的召集機構，也是最好的溝通者。它於 7 月 27 日在博愛校區主辦 2026 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up，有來自五支隊伍的 53 位學生與指導老師參加，建立了專屬的 Taiwan iGEMers 交流網站作為公開紀錄，並拿下最佳專案推廣影片。它也位在新竹，與兩支 NTHU 隊伍、TBMC 的新 GMP 廠和 ITRI 同在一地，這讓它成為任何週期性活動最合適的實體場地。它的聚會缺的是技術內容：圓桌討論談的是團隊凝聚、領導和 Jamboree 準備，不是建模或量測。","firstProject":"Co-host the 2027 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up with a dry-lab track, and stand up a permanent Taiwan iGEM dry-lab repository behind it. NYCU supplies the venue, the convening and the website; GEMS supplies a half-day curriculum on modelling, calibration and reproducibility plus the repository's founding contents — shared calibration protocols, fluorescein standards, model code, SBOL3 construct records and a template pre-registration form. The test of success is that a 2027 team other than GEMS publishes a calibrated measurement using it.","firstProject_zh":"共同主辦 2027 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up，加開一條乾實驗室議程，並在它背後建立一個常設的台灣 iGEM 乾實驗室資料庫。NYCU 提供場地、召集能力和網站；GEMS 提供半天的建模、校正與可重現性課程，以及資料庫的創始內容——共用的校正協議、螢光素標準品、模型程式碼、SBOL3 構築體紀錄和一份預先登錄表單範本。成功的檢驗標準是：2027 年有一支不是 GEMS 的隊伍用它發表一份經過校正的量測。"}],"method":"The tally is built from research/results2026.json (captured from competition.igem.org/results/2026 on 19 November 2026) cross-checked team by team against iGEM's own public API — api.igem.org/v1/teams?year=2026 for the full 463-team roster with countries, cities, sections and acceptance status, and api.igem.org/v1/teams/<id>/awards for each team's medals, nominations and wins — which is how nine Taiwanese registrations absent from the results table were found, including NTHU Taiwan (6416), CCU-Taiwan (6408), WIST (6062) and AEI Prep-Taiwan (6200). Project detail comes from the teams' own 2026 wikis, read directly where server-rendered and through a browser for the client-rendered single-page sites (Labi-Taiwan, CCU-Taiwan), plus the existing researched file at research/teams/6072.json for GEMS-Taiwan and research/trends/industry.json for the TBMC, DayOne and Israel Innovation Authority figures. Two Taiwanese registrations could not be verified beyond their API records: Taipei-TWN (6142) is marked not eligible and has no wiki content, and Oros Biotech (6543) returns a 404 wiki, so nothing is claimed about either project; KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei's project could only be identified by name and navigation structure because its wiki ships a largely unmodified template, and Mingdao's medal-level claims rest on the API rather than on a wiki statement.","method_zh":"這份統計以 research/results2026.json 為基礎（於 2026 年 11 月 19 日從 competition.igem.org/results/2026 擷取），並逐隊與 iGEM 自己的公開 API 交叉核對——api.igem.org/v1/teams?year=2026 取得完整 463 支隊伍的名冊，含國家、城市、組別與受理狀態，api.igem.org/v1/teams/<id>/awards 取得每支隊伍的獎牌、入圍與得獎——這也是找到九個未出現在成績表上的台灣註冊隊伍的方法，包括 NTHU Taiwan（6416）、CCU-Taiwan（6408）、WIST（6062）和 AEI Prep-Taiwan（6200）。專案細節來自各隊自己的 2026 wiki，伺服器端渲染的直接讀取，客戶端渲染的單頁網站（Labi-Taiwan、CCU-Taiwan）則透過瀏覽器讀取，另外加上 GEMS-Taiwan 既有的研究檔案 research/teams/6072.json，以及 research/trends/industry.json 中 TBMC、DayOne 和以色列創新署的數字。有兩個台灣註冊隊伍除了 API 紀錄之外無法再驗證：Taipei-TWN（6142）被標記為不符資格，也沒有 wiki 內容；Oros Biotech（6543）的 wiki 回傳 404，所以本文對這兩個專案不做任何主張。KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei 的專案只能靠名稱和導覽結構辨識，因為它的 wiki 用的幾乎是未經修改的樣板；而 Mingdao 的獎牌層級說法是依據 API，不是依據 wiki 上的陳述。","kicker_zh":"原創分析","order":30},{"id":"technique-census","tab":"drylab","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"What 2026's best teams actually reached for","title_zh":"2026 年最強的團隊，實際上用了什麼","lede":"A census of the computational tools named across all 106 team files in this report — and the one habit that separates the podium from everybody else.","lede_zh":"對本報告全部 106 份團隊檔案中提及的運算工具所做的普查——以及把頒獎台和其他人分開的那一個習慣。","body":"Across the 106 team files gathered here, **AlphaFold is still the default**: it is named by 32 teams, more than any other modelling tool and four times as often as Boltz. ProteinMPNN appears in 14 files, Rosetta in 12, ESMFold and RFdiffusion in 8 each. The academic literature has already moved past this — open models now match or beat the gated flagship — but iGEM has not caught up. That lag is an opportunity: a team that works fluently with the current open stack is doing something most of the competition is not.\n\nThe second pattern is that **the dedicated systems-biology tools have quietly lost**. COPASI, once the standard way an iGEM team built a kinetic model, appears in **one** file out of 106. Tellurium appears in one. MATLAB holds on in five. Everything else is Python — named by 44 teams, more than any other single item in the census, usually SciPy integrating an ODE system written by hand, with scikit-learn behind it in 12 files for anything statistical. Teaching COPASI as the entry point to modelling now teaches a tool the field has left behind.\n\nThe third pattern is the surprise. **Techno-economic analysis — costing the thing, modelling unit economics — is done by more high-school teams than undergraduate ones**: 11 against 8, and a far higher share of a smaller tier. High-school teams are being pushed hard on implementation and business thinking, and they are delivering it. Meanwhile GROMACS, full molecular dynamics, appears in 7 undergraduate files, 1 overgraduate file and **never once** in a high-school one. The two tiers are not weaker and stronger versions of each other; they are differently shaped.\n\n**Then the finding that matters.** We checked which teams do both halves of modelling properly: fit the model to their own measured data (parameter estimation, regression, R², RMSE, confidence intervals, error bars) *and* validate it against something held back (held-out data, cross-validation, a separate experimental test). Only **19 of 106** teams do both.\n\nOf those 19, **10 are Top 10 teams — 53%**. Of the 87 that do not close the loop, 20 are Top 10 — **23%**. A team that closes the model–data loop is more than twice as likely to place. And of the nine who closed it without reaching a Top 10, every one still won or was nominated for a major special prize: XJTLU-China and Jilin-China in Best Model, NJU-China took Best Software & AI Project, UBC-Vancouver took Best Diagnostics, CAU-China took Best Food & Nutrition.\n\nThis is the single most actionable number in the report. Not which model you use — whether you close the loop between the model and your own data. It is also, conveniently, the cheapest capability to build: it needs no GPU, no licence and no collaboration. It needs a student who knows what a residual is.","body_zh":"在本報告蒐集的 106 份團隊檔案中，**AlphaFold 仍然是預設選項**：共 32 支團隊提到它，多於任何其他建模工具，是 Boltz 的四倍。ProteinMPNN 出現在 14 份檔案中，Rosetta 12 份，ESMFold 與 RFdiffusion 各 8 份。學術文獻早已走過這一步——開源模型現已可匹敵甚至超越封閉的旗艦模型——但 iGEM 還沒跟上。這個時間差就是機會：能熟練運用當前開源工具鏈的團隊，正在做大多數競爭者沒做的事。\n\n第二個型態是，**專用的系統生物學工具已悄悄落敗**。COPASI 曾經是 iGEM 團隊建立動力學模型的標準做法，如今在 106 份檔案中只出現**一次**。Tellurium 一次。MATLAB 勉強守住五份。其餘全是 Python——共 44 支團隊提及，多於普查中任何其他單一項目，通常是用 SciPy 積分一組手寫的 ODE 系統，統計部分則由 scikit-learn 在 12 份檔案中接手。現在把 COPASI 當作建模的入門，等於是在教一個領域已經放下的工具。\n\n第三個型態令人意外。**做技術經濟分析——計算成本、建立單位經濟模型——的高中隊伍比大學部隊伍還多**：11 對 8，而且在一個規模更小的組別中占比高出許多。高中組被大力要求落實應用與商業思考，而他們做到了。相對地，完整的分子動力學（GROMACS）出現在 7 份大學部檔案、1 份研究生組檔案，在高中組則**一次也沒有**。這兩個層級不是同一件事的強弱版本，它們的形狀本來就不同。\n\n**接著是真正重要的發現。** 我們檢查了哪些團隊把建模的兩半都做完：以自己量到的資料擬合模型（參數估計、回歸、R²、RMSE、信賴區間、誤差棒），*並且*用保留的資料驗證它（held-out 資料、交叉驗證、獨立的實驗測試）。106 支團隊中只有 **19 支**兩者皆備。\n\n這 19 支裡，**有 10 支是 Top 10 團隊——53%**。而在沒有閉合迴圈的 87 支中，只有 20 支進入 Top 10——**23%**。閉合模型與資料迴圈的團隊，進榜機率是兩倍以上。而閉合了迴圈卻未進 Top 10 的那九支，無一例外都拿下或入圍了重要特別獎：XJTLU-China 與 Jilin-China 在最佳模型，NJU-China 拿下最佳軟體與 AI 專案，UBC-Vancouver 拿下最佳診斷，CAU-China 拿下最佳食品與營養。\n\n這是整份報告中最可執行的一個數字。重點不是你用哪個模型，而是你有沒有把模型與自己的資料之間的迴圈閉合起來。而且它恰好也是最便宜的能力：不需要 GPU、不需要授權、不需要合作對象。它需要的是一位知道什麼叫殘差的學生。","cards":[{"kicker":"The headline number","title":"53% versus 23%","title_zh":"53% 對 23%","body":"Teams that both fit their model to their own data and validated it against something held back reached a Top 10 at 53%. Teams that did not reached it at 23% — less than half the rate. Note the sample is already decorated: every team here is a Top 10 or special-prize winner or nominee, so this is loop-closure separating winners from other winners, not from the general field.","body_zh":"既以自身資料擬合模型、又用保留資料加以驗證的團隊，進入 Top 10 的比例是 53%；沒有這麼做的則是 23%，不到一半。請注意樣本本身已經過篩選：這裡每一支團隊都是 Top 10 或特別獎得主／入圍者，因此這是「閉合迴圈」把贏家從其他贏家中分出來，而不是從一般參賽者中分出來。","chips":["19 of 106 closed the loop","10 of those 19 made Top 10"],"kicker_zh":"關鍵數字"},{"kicker":"Still the default","title":"AlphaFold has not been displaced inside iGEM","title_zh":"在 iGEM 裡，AlphaFold 還沒被取代","body":"32 of 106 teams name AlphaFold, four times the rate of Boltz. The research literature moved to the open stack over the past year; the competition has not. The teams already working in Boltz and the MPNN family — Lambert-GA, Heidelberg, GU Frankfurt, DTU-Denmark, Princeton — are visibly ahead of the curve rather than merely current.","body_zh":"106 支團隊中有 32 支提到 AlphaFold，是 Boltz 的四倍。研究文獻在過去一年已轉向開源工具鏈，競賽卻還沒。已經在用 Boltz 與 MPNN 家族的隊伍——Lambert-GA、Heidelberg、GU Frankfurt、DTU-Denmark、Princeton——明顯走在前面，而不只是跟上。","chips":["AlphaFold ×32","ProteinMPNN ×14","Boltz ×8","RFdiffusion ×8"],"kicker_zh":"仍是預設選項"},{"kicker":"A tool generation ended","title":"Python ate the modelling stack","title_zh":"Python 吃掉了整個建模工具鏈","body":"COPASI appears once in 106 files. Tellurium once. MATLAB five times. Python appears in 44 team files, more than any other item in the census, usually SciPy integrating a hand-written ODE system, with scikit-learn behind it for anything statistical. For a programme deciding what to teach, this settles the question: teach Python and the numerical stack, and treat SBML-based tools as an interchange format rather than a starting point.","body_zh":"COPASI 在 106 份檔案中出現一次，Tellurium 一次，MATLAB 五次。Python 出現在 44 份團隊檔案中，多於普查中任何其他項目，通常是用 SciPy 積分手寫的 ODE 系統，統計部分交給 scikit-learn。對一個正在決定要教什麼的課程而言，這已經定案：教 Python 與數值運算工具鏈，把以 SBML 為基礎的工具當作交換格式，而不是起點。","chips":["Python ×44","scikit-learn ×12","COPASI ×1","Tellurium ×1"],"kicker_zh":"一個工具世代的終結"},{"kicker":"The inversion","title":"High-school teams cost their projects; undergraduates often don't","title_zh":"高中隊伍會算成本，大學部常常不算","body":"Techno-economic analysis appears in 11 high-school files against 8 undergraduate ones, and in a far higher share of the smaller tier. Full molecular dynamics runs the other way: 7 undergraduate files, 1 overgraduate, and never once in a high-school file. The tiers are differently shaped rather than simply further apart, and a high-school programme that assumes it must catch up on everything is aiming at the wrong gap.","body_zh":"技術經濟分析出現在 11 份高中組檔案中，對比大學部的 8 份，而且在規模較小的組別裡占比高出許多。完整的分子動力學則完全相反：7 份大學部、1 份研究生組，高中組一次也沒有。兩個層級的形狀不同，而不只是距離遠近的差別。一個假定自己必須在所有面向上追趕的高中課程，瞄錯了缺口。","chips":["Techno-economic: 11 HS vs 8 UG","GROMACS: 7 UG, 0 HS"],"kicker_zh":"反轉"},{"kicker":"A weaker result, reported anyway","title":"Publishing your failures: an effect that shrank when we added data","title_zh":"公開失敗：加入更多資料後，效果反而縮小了","body":"Several analysts noticed the same thing independently — Toronto, WageningenUR and UZurich each put a prominent negative result on the wiki, and two won the award in that exact category. On the first 54 files the pattern looked real: 54% against 41%. Re-run across all 106 it collapses to **33% against 27%**, and the measurement was always partly circular — it detects how candid *our own summary* of a team was, not reliably how candid the team was. We are leaving it in because reporting the finding that weakened is the same discipline the rest of this page is about. Publish the negative result because it is honest, not because it wins prizes.","body_zh":"好幾位分析員各自獨立注意到同一件事——Toronto、WageningenUR 與 UZurich 都在 wiki 上放了顯著的負面結果，其中兩隊正是在對應類別中獲獎。在最初的 54 份檔案上，這個型態看起來是真的：54% 對 41%。但擴及全部 106 份重跑之後，它塌縮為 **33% 對 27%**；而且這個量測本來就帶有循環性——它偵測到的是*我們自己的摘要*有多坦白，而未必能可靠反映團隊有多坦白。我們把它留下來，是因為「報告那個變弱的發現」正是本頁其餘部分所談的同一種紀律。公開負面結果，是因為那樣才誠實，而不是因為那樣會得獎。","chips":["first 54 files: 54% vs 41%","all 106 files: 33% vs 27%"],"kicker_zh":"較弱的結果，照樣報告"},{"kicker":"What this means for GEMS","title":"The cheapest capability is the one that correlates with winning","title_zh":"最便宜的能力，正好就是和得獎相關的那一個","body":"Closing the model-data loop needs no GPU, no licence, no partner lab and no new chassis. It needs a student who can fit a curve, report an uncertainty and hold data back for a test. That is a term's teaching, and on this evidence it moves the result more than any tool choice. It is Phase 2 of the roadmap for exactly this reason.","body_zh":"閉合模型與資料之間的迴圈，不需要 GPU、不需要授權、不需要合作實驗室、也不需要新的底盤。它需要的是一位會擬合曲線、會報告不確定度、並且懂得保留資料做測試的學生。那是一個學期的教學量，而根據這些證據，它對結果的影響大於任何工具選擇。這正是它成為路線圖階段二的原因。","chips":["No GPU required","One term of teaching"],"kicker_zh":"這對 GEMS 的意義"}],"method":"Counts come from pattern-matching the dry-lab and science-for-good fields of all 106 team files in this report, not from reading the wikis a second time, so a technique a team used but did not write up is invisible here. The sample is decorated teams only — every file is a Top 10 or special-prize winner or nominee — so the baselines are not the whole competition. The loop-closure test looks for explicit language about fitting, uncertainty and validation; a team that did the work but described it loosely will be undercounted. An earlier version of this page reported 71% against 40% from a 54-file snapshot taken while research was still landing; the figures above supersede it. Read the numbers as a ranking, not a measurement.","method_zh":"計數方式是對本報告全部 106 份團隊檔案的乾實驗室與科學向善欄位做樣式比對，而非重新閱讀 wiki，因此團隊做了卻沒寫下來的技術在這裡是看不見的。樣本僅限獲獎隊伍——每一份檔案都是 Top 10 或特別獎得主／入圍者——所以基準值並不代表整個競賽。迴圈閉合的判準是尋找明確描述擬合、不確定度與驗證的文字；做了卻寫得含糊的團隊會被低估。本頁較早的版本依據研究仍在進行時的 54 份檔案快照，報告了 71% 對 40%；上述數字取代該版本。請把這些數字當成排序，而不是量測。","kicker_zh":"原創分析","order":30},{"id":"good-patterns","tab":"good","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"What separated real engagement from outreach theatre","title_zh":"真正的參與，和表演式推廣，差別在哪裡","lede":"Across the 2026 field, the teams whose Science for Good work counted did four things the rest did not.","lede_zh":"綜觀 2026 年的參賽團隊，那些「科學向善」真正有份量的隊伍，做了另外四件其他人沒做的事。","body":"**They designed education from data, then measured it like an experiment.** UCAS-China did not start from \"raise awareness\". It ran clinician interviews and a 461-person questionnaire, found that patients stop medication once they feel better and that parents refuse to start it for children out of fear of side effects, and made *compliance* the target instead of awareness. UOregon wrote three separate curricula for three audiences with different prior knowledge and ran them as three DBTL iterations across June, July and October, carrying each round's lessons forward. HFI ran everything through a five-step cycle it named CLEAR, in which **every activity had to report a measured outcome and a change for the next iteration**.\n\nThe sharpest version of this is publishing the results when they are bad. GEMS-Taiwan ran pre- and post-lesson surveys with 140 students across five schools and published per-question accuracy charts including the failures — only 30% of students got DNA base pairing right. That number is worth more to the next teacher than any photograph of a full classroom.\n\n**They trained themselves before training anybody else.** Nineteen GU Frankfurt members took the \"Basics of Science Communication\" workshop run by NaWik, Germany's national institute for science communication, and used its core-message and cloverleaf tools as the basis of everything that followed. Most teams treat communication as something you already know how to do because you can talk.\n\n**They put disagreeing people in the same room.** Oxford's *Buzz In* podcast is the most quietly radical format in the 2026 field: rather than interviewing stakeholders separately and summarising, it deliberately paired people who disagree — a Varroa-resistance academic with a commercial beekeeper on whether to treat at all, then an industry council CEO with amateur beekeepers. Disagreement is the thing most human-practices pages are built to smooth over; Oxford made it the content.\n\nKIT won Inclusivity by turning the same honesty inward. It read the iGEM Diversity and Inclusion Committee's own writing, surveyed five previous iGEM gender-equity projects, and noticed that nearly all of them face **outward** — role models, outreach to girls, awareness — and almost none examine the team itself. So KIT examined the team itself.\n\n**They quantified the need, and built a business model that was not \"sell the product\".** Oxford states the problem in numbers rather than adjectives: Australia's failed Varroa eradication cost A$101 million and destroyed about 30,000 hives; surveyed US commercial operations lost roughly 62% of colonies in 2024–25. DTU-Denmark anchors on a date and a measurement: the Danish wind industry's voluntary landfill ban took effect on 1 January 2026, and a Danish EPA screening detected bisphenol A in every tank leaching test on blade material.\n\nThen the models themselves. HongKong-JSS sells **Certification-as-a-Service** — farmers subscribe annually, the team tests soil on site, passing farms get a \"Heavy Metal-Free\" logo for supermarket packaging that earns a premium, and surprise re-tests throughout the year are affordable precisely because the test is cheap. GEMS-Taiwan deploys through farmer collectives rather than direct sales, because its own fleet analysis shows a reactor owned by a single farm sits idle most of the season. GU Frankfurt chose exclusive licensing over a start-up because an autologous cell therapy's facility and specialist-salary costs cannot be carried by a spin-out, and has a letter of support from Miltenyi Biotec to show for it. XJTLU-China gives catmaOS away, on the argument that accessibility *is* the commercial thesis.\n\nUAlberta's case is the most evidentially careful: demand is tabulated by customer role **with the strength of each piece of evidence named** — two clinician letters of support, a signed letter of intent from one clinic, 86% of 38 surveyed dry eye patients interested, an application at interview stage with Nucleate Canada. And UCAS-China opens its commercial section by stating outright that the case must rest on a defined unmet need rather than on technological novelty, then tabulates the strengths of the existing drugs it would have to displace. A team willing to argue against itself is a team worth believing.","body_zh":"**他們從資料出發設計教育，再像做實驗一樣去量測它。** UCAS-China 的起點不是「提升認知」。他們訪談臨床醫師、做了 461 人的問卷，發現病人一感覺好轉就停藥、家長因為害怕副作用而不願意讓孩子開始用藥，於是把目標從「認知」改成*服藥遵從性*。UOregon 為三種先備知識不同的對象寫了三套獨立課程，並在六月、七月與十月以三次 DBTL 迭代執行，把每一輪的教訓帶進下一輪。HFI 則讓所有活動都跑一個他們命名為 CLEAR 的五步驟循環，其中**每一項活動都必須回報一個量測到的結果，以及下一次要改什麼**。\n\n這件事最鋒利的版本，是在結果難看的時候照樣公布。GEMS-Taiwan 在五所學校對 140 名學生做了課前課後問卷，並公布逐題正確率圖表，包含失敗的部分——DNA 鹼基配對只有 30% 的學生答對。對下一位老師而言，這個數字比任何一張坐滿學生的照片都有價值。\n\n**他們先訓練自己，再去訓練別人。** GU Frankfurt 有 19 位成員上了德國國家科學傳播研究所 NaWik 的「科學傳播基礎」工作坊，並以其核心訊息與四葉草等工具作為後續一切的基礎。多數團隊把傳播當成「反正我會說話就會做」的事。\n\n**他們把意見不合的人放進同一個房間。** Oxford 的 *Buzz In* podcast 是 2026 年最安靜地激進的形式：它不是分別訪談各方再做摘要，而是刻意把意見相左的人配成一對——讓研究 Varroa 抗性的學者與商業養蜂人辯論「到底該不該用藥」，再讓產業公會執行長與業餘養蜂人對談。多數人類實踐頁面的設計目的就是把分歧抹平；Oxford 直接把分歧當成內容。\n\nKIT 則把同樣的誠實轉向內部，因而拿下包容性獎。他們讀了 iGEM 多元與包容委員會自己的文章，檢視了五個過去的 iGEM 性別平等專案，注意到它們幾乎全部朝**外**——榜樣、對女孩的推廣、意識提升——而幾乎沒有一個檢視團隊自身。於是 KIT 檢視了團隊自身。\n\n**他們把需求量化，而且做出來的商業模式不是「把產品賣掉」。** Oxford 用數字而非形容詞陳述問題：澳洲失敗的 Varroa 根除行動花了 1.01 億澳元、摧毀約 3 萬個蜂箱；受調查的美國商業蜂場在 2024–25 年損失了約 62% 的蜂群。DTU-Denmark 則錨定在一個日期與一次量測上：丹麥風電產業的自願掩埋禁令自 2026 年 1 月 1 日生效，而丹麥環保署的篩檢在葉片材料的每一次槽式溶出試驗中都測到雙酚 A。\n\n接著是商業模式本身。HongKong-JSS 賣的是**認證即服務**——農民年度訂閱，團隊到場檢測土壤，通過的農場取得「無重金屬」標章可用於超市包裝並賣出溢價，而全年不定期的突擊複檢之所以負擔得起，正是因為檢測又便宜又快。GEMS-Taiwan 透過農民合作社而非直接銷售來部署，因為他們自己的機隊分析顯示：單一農場自有的反應器一整季大部分時間都閒置。GU Frankfurt 選擇獨家授權而非自行創業，因為自體細胞治療的廠房與專業人力成本不是一間新創扛得起的，而他們手上有 Miltenyi Biotec 的支持信。XJTLU-China 則把 catmaOS 免費釋出，理由是可及性*本身*就是商業論點。\n\nUAlberta 的案例在證據上最為嚴謹：需求依客戶角色列表，而且**每一項證據的強度都被標明**——兩封臨床醫師支持信、一間診所簽署的意向書、38 位乾眼症受訪患者中 86% 有興趣、一件已進入面試階段的 Nucleate Canada 申請。UCAS-China 則在商業章節的開頭直接寫明：這個案子必須建立在明確的未滿足需求上，而不是技術新穎性，接著列表說明它必須取代的既有藥物有哪些優點。一支願意對自己提出反方論證的團隊，才值得相信。","cards":[{"kicker":"The format worth stealing","title":"Oxford's Buzz In: put the disagreement on the record","title_zh":"Oxford 的 Buzz In：把分歧記錄下來","body":"A three-episode podcast that deliberately paired stakeholders who disagree, rather than interviewing them separately and summarising. Episode one put a Varroa-resistance academic opposite a commercial beekeeper on whether to treat at all. Most human-practices pages exist to smooth disagreement away; this one makes it the content, and it is far harder to fake than a list of meetings.","body_zh":"一個三集的 podcast，刻意把意見相左的利害關係人配對，而不是分別訪談後再做摘要。第一集讓研究 Varroa 抗性的學者，與商業養蜂人正面交鋒「到底該不該用藥」。多數人類實踐頁面的存在目的是把分歧抹平；這一個把分歧變成內容，而且它比一份會議清單難假造得多。","chips":["3 episodes","paired opponents"],"kicker_zh":"值得借用的形式"},{"kicker":"The habit worth stealing","title":"Publish the question your students got wrong","title_zh":"公布學生答錯的那一題","body":"GEMS-Taiwan surveyed 140 students across five schools before and after each lesson and published per-question accuracy — including DNA base pairing, where only 30% answered correctly. Reporting the failure makes the whole dataset credible and hands the next teacher something actionable. A photograph of a full classroom does neither.","body_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 在五所學校對 140 名學生做課前課後問卷，並公布逐題正確率——包括 DNA 鹼基配對，只有 30% 答對。報告失敗讓整份資料變得可信，也交給下一位老師一個可以採取行動的東西。一張坐滿學生的照片兩者都做不到。","chips":["140 students · 5 schools","30% on base pairing"],"kicker_zh":"值得借用的習慣"},{"kicker":"The habit worth stealing","title":"Train the team before training the public","title_zh":"先訓練團隊，再去教公眾","body":"Nineteen GU Frankfurt members took the Basics of Science Communication workshop from NaWik, Germany's national science-communication institute, and built everything afterwards on its core-message and cloverleaf tools. Science communication is a craft with a literature; almost every other team treats it as something you can already do because you can talk.","body_zh":"GU Frankfurt 有 19 位成員上了德國國家科學傳播研究所 NaWik 的「科學傳播基礎」工作坊，並以其核心訊息與四葉草工具為基礎建構後續所有內容。科學傳播是一門有文獻的技藝；幾乎其他所有團隊都把它當成「我會說話所以我就會」。","chips":["19 members trained","NaWik"],"kicker_zh":"值得借用的習慣"},{"kicker":"The business model worth stealing","title":"Sell the certificate, not the instrument","title_zh":"賣證書，不要賣儀器","body":"HongKong-JSS does not sell its mercury assay. Farmers subscribe annually, the team tests on site, passing farms get a 'Heavy Metal-Free' logo for supermarket packaging that commands a premium, and surprise re-tests through the year keep the certificate honest — affordable precisely because the test itself is cheap. The cheapness of the science becomes the business model rather than a weakness.","body_zh":"HongKong-JSS 不賣他們的汞檢測。農民年度訂閱，團隊到場檢測，通過的農場取得可用於超市包裝的「無重金屬」標章並賣出溢價，而全年不定期的突擊複檢維持證書的公信力——之所以負擔得起，正因為檢測本身很便宜。科學的廉價在這裡變成商業模式，而不是弱點。","chips":["Certification-as-a-Service","surprise re-tests"],"kicker_zh":"值得借用的商業模式"},{"kicker":"The business model worth stealing","title":"Name the strength of each piece of evidence","title_zh":"標明每一項證據的強度","body":"UAlberta tabulates demand by customer role and says how strong each item is: two clinician letters of support, one signed letter of intent, 86% of 38 surveyed patients interested, one application at interview stage with Nucleate Canada. A letter of intent and a survey response are not the same kind of evidence, and saying so is what makes the table worth reading.","body_zh":"UAlberta 依客戶角色把需求列表，並說明每一項證據有多強：兩封臨床醫師支持信、一封已簽署的意向書、38 位受訪患者中 86% 有興趣、一件進入面試階段的 Nucleate Canada 申請。一封意向書和一份問卷回覆不是同一種證據，而把這件事講清楚，正是這張表值得讀的原因。","chips":["evidence graded by strength"],"kicker_zh":"值得借用的商業模式"},{"kicker":"For GEMS","title":"Argue against yourself in public","title_zh":"公開地為自己提出反方論證","body":"UCAS-China opens its commercial section by saying the case must rest on unmet need rather than technological novelty, then lists what the existing drugs do well. GEMS-Taiwan publishes a 68-year payback against a partner's 4.9-year figure and names the disagreement instead of resolving it. This is the practice that most distinguishes the 2026 podium, and it costs nothing but nerve.","body_zh":"UCAS-China 在商業章節的開頭就說：這個案子必須建立在未滿足需求上，而非技術新穎性，接著列出既有藥物的優點。GEMS-Taiwan 公布了 68 年的回收期，對照合作夥伴算出的 4.9 年，並指名這個歧異而不去解決它。這是 2026 年頒獎台上最顯著的共同做法，而它唯一的代價是膽識。","chips":["no budget required"],"kicker_zh":"給 GEMS"}],"method":"Drawn from the Science for Good fields of the team files in this report, each researched from the team's own 2026 wiki. Audience numbers and survey sizes are the teams' own figures and are not independently verified. The judgement about what 'counted' is ours; the team files and the wikis behind them are linked so a reader can disagree. GEMS-Taiwan is the report author's own team and appears here on the same terms as the rest.","method_zh":"資料取自本報告團隊檔案中的「科學向善」欄位，每一份都來自該隊自己的 2026 wiki。參與人數與問卷樣本數為各隊自報數字，未經獨立查證。關於「什麼才算數」的判斷出自我們；團隊檔案與其背後的 wiki 都附有連結，讀者可以自行判斷是否同意。GEMS-Taiwan 是本報告作者自己的團隊，在此與其他隊伍適用相同標準。","kicker_zh":"原創分析","order":32},{"id":"highschool-ceiling","tab":"drylab","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"The high-school ceiling, measured honestly","title_zh":"誠實地量一次高中組的天花板","lede":"What a high-school dry lab can actually reach in one season — and the finding that the gap is not about tools.","lede_zh":"一個高中乾實驗室在一季之內真正能做到什麼——以及那個發現：差距不在工具。","body":"Read the ten High School Top 10 dry labs side by side and the first surprise is how ordinary the software is. **Eton-College-UK** built its protease substrate predictor out of L2-regularised logistic regression and a BLOSUM62-smoothed position-specific scoring matrix — techniques older than the students using them. **HFI** used NetLogo, which is free and was designed for schools. **GHCIS** used a local install of NUPACK. **HangzhouFourteenAP** used PyMOL and FoldX. **HKSSC** used AlphaFold, UCSF Chimera and HotSpot Wizard. **HongKong-HS** reused another team's tool outright — miRADAR, released by Wageningen's 2024 team — rather than rebuilding it. Almost none of this costs money, and none of it requires a cluster.\n\nOnly **Lambert-GA**, the Grand Prize winner, works at the frontier of the toolchain: BindCraft, Boltz-2, Protenix, Mosaic. And even there the thing that earned Best Model was not the tools. It was that they **benchmarked the confidence metrics themselves** — ipSAE, ipTM and a 38-metric ensemble, against 5,721 labelled experimental designs — found the ensemble barely beat chance at ROC-AUC 0.541, noticed that their own eventual hit did not have the best score, and published all of that rather than quietly reporting the hit.\n\nThat is the pattern, and it holds across the whole tier. **The differentiator at high-school level is evaluation discipline, not tool sophistication.**\n\nThe evidence is specific. Eton clustered near-duplicate sequences by Hamming distance and split whole clusters across folds, then ran a label-shuffle control and a composition-only ablation — three cheap steps that separate a real classifier from a leaky one. **HongKong-JSS** split runs into calibration and validation *before* fitting anything, subtracted a matched control from the same run and timepoint, and reported RMSE on held-out runs with the failures left in. HKSSC could not measure molar enzyme concentration, so rather than report an invalid *k*cat/*K*m they defined and justified a mass-normalised metric valid only below *K*m, then ran a two-way ANOVA, found unequal variances, and moved to a median-based test. GHCIS specified its colour-classification algorithm down to the equation and the threshold, including an explicit **\"unresolved, and must not be read as Negative\"** state, and shipped it with one-command Docker deployment. HangzhouFourteenAP reported the prediction that lost: FoldX ranked Y166Q first, the bench preferred Q172P, and the wiki revises its own ranking while using BCA normalisation to rule out protein load as the explanation.\n\n**GEMS-Taiwan** belongs on that list and is worth reading closely, because the wiki is unusually candid about its own weaknesses. The strengths are real: a genuinely pre-registered growth-rate forecast, registered on 1 October and scored on run 6, which landed inside its stated interval; an autoencoder that flagged a failing photometer 26.7 hours before it died; and a crop-stress index fitted to 25 years of county rice yields rather than to expert judgement. The weaknesses are stated by the team itself: secreted activity at n=1 and below the limit of quantitation; two induction runs that disagree on the *sign* of the change; a Hill curve assumed to hold at 20 L when every induction ran at a single light intensity; a 2.44× rice canopy correction that is modelled, not measured; an efficacy coefficient of 0.58 explicitly withdrawn; and a payback period of 68 years on the team's own loss figure against a partner's 4.9 years, with the disagreement named rather than resolved. Naming the disagreement instead of picking the flattering number is the practice worth keeping.\n\n**And the control case.** **GCGS** reached the High School Top 10 with no model page and no software page at all — both routes return 404. Its one modelling claim is an undocumented circuit-level simulation with no parameters, equations or tooling named. A team can still place in the top ten of its section with essentially no dry lab. What GCGS could not do is win a modelling, measurement or software prize, and that is the precise shape of the opportunity.","body_zh":"把高中組 Top 10 的十個乾實驗室並排來讀，第一個意外是：他們用的軟體有多麼普通。**Eton-College-UK** 的蛋白酶受質預測器，是用 L2 正規化的 logistic regression 加上以 BLOSUM62 平滑的位置特異性計分矩陣（PSSM）做出來的——這些技術比使用它們的學生還老。**HFI** 用的是 NetLogo，免費，而且本來就是為學校設計的。**GHCIS** 用本機安裝的 NUPACK。**HangzhouFourteenAP** 用 PyMOL 與 FoldX。**HKSSC** 用 AlphaFold、UCSF Chimera 與 HotSpot Wizard。**HongKong-HS** 則直接沿用別隊的工具——Wageningen 2024 年釋出的 miRADAR——而不是重做一個。這些幾乎都不花錢，也都不需要叢集運算。\n\n只有總冠軍 **Lambert-GA** 站在工具鏈的前沿：BindCraft、Boltz-2、Protenix、Mosaic。但即使在那裡，替他們贏得最佳模型的也不是工具，而是他們**對信心指標本身做了基準測試**——拿 ipSAE、ipTM 與一組 38 項指標的集成，去對照 5,721 個有實驗標註的設計——發現該集成的 ROC-AUC 只有 0.541，幾乎只比亂猜好一點，還注意到自己最後成功的那個設計分數並不是最高的，然後把這一切全部公開，而不是安靜地只報成功的那一個。\n\n這就是整個型態，而且在整個層級中都成立。**高中層級的差異來自評估的紀律，而不是工具的精密度。**\n\n證據很具體。Eton 以 Hamming 距離把近似重複的序列分群，再把整群一起分到同一個 fold，接著跑標籤洗牌對照與僅用胺基酸組成的消融測試——三個便宜的步驟，就把一個真正的分類器和一個資料外洩的分類器分開了。**HongKong-JSS** 在擬合任何東西*之前*就把實驗批次分成校正組與驗證組，扣除同一批次、同一時間點的對照，並在保留批次上報告 RMSE，而且把失敗的資料留在裡面。HKSSC 無法量到酵素的莫耳濃度，於是沒有去報一個無效的 *k*cat/*K*m，而是定義並論證了一個只在低於 *K*m 時有效的質量標準化指標，接著做雙因子 ANOVA，發現變異數不齊，再改用以中位數為基礎的檢定。GHCIS 把顏色判讀演算法寫到方程式與閾值的層級，包含一個明確的**「無法判定，且不得視為陰性」**狀態，並以一行指令的 Docker 部署出貨。HangzhouFourteenAP 報告了那個輸掉的預測：FoldX 把 Y166Q 排第一，實驗卻偏好 Q172P，而 wiki 修正了自己的排序，同時用 BCA 標準化排除「蛋白質上樣量不同」這個解釋。\n\n**GEMS-Taiwan** 也屬於這份名單，而且值得仔細讀，因為這個 wiki 對自身弱點的坦白程度相當罕見。強項是真的：一個貨真價實的預先登記成長率預測，10 月 1 日登記、在第 6 批次評分，結果落在所宣告的區間內；一個在光度計故障前 26.7 小時就示警的自編碼器；以及一個以 25 年各縣市稻作產量擬合、而非靠專家判斷加權的作物逆境指數。弱點則由團隊自己寫出來：分泌活性 n=1 且低於定量極限；兩次誘導實驗對變化的*正負號*彼此矛盾；Hill 曲線被假定在 20 公升仍然成立，但所有誘導都只在單一光強度下進行；2.44 倍的水稻冠層修正是模擬出來而非量出來的；一個 0.58 的效能係數被明確撤回；以及以團隊自己的損失數字計算出 68 年的回收期，對比合作夥伴算出的 4.9 年，而這個歧異被指名寫出，而不是被解決掉。把歧異寫出來、而不是挑一個好看的數字，正是值得保留的做法。\n\n**還有對照組。** **GCGS** 在完全沒有 model 頁也沒有 software 頁的情況下進入高中組 Top 10——兩個路徑都回傳 404。它唯一的建模主張，是一個沒有記載參數、方程式或工具名稱的電路層級模擬。一支隊伍確實可以幾乎沒有乾實驗室，仍然進入該組前十名。但 GCGS 做不到的是拿下建模、測量或軟體獎項——而那正是機會的確切形狀。","cards":[{"kicker":"The ceiling","title":"Lambert-GA, and what the frontier costs","title_zh":"Lambert-GA，以及站上前沿的代價","body":"Four linked models: protein-design metric benchmarking on 5,721 labelled designs, a Sobol-analysed oral pharmacokinetic model, a 13-ODE SimBiology RNAi network, and an individual-based six-year, 800-run colony epidemiology. They produced the first reported DWV VP3 minibinder for under $400 of compute, released the open-source PRINCE site ranker (45.8% top-3 hit rate against 23.8% random on a no-homolog subset), and an $80 dryer externally validated at two universities. This is the ceiling, and it is reachable.","body_zh":"四個彼此連動的模型：在 5,721 個有標註的設計上做蛋白質設計指標的基準測試、一個經 Sobol 分析的口服藥物動力學模型、一個 13 條 ODE 的 SimBiology RNAi 網路，以及一個為期六年、跑 800 次的個體導向族群流行病學模擬。他們以不到 400 美元的運算成本做出第一個被報導的 DWV VP3 minibinder，釋出開源的 PRINCE 位點排序工具（在無同源子集上，前三名命中率 45.8%，對照隨機的 23.8%），以及一台 80 美元、經兩所大學外部驗證的乾燥裝置。這就是天花板，而且搆得到。","chips":["Boltz-2 · BindCraft · Protenix","under $400 of compute"],"kicker_zh":"天花板"},{"kicker":"The floor","title":"GCGS: Top 10 with no dry lab at all","title_zh":"GCGS：完全沒有乾實驗室也能進 Top 10","body":"Both /model and /software return 404. The single modelling claim is an undocumented circuit-level simulation with no parameters, equations or tooling named. GCGS still reached the High School Top 10 on the strength of a clean two-cycle DBTL and its Best New Improved Part. Read it as the honest floor: the dry lab is not what gets you into the top ten — it is what gets you a prize.","body_zh":"/model 與 /software 都回傳 404。唯一的建模主張是一個沒有記載參數、方程式或工具名稱的電路層級模擬。GCGS 仍然憑著乾淨的兩輪 DBTL 與最佳改良基因元件獎進入高中組 Top 10。請把它讀成誠實的底線：乾實驗室不是讓你擠進前十名的東西——它是讓你拿到獎項的東西。","chips":["no model page","still Top 10"],"kicker_zh":"地板"},{"kicker":"The pattern","title":"Three cheap controls that separate real from leaky","title_zh":"三個便宜的對照，分開真實與外洩","body":"From Eton-College-UK, and transferable to any student machine-learning project: cluster near-duplicate sequences by Hamming distance and split whole clusters across folds, so the model cannot memorise a near-copy; run a label-shuffle control, which must collapse to chance; run an ablation that strips the information you claim to be using. None of these needs a GPU. Together they turn a high-school classifier into something a reviewer can believe.","body_zh":"來自 Eton-College-UK，可移植到任何學生的機器學習專案：以 Hamming 距離把近似重複的序列分群，並把整群分到同一個 fold，讓模型無法記住近似副本；跑標籤洗牌對照，其表現必須塌回隨機水準；跑一個消融測試，剝除你宣稱正在使用的那項資訊。這些都不需要 GPU。合起來，它們能把一個高中生的分類器變成審閱者願意相信的東西。","chips":["cluster-aware CV","label shuffle","ablation"],"kicker_zh":"共同型態"},{"kicker":"The pattern","title":"Split before you fit","title_zh":"先切分，再擬合","body":"HongKong-JSS divided its runs into calibration and validation before fitting anything, subtracted a matched control from the same run and timepoint, inverted the fit to predict unknowns, and reported RMSE on the held-out runs with the failures left in — then published a list of the statistics they had not yet done. That last habit is rarer and more valuable than the first.","body_zh":"HongKong-JSS 在擬合任何東西之前就把實驗批次分成校正組與驗證組，扣除同一批次、同一時間點的對照，反解擬合式來預測未知樣本，並在保留批次上報告 RMSE、把失敗的資料留在裡面——接著公布了一份他們還沒做的統計分析清單。最後這個習慣比第一個更罕見，也更有價值。","chips":["held-out RMSE","published what is not yet done"],"kicker_zh":"共同型態"},{"kicker":"The pattern","title":"Publish the prediction that lost","title_zh":"公開那個輸掉的預測","body":"HangzhouFourteenAP's FoldX pipeline ranked Y166Q first; the bench preferred Q172P. Rather than bury it, the wiki revises its own ranking, demotes the failed candidate to a mechanistic probe, and uses BCA normalisation to rule out protein load as the confound. Lambert-GA did the same at a larger scale by showing its own hit was not the top-scoring design. A dry lab earns more credibility from one well-controlled loss than from three unexamined wins.","body_zh":"HangzhouFourteenAP 的 FoldX 流程把 Y166Q 排第一，實驗卻偏好 Q172P。他們沒有把它埋掉，而是在 wiki 上修正自己的排序，把失敗的候選降級為機制探針，並以 BCA 標準化排除「蛋白質上樣量」這個干擾因子。Lambert-GA 在更大的尺度上做了同樣的事：證明自己成功的那個設計並不是分數最高的。一個乾實驗室從一次控制良好的失敗中得到的可信度，大於三次未經檢驗的成功。","chips":["FoldX said Y166Q","the bench said Q172P"],"kicker_zh":"共同型態"},{"kicker":"For GEMS","title":"The gap is one term of teaching, not a budget line","title_zh":"差距是一個學期的教學，不是一筆預算","body":"Every practice above — cluster-aware splits, label-shuffle controls, calibration/validation separation, provenance tagging, publishing the loss — costs nothing but attention and can be taught in a term. The tools the 2026 high-school field actually used are free: NetLogo, NUPACK, PyMOL, FoldX, scikit-learn, ImageJ, Chimera, the AlphaFold server. GEMS does not need to buy its way to the ceiling. It needs to make evaluation discipline the house style.","body_zh":"上述每一項做法——分群感知的資料切分、標籤洗牌對照、校正與驗證分離、來源標註、公開失敗——都不花錢，只花注意力，而且一個學期就能教完。2026 年高中組實際用到的工具都是免費的：NetLogo、NUPACK、PyMOL、FoldX、scikit-learn、ImageJ、Chimera、AlphaFold server。GEMS 不需要靠花錢爬上天花板，它需要的是把評估紀律變成自己的風格。","chips":["all free tools","one term"],"kicker_zh":"給 GEMS"}],"table":{"head":["Team","Headline dry-lab work","Main tools","The discipline that stands out"],"head_zh":["團隊","乾實驗室重點工作","主要工具","最突出的紀律"],"rows":[["Lambert-GA","Four linked models: de novo minibinder design, oral PK, 13-ODE RNAi network, colony epidemiology","BindCraft, Boltz-2, Protenix, Mosaic","Benchmarked the confidence metrics themselves and published that its own hit was not top-scoring"],["Eton-College-UK","Seven-protease substrate predictor on 10,472 cleavage windows","scikit-learn, PSSM, BLOSUM62, VHSE","Hamming-cluster-aware cross-validation, label-shuffle and ablation controls"],["GEMS-Taiwan","Crop-stress index fitted to 25 years of county rice yields; optogenetic circuit; anomaly detection","Python, autoencoder, Kalman filter, ERA5, QGIS, AlphaFold","A pre-registered forecast scored after the fact, and a published disagreement between its own runs"],["GHCIS","Toehold design pipeline, plus ARGUS, a deployable colour-classification platform","NUPACK 4.1.0.1, Node.js, Docker, SQLite","Algorithm specified to the threshold, with an explicit 'unresolved' state"],["HongKong-JSS","Calibration and inverse prediction for an in-field mercury assay","ImageJ, log-linear calibration, Onshape, ESP32","Calibration/validation split before fitting; RMSE on held-out runs with failures left in"],["HKSSC","Structure-guided mutagenesis and enzyme kinetics for a paraben-degrading esterase","AlphaFold, UCSF Chimera, HotSpot Wizard, CB-Dock2","Invented a justified mass-normalised metric rather than report an invalid kcat/Km"],["HFI","Agent-based contact model and a 13-variable ODE system, both as wet-lab gatekeepers","NetLogo 3D, Runge-Kutta, interactive HTML front-ends","Screened seven RBS parts computationally before a single plasmid was built"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","Mutation prioritisation pipeline for CoGH66","PyMOL, FoldX, MAFFT, AlphaFold Server","Reported the computational prediction the bench overturned, with the confound controlled"],["HongKong-HS","Toehold switch thermodynamics for a urinary miRNA screening kit","NUPACK, miRADAR (Wageningen iGEM 2024)","Reused another team's released tool instead of rebuilding it"],["GCGS","No model or software page exists","—","The control case: Top 10 without a dry lab, but no modelling prize"]],"rows_zh":[["Lambert-GA","四個連動模型：de novo minibinder 設計、口服藥物動力學、13 條 ODE 的 RNAi 網路、族群流行病學","BindCraft, Boltz-2, Protenix, Mosaic","對信心指標本身做基準測試，並公開自己成功的設計其實不是分數最高的"],["Eton-College-UK","在 10,472 個切割視窗上建立七種蛋白酶的受質預測器","scikit-learn, PSSM, BLOSUM62, VHSE","以 Hamming 距離分群的交叉驗證，加上標籤洗牌與消融對照"],["GEMS-Taiwan","以 25 年各縣市稻作產量擬合的作物逆境指數；光遺傳電路；異常偵測","Python, autoencoder, Kalman filter, ERA5, QGIS, AlphaFold","一個事後評分的預先登記預測，以及公開自己兩次實驗之間的矛盾"],["GHCIS","Toehold 設計流程，外加可部署的顏色判讀平台 ARGUS","NUPACK 4.1.0.1, Node.js, Docker, SQLite","演算法明確寫到閾值，並設有明確的「無法判定」狀態"],["HongKong-JSS","現場汞檢測的校正與反解預測","ImageJ, 對數線性校正, Onshape, ESP32","擬合前先切分校正組與驗證組；在保留批次上報告 RMSE 並保留失敗資料"],["HKSSC","對羥苯甲酸酯分解酯酶的結構導向突變與酵素動力學","AlphaFold, UCSF Chimera, HotSpot Wizard, CB-Dock2","沒有報告無效的 kcat/Km，而是提出並論證一個質量標準化指標"],["HFI","代理人基礎接觸模型與 13 變數 ODE 系統，兩者都作為濕實驗的守門員","NetLogo 3D, Runge-Kutta, 互動式 HTML 前端","在建出任何一個質體之前，先以運算篩選七個 RBS 元件"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","CoGH66 的突變優先排序流程","PyMOL, FoldX, MAFFT, AlphaFold Server","公開那個被實驗推翻的運算預測，並控制了干擾因子"],["HongKong-HS","尿液 miRNA 篩檢套組的 toehold switch 熱力學","NUPACK, miRADAR（Wageningen iGEM 2024）","沿用別隊已釋出的工具，而不是重做一個"],["GCGS","沒有 model 頁，也沒有 software 頁","—","對照組：沒有乾實驗室也能進 Top 10，但拿不到建模類獎項"]]},"method":"Drawn from the ten High School Top 10 team files in this report, each researched from the team's own 2026 wiki. Tool lists are what each team names; a team may have used more than it wrote down. The judgement about what 'stands out' is ours, and a reader who disagrees should open the team file and the wiki behind it — both are linked. GEMS-Taiwan is the report author's own team and has been assessed on the same terms as the rest.","method_zh":"資料來自本報告中高中組 Top 10 的十份團隊檔案，每一份都取自該隊自己的 2026 wiki。工具清單是各隊自己寫出來的；團隊實際用到的可能多於其所記載。關於「什麼最突出」的判斷出自我們，不同意的讀者可以直接打開團隊檔案與其背後的 wiki——兩者都有連結。GEMS-Taiwan 是本報告作者自己的團隊，評判標準與其他隊伍相同。","kicker_zh":"原創分析","order":32},{"id":"wiki-craft","tab":"teams","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"What the Best Wiki winners did differently","title_zh":"最佳 Wiki 得獎隊伍做了哪些不一樣的事","lede":"The four 2026 Best Wiki winners did not win on visual polish or page weight; they won by building an executive layer that tells a judge where the evidence is, and then by being unusually specific and unusually honest underneath it.","lede_zh":"2026 年四組最佳 Wiki 得獎隊伍並不是靠視覺精緻度或頁面重量取勝；他們靠的是建立一層明確的摘要層，直接告訴評審證據在哪裡，然後在這層底下做到異常具體、異常誠實。","body":"Three of the four winners ship pages whose text exists in the HTML before any JavaScript runs: **Heidelberg** writes static HTML by hand, **Uni-Padua-IT** prerenders SvelteKit, **Lambert-GA** builds with Astro. TU Delft is the exception, a Vite single-page app behind a 3.4 MB bundle, and it compensates deliberately with an `llms.txt` at the wiki root and a plain-Markdown mirror of every page at `/tu-delft/<page>.md`. Against that, the control group — Princeton, Cornell, LYON, UAlberta, UCNZ, Athens, GU Frankfurt and Eton-College-UK, all winners of serious 2026 science prizes — serves near-empty shells of 486 bytes to 15 kB, as little as seven characters of text without JS.\n\nThe real differentiator is an explicit executive layer. Uni-Padua-IT and Lambert-GA both ship a `/judging` page that walks medal criterion by criterion, summarises each in two or three sentences and deep-links the evidence — Padua pointing straight at its own negative results, Lambert stating in the summary that fifteen minibinder designs produced no confirmed hits before a second campaign of twenty produced one binder at roughly 604 nM. TU Delft reaches the same place with an illustrated module map on Results where hovering highlights a module and clicking jumps to it, over the same five modules that organise the project; Heidelberg puts three summary cards above the fold and gives every nav link a one-line subtitle, so \"Results\" reads \"Where data tells the story\".\n\nUnderneath, the winners are simply more specific. **Heidelberg**'s captions carry panel letters, 547 ng and 433 ng transfection masses, 18,000 × g, and an effect size quoted with its range — 5.6×, 4.3 to 6.4× depending on the haze setting — while Padua photographs the plate that grew nothing, numbers it as a figure, and explains why an earlier transformation failed. **TU Delft** built a content system rather than a set of pages: 1,604 reference tags over 735 unique DOIs, 724 glossary calls against 102 definitions, 307 auto-numbered figures, and one unvarying Background → Results → Discussion → Future Perspective spine. Its decision matrix tags every cell as Factual, Inferred, Estimated or Speculative, with a legend saying the tag records the strength of the evidence behind the cell rather than the judgement — epistemic honesty rendered as a UI component, and I saw nothing like it elsewhere.\n\nWhat did not decide it is as instructive. Page weight spans two orders of magnitude inside the winners' circle, from Lambert-GA's 78 kB homepage to TU Delft's 3.4 MB. None of Heidelberg, Uni-Padua, Lambert-GA, Stanford, UCAS-China or Toronto declares a `prefers-color-scheme` rule, and meaningful alt text ran at 27 to 48 per cent across the winners while HongKong-JSS, ProFuture-China and WageningenUR hit 90, 86 and 81 per cent and won nothing for it. The winners do all honour `prefers-reduced-motion` — thirteen blocks in Heidelberg's stylesheet, eleven in TU Delft's bundle — and Heidelberg goes further, sniffing for a software WebGL renderer and dropping to a lite mode automatically, with `?lite=0` and `?perf=1` for anyone who wants to look: the motion budget goes to figure interactions and graceful degradation, not to hero spectacle.","body_zh":"四組得獎隊伍中有三組，頁面文字在任何 JavaScript 執行之前就已經存在於 HTML 裡：**Heidelberg** 手寫靜態 HTML，**Uni-Padua-IT** 以 SvelteKit 預先渲染，**Lambert-GA** 用 Astro 建置。TU Delft 是例外，它是一個 3.4 MB bundle 的 Vite 單頁應用，而它刻意用 wiki 根目錄的 `llms.txt`，以及每一頁在 `/tu-delft/<page>.md` 的純 Markdown 鏡像來補償。相對地，對照組——Princeton、Cornell、LYON、UAlberta、UCNZ、Athens、GU Frankfurt 和 Eton-College-UK，全都是 2026 年重量級科學獎項的得主——送出的是 486 位元組到 15 kB 的近乎空殼，在沒有 JS 的情況下最少只有七個字元的文字。\n\n真正的分水嶺是一層明確的摘要層。Uni-Padua-IT 和 Lambert-GA 都提供 `/judging` 頁面，逐條走過每一項獎牌標準，每一項用兩三句話摘要，並深層連結到證據——Padua 直接指向自己的負面結果，Lambert 在摘要裡寫明十五個 minibinder 設計沒有產生任何確認的命中，第二輪二十個設計才做出一個親和力約 604 nM 的 binder。TU Delft 以另一種方式到達同一處：Results 頁上一張插圖式的模組地圖，滑鼠移過會凸顯某個模組，點擊則跳到該模組，涵蓋的正是組織整個專案的那五個模組；Heidelberg 把三張摘要卡放在首屏之上，並給每個導覽連結一行副標，於是「Results」讀起來是「Where data tells the story」。\n\n再往下看，得獎隊伍就只是更具體。**Heidelberg** 的圖說帶有分圖編號、547 ng 與 433 ng 的轉染量、18,000 × g，以及附上範圍的效應量——5.6 倍，依 haze 設定落在 4.3 到 6.4 倍之間——而 Padua 把什麼都沒長出來的培養盤拍下來、編上圖號，並解釋早先一次轉形為何失敗。**TU Delft** 建的是一套內容系統，而不是一疊頁面：1,604 個引用標記對應 735 個不重複的 DOI、724 次詞彙表呼叫對應 102 條定義、307 張自動編號的圖，以及一條從不變動的 Background → Results → Discussion → Future Perspective 骨幹。它的決策矩陣為每一格標上 Factual、Inferred、Estimated 或 Speculative，圖例並說明這個標記記錄的是該格背後證據的強度，而不是判斷本身——把知識論上的誠實做成一個介面元件，這種作法我在別處沒有看到。\n\n沒有決定勝負的因素同樣值得一看。得獎圈內的頁面重量橫跨兩個數量級，從 Lambert-GA 78 kB 的首頁到 TU Delft 的 3.4 MB。Heidelberg、Uni-Padua、Lambert-GA、Stanford、UCAS-China 和 Toronto 都沒有宣告任何 `prefers-color-scheme` 規則；有意義的替代文字在得獎隊伍之間只有 27% 到 48%，而 HongKong-JSS、ProFuture-China 和 WageningenUR 分別達到 90%、86% 和 81%，卻沒有因此得到任何獎。得獎隊伍確實全都尊重 `prefers-reduced-motion`——Heidelberg 的樣式表裡有十三段，TU Delft 的 bundle 裡有十一段——而 Heidelberg 走得更遠，它會偵測軟體 WebGL 轉譯器並自動降為輕量模式，還留了 `?lite=0` 和 `?perf=1` 給想細看的人：動態效果的預算花在圖表互動和優雅降級上，而不是首頁的視覺奇觀。","cards":[{"kicker":"Information architecture","title":"Build a judging page and make it the front door","title_zh":"做一個 judging 頁面，並讓它成為正門","body":"Uni-Padua-IT and Lambert-GA each ship a `/judging` route that indexes every medal criterion and every award they apply for. Each entry is two or three sentences of plain summary followed by a deep link into the page that holds the evidence. Padua links directly to its own failed Design-Build-Test-Learn cycles under Silver; Lambert quotes the binding affinity and the two failed design campaigns in the Gold section. It costs one page and it converts a pile of required sections into a reading order.","body_zh":"Uni-Padua-IT 和 Lambert-GA 各自提供一個 `/judging` 路徑，索引每一條獎牌標準和每一個申請的獎項。每一則是兩三句樸素的摘要，後面接一個深層連結，直通存放證據的頁面。Padua 在銀牌項下直接連到自己失敗的 Design-Build-Test-Learn 循環；Lambert 在金牌段落引用結合親和力和兩次失敗的設計輪次。代價是一頁，換來的是把一堆規定章節轉成一條閱讀動線。","chips":["Uni-Padua-IT","Lambert-GA","2 clicks to evidence","One page"],"kicker_zh":"資訊架構"},{"kicker":"Data presentation","title":"Label the provenance of every number you did not measure","title_zh":"為每一個不是你量出來的數字標註來源","body":"TU Delft's entrepreneurship page scores four candidate applications against eleven weighted parameters. Every single cell carries a bracketed tag — [F]actual, [I]nferred, [E]stimated or [S]peculative — and the legend states that the tag records how strong the evidence behind the cell is, not the score, because every score is a judgement applied to sourced facts. The weights sum to 100 per cent and the weighted total is given to two decimals. It is the single most copyable device I found in 2026.","body_zh":"TU Delft 的創業頁面用十一個加權參數為四個候選應用評分。每一格都帶一個方括號標記——[F]actual、[I]nferred、[E]stimated 或 [S]peculative——圖例說明這個標記記錄的是該格背後證據有多強，而不是分數本身，因為每個分數都是對有來源的事實所做的判斷。權重加總為 100%，加權總分給到小數第二位。這是我在 2026 年找到最值得照抄的一項設計。","chips":["TU Delft","F / I / E / S","Weighted matrix","Shows its working"],"kicker_zh":"資料呈現"},{"kicker":"Human practices","title":"Date every pivot and name who caused it","title_zh":"為每一次轉向標上日期，並指名是誰造成的","body":"Lambert-GA applies one named framework, H.I.V.E. — Hear, Inquire, Validate, Evolve — identically to every stakeholder, then closes with a Project Pivots timeline. Five entries, each with a date, the named expert whose feedback caused it, and a literal before-and-after: nanobody changed to minibinder, P-domain in general changed to specific hotspots. The caption says every change shown came directly from stakeholder feedback rather than internal decisions. It makes integration auditable instead of asserted.","body_zh":"Lambert-GA 對每一位利害關係人都套用同一個具名框架 H.I.V.E.——Hear、Inquire、Validate、Evolve——最後以一條 Project Pivots 時間軸收尾。五則記錄，每一則都有日期、意見造成這次轉向的具名專家，以及字面上的前後對照：nanobody 改成 minibinder，整個 P-domain 改成特定的熱點。圖說寫明所列的每一項改變都直接來自利害關係人的意見，而不是團隊內部的決定。這讓整合變成可查核的，而不是宣稱的。","chips":["Lambert-GA","H.I.V.E.","Dated timeline","Before → after"],"kicker_zh":"人類實踐"},{"kicker":"Technical build","title":"Mirror the wiki as plain Markdown","title_zh":"把 wiki 鏡像成純 Markdown","body":"TU Delft's wiki is a Vite single-page app and the heaviest I measured, yet it publishes an `llms.txt` at the wiki root listing twelve pages, each mirrored as plain Markdown at `/tu-delft/<page>.md`. That gives a JS-free fallback, a machine-readable corpus, and a diffable source of truth for the content, all from one build step. If you insist on a client-rendered framework, this is the tax you should pay for it.","body_zh":"TU Delft 的 wiki 是 Vite 單頁應用，也是我量過最重的一個，但它在 wiki 根目錄發布 `llms.txt`，列出十二個頁面，每一頁都在 `/tu-delft/<page>.md` 鏡像成純 Markdown。這一個建置步驟同時換來不需要 JS 的替代方案、一份機器可讀的語料，以及一份可以做 diff 的內容真實來源。如果你堅持要用客戶端渲染的框架，這就是你該付的稅。","chips":["TU Delft","llms.txt","/page.md","JS-free fallback"],"kicker_zh":"技術實作"},{"kicker":"Figures","title":"Write captions that stand alone, and number the negative control","title_zh":"寫能獨立成立的圖說，並為陰性對照編上圖號","body":"Heidelberg's captions carry panel letters, exact reagent masses, exact centrifugation and pressure conditions, and effect sizes quoted with a range across settings — a reader can take the figure out of the page and still understand it. Uni-Padua-IT goes one better on controls: the plate that grew nothing gets its own numbered figure with the full condition in the caption, sitting beside the plate that grew two colonies. Showing the control is cheap and it is the fastest way to look like you know what you are doing.","body_zh":"Heidelberg 的圖說帶有分圖編號、確切的試劑用量、確切的離心與壓力條件，以及跨設定給出範圍的效應量——讀者把圖從頁面裡拿出來也看得懂。Uni-Padua-IT 在對照組上更進一步：什麼都沒長出來的培養盤有自己的圖號，圖說裡寫出完整條件，就放在長出兩個菌落的培養盤旁邊。把對照組放出來很便宜，而且這是讓人看起來知道自己在做什麼的最快方法。","chips":["Heidelberg","Uni-Padua-IT","Units + n + conditions","Show the control"],"kicker_zh":"圖表"},{"kicker":"Build discipline","title":"Keep content out of components","title_zh":"別把內容寫進元件裡","body":"Stanford University — Grand Prize winner and a Best Wiki nominee, though not a winner — stores each page as a single hand-written JavaScript object with a documented block grammar of p, sh, gal, list, table, steps, math and quotes, plus a per-page accent colour and icon. TU Delft does the equivalent in MDX with a fixed component vocabulary. Either way the layout is written once and the copy is written by people who are not touching layout, which is why neither wiki drifts between pages.","body_zh":"Stanford University——總冠軍得主，也是最佳 Wiki 入圍者，但沒有得獎——把每一頁存成一個手寫的 JavaScript 物件，配上一套文件化的區塊語法：p、sh、gal、list、table、steps、math 和 quotes，再加上每頁自己的強調色與圖示。TU Delft 則用 MDX 搭配固定的元件詞彙做到同一件事。不論哪一種，版面只寫一次，文字由不碰版面的人來寫，這就是這兩個 wiki 不會在頁與頁之間走樣的原因。","chips":["Stanford University","TU Delft","One file per page","Block grammar"],"kicker_zh":"建置紀律"},{"kicker":"Craft","title":"Degrade on purpose, not by accident","title_zh":"刻意降級，而不是意外降級","body":"Heidelberg's wiki detects a software WebGL renderer on load and automatically switches to a lite mode, with `?lite=0` and `?lite=1` to force it either way and `?perf=1` to load a performance reporter. Its stylesheet carries thirteen `prefers-reduced-motion` blocks; TU Delft's bundle carries eleven. The winners treat a judge on a tired laptop as a real user. Nobody built a dark mode, and nobody needed one.","body_zh":"Heidelberg 的 wiki 在載入時偵測軟體 WebGL 轉譯器，並自動切換到輕量模式，另有 `?lite=0` 和 `?lite=1` 可以強制切換，`?perf=1` 則載入效能回報器。它的樣式表裡有十三段 `prefers-reduced-motion`；TU Delft 的 bundle 裡有十一段。得獎隊伍把用著一台老舊筆電的評審當成真實使用者。沒有人做深色模式，也沒有人需要。","chips":["Heidelberg","?lite=1","prefers-reduced-motion","Hardware sniffing"],"kicker_zh":"工藝"}],"table":{"head":["Wiki","Section","Framework / build","The one thing it does best"],"head_zh":["Wiki","組別","框架／建置","它做得最好的一件事"],"rows":[["Heidelberg","Undergrad — winner","Hand-written static HTML, Bootstrap plus a 77 kB token layer; ~1 MB of HTML, CSS and JS","Journal-grade figure captions, and an automatic lite mode for weak GPUs"],["Uni-Padua-IT","Undergrad — winner","SvelteKit, prerendered; 266 kB across 17 code-split files","A /judging page that links each medal criterion straight at the evidence, failures included"],["TU Delft","Overgrad — winner","Vite SPA, one 3.4 MB bundle, 16 flat routes; MDX content with a fixed component vocabulary","Per-cell evidence-provenance labels, plus every page mirrored as Markdown behind llms.txt"],["Lambert-GA","High School — winner","Astro, fully static; 78 kB of HTML, CSS and JS on the homepage","A dated pivot timeline that attributes each project change to a named stakeholder"],["Stanford University","Undergrad — nominee","Client-rendered template app; 15 hand-written content files with a documented block grammar","Content fully separated from layout, so nothing drifts between pages"],["UCAS-China","Undergrad — nominee","Static HTML, 18 pages including a /medal index","An odometer-style opening statistic that lands the problem in one screen"]],"rows_zh":[["Heidelberg","大學組——得獎","手寫靜態 HTML，Bootstrap 加一層 77 kB 的 token 層；HTML、CSS 與 JS 合計約 1 MB","期刊級的圖說，以及針對弱 GPU 的自動輕量模式"],["Uni-Padua-IT","大學組——得獎","SvelteKit，預先渲染；17 個程式碼分割檔案共 266 kB","/judging 頁面把每一條獎牌標準直接連到證據，失敗的部分也包含在內"],["TU Delft","研究生組——得獎","Vite 單頁應用，單一 3.4 MB bundle，16 條扁平路由；MDX 內容搭配固定的元件詞彙","逐格標註證據來源，並把每一頁鏡像成 Markdown 放在 llms.txt 後面"],["Lambert-GA","高中組——得獎","Astro，完全靜態；首頁的 HTML、CSS 與 JS 合計 78 kB","一條標了日期的轉向時間軸，把每次專案變更歸因到具名的利害關係人"],["Stanford University","大學組——入圍","客戶端渲染的樣板應用；15 個手寫內容檔，搭配文件化的區塊語法","內容與版面完全分離，所以頁與頁之間不會走樣"],["UCAS-China","大學組——入圍","靜態 HTML，18 個頁面，含一個 /medal 索引","里程表式的開場統計數字，一個畫面就把問題講清楚"]]},"checklist":["Ship HTML that already contains your words — prerender, or mirror every page as Markdown with an llms.txt, as TU Delft did.","Build a /judging page that answers each medal criterion in two or three sentences and deep-links the evidence.","State the controlling question on the first screen and repeat it in the same words on every summary layer.","Put a three-card or five-module summary above the detail on every long page, before any subsection.","Fix one spine for every results subsection — Background, Results, Discussion, Future Perspective — and never vary it.","Write captions that stand alone: panel letters, exact conditions, units, n, and the effect size with its range.","Photograph the negative control and give it a figure number of its own.","Name your failures with numbers, and name them in the executive layer rather than burying them.","Tag the provenance of every number you did not measure yourself — factual, inferred, estimated or speculative.","Keep content in one data file per page with a documented block grammar; let layout be written once.","Date every human-practices pivot, name the person whose feedback caused it, and show before and after.","Honour prefers-reduced-motion and spend the motion budget on figure interactions, not on the hero."],"checklist_zh":["送出已經包含你文字的 HTML——預先渲染，或像 TU Delft 那樣把每一頁鏡像成 Markdown 並配上 llms.txt。","做一個 /judging 頁面，用兩三句話回答每一條獎牌標準，並深層連結到證據。","在第一個畫面就寫出主導問題，並在每一層摘要用一模一樣的字重複它。","在每一個長頁面的細節之前，放上三張卡片或五個模組的摘要，排在任何子章節之前。","為每一個結果子章節固定同一條骨幹——Background、Results、Discussion、Future Perspective——而且絕不變動。","寫能獨立成立的圖說：分圖編號、確切條件、單位、n，以及附上範圍的效應量。","把陰性對照拍下來，並給它自己的圖號。","用數字說出你的失敗，而且要說在摘要層裡，不要埋起來。","為每一個不是你自己量出來的數字標註來源——事實、推論、估計或推測。","把內容放在每頁一個資料檔裡，搭配文件化的區塊語法；版面只寫一次。","為每一次人類實踐的轉向標上日期、指名是誰的意見造成的，並呈現前後對照。","尊重 prefers-reduced-motion，把動態效果的預算花在圖表互動上，而不是首頁主視覺。"],"antipatterns":["Dark mode and theme toggles. Not one of Heidelberg, Uni-Padua-IT, Lambert-GA, Stanford, UCAS-China or Toronto declares a prefers-color-scheme rule, and all of them placed well.","A late alt-text compliance sweep. The four winners ran 27 to 48 per cent meaningful alt text while HongKong-JSS (90 per cent), ProFuture-China (86) and WageningenUR (81) all beat them and none was a Best Wiki winner — it is a floor, not a differentiator, so do it early and cheaply.","Huge homepage media galleries. Toronto pulls 214 images and 252 .avif references on the homepage alone and ETH-Zurich serves a single 1.9 MB HTML page; neither won Best Wiki.","A client-rendered SPA with no text fallback. This is the default in the control group — Princeton, Cornell, LYON, UAlberta, UCNZ, Athens, GU Frankfurt and Eton-College-UK all serve near-empty shells despite winning major science prizes.","Per-page mascots, bespoke icon sets and per-page accent colours. Stanford invested in all three and placed as a nominee; none of the four winners has a mascot system.","Treating the mandatory section list as the information architecture. A deep-linked judging index does the same job in one page and reads as an argument rather than a form."],"antipatterns_zh":["深色模式與主題切換。Heidelberg、Uni-Padua-IT、Lambert-GA、Stanford、UCAS-China 和 Toronto 沒有一個宣告 prefers-color-scheme 規則，而他們的名次全都不錯。","最後才做一輪替代文字合規清查。四組得獎隊伍有意義的替代文字只有 27% 到 48%，而 HongKong-JSS（90%）、ProFuture-China（86%）和 WageningenUR（81%）都勝過他們，卻沒有一個是最佳 Wiki 得主——這是底線，不是差異點，所以早做、便宜做就好。","首頁放巨大的媒體圖庫。Toronto 光首頁就拉了 214 張圖和 252 個 .avif 參照，ETH-Zurich 送出單一 1.9 MB 的 HTML 頁面；兩者都沒有拿到最佳 Wiki。","客戶端渲染的單頁應用，而且沒有任何文字替代方案。這是對照組的預設做法——Princeton、Cornell、LYON、UAlberta、UCNZ、Athens、GU Frankfurt 和 Eton-College-UK 全都送出近乎空殼的頁面，儘管他們都拿下了重要的科學獎項。","每頁一隻吉祥物、客製圖示組和每頁不同的強調色。Stanford 三者都投資了，結果只是入圍；四組得獎隊伍沒有一個有吉祥物系統。","把規定的章節清單當成資訊架構。一個深層連結的 judging 索引用一頁就做到同一件事，而且讀起來像論證，不像表格。"],"method":"I rendered and read the four winners in full — Heidelberg, Uni-Padua-IT, TU Delft and Lambert-GA — by fetching their page HTML directly where it is server-rendered, by reading TU Delft's Markdown mirrors, and by loading the client-rendered pages in a browser; counts of references, figures, components, image formats, alt attributes and prefers-reduced-motion rules were taken from the shipped source. I sampled around thirty nominees and controls more shallowly, measuring framework, rendered text length, asset weight and alt-text coverage for all of them, and reading Stanford's and UCAS-China's content in detail as the closest nominees. I could not render several Vite single-page nominees deeply — Oxford, UCSC, NUS-Singapore, KAUST-KSA, Muenster-University, IISER-Kolkata and UOttawa among them — because a shared browser pane kept being navigated away mid-session, so they are excluded from the table and their design is not characterised here; I also did not measure real-world load time, mobile layout or screen-reader behaviour beyond the markup.","method_zh":"我完整渲染並讀過四組得獎隊伍——Heidelberg、Uni-Padua-IT、TU Delft 和 Lambert-GA：伺服器端渲染的部分直接抓取頁面 HTML，TU Delft 的部分讀它的 Markdown 鏡像，客戶端渲染的頁面則在瀏覽器中載入；引用、圖、元件、影像格式、alt 屬性和 prefers-reduced-motion 規則的數量，都取自實際送出的原始碼。我以較淺的方式抽樣約三十組入圍隊伍與對照隊伍，為全部這些隊伍量測框架、渲染後文字長度、資產重量和替代文字覆蓋率，並把 Stanford 與 UCAS-China 的內容當成最接近的入圍者細讀。有幾組 Vite 單頁應用的入圍隊伍我無法深入渲染——包括 Oxford、UCSC、NUS-Singapore、KAUST-KSA、Muenster-University、IISER-Kolkata 和 UOttawa——因為共用的瀏覽器面板在過程中一直被導向其他頁面，所以它們不列入表格，本文也不描述它們的設計；此外，除了標記語言本身之外，我沒有量測真實的載入時間、行動版版面或螢幕閱讀器行為。","kicker_zh":"原創分析","order":32},{"id":"collaboration-network","tab":"teams","order":34,"kicker":"Original analysis","kicker_zh":"原創分析","title":"Who worked with whom in 2026","title_zh":"2026 年誰和誰合作","lede":"Sixty-nine of the 106 decorated teams record working with at least one other iGEM team; thirty-seven record none. Almost all of it is meet-ups. Not one team in the cohort ran an inter-lab measurement ring, and the team that offered to run the nearest thing got no replies. GEMS-Taiwan has no collaboration page and appears on nobody else's — and still took Top 10 and three wins, which is the uncomfortable part.","lede_zh":"106 支得獎隊伍中有 69 支記錄了與至少一支其他 iGEM 隊伍的合作，37 支完全沒有。這些合作幾乎都是聚會。整個群體裡沒有任何一支隊伍跑過跨實驗室的量測環（inter-lab measurement ring），而唯一提出最接近做法的隊伍，一封回覆都沒收到。GEMS-Taiwan 沒有合作頁面，也沒出現在任何其他隊伍的頁面上——卻仍然拿下 Top 10 與三項大獎，而這正是尷尬的地方。","body":"Across the 106 researched team files, **69 teams document working with at least one other iGEM team and 37 document none**. The forms are not equally weighted. The dominant one by a wide margin is the **regional meet-up**: BFH's European Meet-Up in Hamburg on 15–17 May (third edition, co-run by Bielefeld, Frankfurt and Hamburg), KIT's first iGEM Baden-Württemberg Meetup on 13 June with eight German teams, HUST-China's First Central-China iGEM Forum on 12 July with fifteen teams, Uni-Padua-IT's Italian Meet-Up in the Botanical Garden of Padua on 25 July with Bologna and Milan, NYCU-Taiwan's Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up on 27 July, Labi-Taiwan's TGEM at National Taiwan University on 22 August, Grand APiC at SUSTech and the University of Hong Kong on 16–19 August, ETH-Zurich's Swiss iGEM Meetup for five teams, Baltimore's Mid-Atlantic Meetup with nine regional teams, TAU-Israel's online Mini-Jamboree with eight. Below that sit mentorship of school teams by university teams, co-authored community publications, peer review, and a long tail of poster boards and podcast guest slots.\n\nSort them by whether a third party can use the output and the list gets short. **What survives contact with a stranger**: JLU-FBH's myth-busting handbook *Together with iGEM: Across Villages, From Myths to Facts*, chief-edited across submissions from 17-plus teams; HBUT-China's five-school joint biosafety manual for anti-tumour projects, written with ZJU-China, BNU-China, JLU-FBH and ZJUT-China and released as a downloadable PDF with deliberately differentiable risk protocols because the five teams use different carriers; SJTU-BioX-Shanghai's cross-team Education Activity Handbook, where they took responsibility for Part 7; the MSP Vector peer-reviewed iGEM journal run from Maastricht, where Madrid-UCM refereed three other teams' papers and Stockholm contributed a literature review and reviewed in turn; McGill's BIOME Book, to which NYCU-Taiwan supplied the text and concept for an LbCas12a entry and McGill supplied the artwork; and KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei and HKSSC splitting the central dogma between them into two physical teaching models over two planning calls on 20 August and 19 September, sharing prototypes through a common Drive, then each adapting to its own audience — KCIS rebuilding HKSSC's flat felt translation framework as a 3D tactile box with slotted E, P and A sites for seven students at the Taipei School for the Visually Impaired. **What does not**: icebreakers, rock stacking, beanbag toss, community blackboards, 'we met other teams and exchanged ideas'. NYCU-Taiwan says the quiet part itself on its own wiki: documenting an event does not by itself demonstrate its long-term impact.\n\nThe biggest hole in 2026 is technical. **Not one of the 106 teams ran an inter-lab measurement ring** — the same construct or sample measured by several teams on several instruments, with the between-lab spread published. The closest anyone came was negative. Uni-Padua-IT, who went on to win Best Software Tool and Best Wiki in the Undergraduate section, wrote on their software page: *\"On 9 August 2026 we published an open call for collaboration to validate the software and shared it in the two ways that actually reach people: on our social media channels and directly with other iGEM teams. The offer was simple: tell us your chassis, and we will optimise a sequence for it and send the result back. Unfortunately, we did not receive any replies.\"* The only genuine independent replications in the cohort came from outside iGEM — four mechanical engineering students at Hanyang University rebuilt PSI Korea's reader from the released documentation alone — or across years, where HongKong-HS generated its toehold candidates with miRADAR, the tool Wageningen released in 2024, and Mingdao re-characterised the cenA part lineage (Edinburgh 2008, CAU_China 2019, XMU-China 2019, SYSU-CHINA 2021) at 34 °C in Bis-Tris pH 6.4 instead of the standard 50 °C acidic assay. Live part or sample exchange between two 2026 teams: essentially absent.\n\n**Does it correlate with placing? Honestly, no.** Coding the 106 files three ways — substantive co-production (S, n = 48), attendance or visibility only (A, n = 21), nothing documented (N, n = 37) — gives Top 10 rates of 14/48 (29%), 10/21 (48%) and 6/37 (16%), and at-least-one-win rates of 29/48 (60%), 10/21 (48%) and 15/37 (41%). The hypothesis that substantive beats attendance runs the wrong way and is not significant (Fisher exact p = 0.17). The only thing with any signal is the crude contrast — any documented inter-team work, 24/69 Top 10, against none, 6/37 — and that is p = 0.069, suggestive at best, and confounded by the fact that teams who write more win more. The two biggest connectors in the whole network, Bielefeld-CeBiTec, which ran the European Meet-Up and the Community Blackboard that roughly 37 teams passed through, and JLU-FBH, which chief-edited the 17-team handbook, each took a Gold medal and nothing else. **One award does correlate, and it is the one other teams vote for.** Both 2026 iGEMers Prizes went to the most documented community builders in their tier: HUST-China, which hosted a fifteen-team forum and wrote entries into two other teams' publications, and Labi-Taiwan, which runs TGEM. Judges did not reward collaboration in 2026. Peers did.\n\nTaiwan ran **two** national events and GEMS-Taiwan was at neither. NYCU-Taiwan hosted the 2026 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up at Xian-Qi Hall on the Bo-Ai Campus on 27 July: 53 students and advisors, five Taiwanese teams (NYCU-Taiwan, HIA-Taiwan, NCKU-Tainan, VIS, WIST) plus Okinawa joining online, four icebreakers, five roundtable themes, two guest speakers, five fifteen-minute mock presentations, and — the part that matters — an iGEM Team Operations Guide compiled from the roundtable notes plus published preparation SOPs, registration templates and schedules for future organisers. Labi-Taiwan ran the fourth TGEM on 22 August at the Boya Building, National Taiwan University, co-hosted with NTU's Department of Biochemical Science and Technology: a mock competition of five-minute pitches and twenty-minute interrogation by professors, PIs and industry judges. TGEM has run annually since 2023, founded by Kang Chiao International School Linkou, Labi-Taiwan's own predecessor. Its named 2026 participants include NTHU Taiwan, Claremont CA, AEI Prep-Taiwan and KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei. NCKU-Tainan is the busiest Taiwanese partner on record: Mingdao mentorship on 7 March, the NYCU meet-up in July, a full online session with WIST on 17 September covering wet-lab bottlenecks and a dry-lab model comparison, CCU-Taiwan on 19 September, HIA-Taiwan on 20 September, and TAU-Israel's eight-team Mini-Jamboree on 8 October alongside NTHU. **GEMS-Taiwan has no /collaborations page, no /partnership page, and no other iGEM team named anywhere on its wiki.** Its one listed 'partner team' is Geospatial Analysis, an internal sub-team.\n\nA closing warning about the evidence. **Collaboration claims in 2026 are frequently one-sided.** NCKU-Tainan documents mentoring Mingdao in March and a detailed technical session with WIST in September; neither Mingdao's nor WIST's wiki mentions NCKU-Tainan. ASIJ-Tokyo lists KCIS Xiugang among eight partner teams; KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei's collaboration page names only HKSSC. NYCU-Taiwan lists WIST as a meet-up attendee; WIST's pages do not mention the event. Where a claim appears on one wiki and not the other, the collaboration was usually real and the documentation was unilateral — which is itself the lesson. The partner who writes it up gets the credit and the reusable artefact; the partner who does not gets a photograph.","body_zh":"在 106 份隊伍研究檔案中，**69 支隊伍記錄了與至少一支其他 iGEM 隊伍的合作，37 支完全沒有**。但各種形式的份量並不相等。遙遙領先的主流形式是**區域聚會**：BFH 於 5 月 15 至 17 日在 Hamburg 舉辦的 European Meet-Up（第三屆，由 Bielefeld、Frankfurt 與 Hamburg 三隊合辦）、KIT 於 6 月 13 日舉辦的第一屆 iGEM Baden-Württemberg Meetup（八支德國隊伍）、HUST-China 於 7 月 12 日舉辦的第一屆華中 iGEM 論壇（15 支隊伍）、Uni-Padua-IT 於 7 月 25 日在 Botanical Garden of Padua 舉辦的 Italian Meet-Up（與 Bologna、Milan）、NYCU-Taiwan 於 7 月 27 日的 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up、Labi-Taiwan 於 8 月 22 日在台灣大學舉辦的 TGEM、8 月 16 至 19 日在 SUSTech 與香港大學舉行的 Grand APiC、ETH-Zurich 為五支隊伍合辦的 Swiss iGEM Meetup、Baltimore 參加的九隊 Mid-Atlantic Meetup，以及 TAU-Israel 八隊的線上 Mini-Jamboree。再往下才是大學隊伍對中學隊伍的指導、跨隊共同著作、同儕審查，以及一長串海報牆與播客客座。\n\n若以「第三方能不能拿去用」來篩選，清單立刻變短。**能通過陌生人檢驗的**：由 JLU-FBH 擔任主編、彙整 17 支以上隊伍投稿的破除迷思手冊《Together with iGEM: Across Villages, From Myths to Facts》；HBUT-China 與 ZJU-China、BNU-China、JLU-FBH、ZJUT-China 合寫的五校抗腫瘤專案聯合生物安全手冊，以 PDF 公開，並因五隊載體不同而刻意設計成可區分的風險評估流程；SJTU-BioX-Shanghai 參與的跨隊教育活動手冊，他們負責第 7 部分；由 Maastricht 營運的同儕審查期刊 MSP Vector，Madrid-UCM 在其中審了三支隊伍的論文，Stockholm 投了一篇文獻回顧並參與審查；McGill 的 BIOME Book，NYCU-Taiwan 提供 LbCas12a 條目的文字與概念、McGill 負責繪圖；以及 KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei 與 HKSSC 把中心法則一分為二做成兩套實體教具——8 月 20 日與 9 月 19 日兩次線上規劃會議、以共用 Google Drive 交換原型，然後各自針對自己的受眾改編：KCIS 把 HKSSC 的平面不織布轉譯框架重做成帶有 E、P、A 位點凹槽的立體觸覺盒，給台北啟明學校的七名學生使用。**通不過的**：破冰遊戲、疊疊樂、沙包投擲、社群佈告欄、「我們和其他隊伍交換了想法」。NYCU-Taiwan 自己在 wiki 上就把話說破了：把活動記錄下來，本身並不能證明它的長期影響。\n\n2026 年最大的缺口在技術面。**106 支隊伍中沒有任何一支跑過跨實驗室量測環**——也就是同一個構築體或樣本由數支隊伍在各自儀器上量測，並公布實驗室之間的差異。最接近的一次，結果是零。後來拿下大專組 Best Software Tool 與 Best Wiki 的 Uni-Padua-IT 在軟體頁上寫道：*「2026 年 8 月 9 日，我們發出一份公開的合作邀請，希望有人協助驗證這個軟體，並用兩種真的能觸及到人的管道發布：我們的社群媒體，以及直接寄給其他 iGEM 隊伍。條件很簡單：告訴我們你的宿主，我們幫你最佳化一條序列再寄回去。可惜的是，我們沒有收到任何回覆。」* 這個群體裡唯一真正的獨立重現來自 iGEM 之外——四名 Hanyang University 的機械工程系學生，僅憑公開文件就重建了 PSI Korea 的判讀器——或是跨年度的：HongKong-HS 用 Wageningen 2024 年釋出的 miRADAR 產生 toehold 候選序列，Mingdao 則在 34 °C、Bis-Tris pH 6.4 的條件下重新表徵 cenA 這條零件血脈（Edinburgh 2008、CAU_China 2019、XMU-China 2019、SYSU-CHINA 2021），而不是沿用標準的 50 °C 酸性條件。至於兩支 2026 年隊伍之間真正的零件或樣本交換：基本上不存在。\n\n**那合作和名次有關嗎？老實說，沒有。** 把 106 份檔案分成三類——實質共同產出（S，n = 48）、僅出席或露臉（A，n = 21）、沒有任何記錄（N，n = 37）——Top 10 的比例分別是 14/48（29%）、10/21（48%）與 6/37（16%）；至少拿下一項大獎的比例是 29/48（60%）、10/21（48%）與 15/37（41%）。「實質合作勝過單純出席」這個假設方向是反的，而且不顯著（Fisher 精確檢定 p = 0.17）。唯一還有點訊號的是最粗的對比——有任何跨隊記錄者 24/69 進 Top 10，對上完全沒有的 6/37——但 p = 0.069，最多只能說有暗示，而且還被一個事實干擾：寫得多的隊伍本來就得獎得多。整個網路裡兩個最大的連結點，辦了 European Meet-Up 與大約 37 隊經手的 Community Blackboard 的 Bielefeld-CeBiTec，以及主編 17 隊手冊的 JLU-FBH，各自只拿到一面金牌，別無其他。**只有一個獎項真的相關，而那個獎是其他隊伍投出來的。** 2026 年兩座 iGEMers Prize 都落在各自組別中社群建設記錄最完整的隊伍：主辦 15 隊論壇並為另外兩隊的出版品撰稿的 HUST-China，以及營運 TGEM 的 Labi-Taiwan。2026 年評審沒有獎勵合作，同儕有。\n\n台灣辦了**兩場**全國性活動，而 GEMS-Taiwan 兩場都不在。NYCU-Taiwan 於 7 月 27 日在博愛校區賢齊廳舉辦 2026 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up：53 名學生與指導老師、五支台灣隊伍（NYCU-Taiwan、HIA-Taiwan、NCKU-Tainan、VIS、WIST）外加線上參與的 Okinawa、四項破冰活動、五個圓桌主題、兩位講者、五場十五分鐘的模擬簡報，以及真正重要的那一項——把圓桌便利貼整理成一份 iGEM Team Operations Guide，並公開籌備 SOP、報名表單範本與議程，供未來的主辦者沿用。Labi-Taiwan 則於 8 月 22 日在台灣大學博雅教學館舉辦第四屆 TGEM，與台大生化科技學系合辦：模擬競賽採五分鐘簡報加二十分鐘由教授、PI 與業界評審提問的形式。TGEM 自 2023 年起每年舉辦，由康橋國際學校林口校區創立，也就是 Labi-Taiwan 自己的前身。2026 年具名的參與隊伍包括 NTHU Taiwan、Claremont CA、AEI Prep-Taiwan 與 KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei。NCKU-Tainan 是記錄上最忙碌的台灣夥伴：3 月 7 日指導 Mingdao、7 月的 NYCU 聚會、9 月 17 日與 WIST 的完整線上交流（涵蓋濕式實驗瓶頸與乾式建模比較）、9 月 19 日與 CCU-Taiwan、9 月 20 日與 HIA-Taiwan，以及 10 月 8 日和 NTHU 一起參加 TAU-Israel 的八隊 Mini-Jamboree。**GEMS-Taiwan 沒有 /collaborations 頁、沒有 /partnership 頁，整個 wiki 上也沒有提到任何一支其他 iGEM 隊伍。** 它唯一列出的「夥伴隊伍」是 Geospatial Analysis，那是隊內的分組。\n\n最後對證據本身提一個警告。**2026 年的合作宣稱經常只有單方面記錄。** NCKU-Tainan 詳述了三月指導 Mingdao、九月與 WIST 的技術交流；Mingdao 與 WIST 的 wiki 都沒提到 NCKU-Tainan。ASIJ-Tokyo 把 KCIS Xiugang 列入八支夥伴隊伍；KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei 的合作頁只寫了 HKSSC。NYCU-Taiwan 把 WIST 列為聚會出席者；WIST 的頁面沒提這場活動。當一項宣稱只出現在其中一方的 wiki 上，合作通常是真的，單方面的是記錄——而這本身就是教訓：寫下來的那一方拿到功勞，也拿到那個可重複使用的成果；沒寫的那一方只拿到照片。","cards":[{"kicker":"Taiwan · 27 July","kicker_zh":"台灣 · 7 月 27 日","title":"NYCU-Taiwan's Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up","title_zh":"NYCU-Taiwan 的 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up","body":"53 students and advisors from five Taiwanese teams — NYCU-Taiwan, HIA-Taiwan, NCKU-Tainan, VIS and WIST — at Xian-Qi Hall, Bo-Ai Campus, with Okinawa joining online for a sixth. Four icebreakers, five roundtable themes, two guest speakers, five fifteen-minute mock presentations. The reusable outputs are an iGEM Team Operations Guide compiled from the roundtable notes, plus preparation SOPs, registration form templates and event schedules published for future organisers. NYCU reached Okinawa by flying there in person first. HIA-Taiwan ran a separate bilateral exchange with NYCU on 21 July and surveyed it: 73.3 percent of participants rated their understanding of the other team's project 4 or 5.","body_zh":"53 名學生與指導老師，來自五支台灣隊伍——NYCU-Taiwan、HIA-Taiwan、NCKU-Tainan、VIS 與 WIST——地點在博愛校區賢齊廳，Okinawa 以線上方式成為第六隊。四項破冰活動、五個圓桌主題、兩位講者、五場十五分鐘模擬簡報。可重複使用的成果是從圓桌便利貼整理出的 iGEM Team Operations Guide，加上公開給未來主辦者的籌備 SOP、報名表單範本與活動議程。NYCU 是先親自飛去沖繩才連上 Okinawa 的。HIA-Taiwan 另外在 7 月 21 日與 NYCU 做了一場雙邊交流並做了問卷：73.3% 的參與者對另一隊專案的理解程度自評 4 或 5 分。","chips":["53 attendees","5 Taiwan teams","+1 online","27 Jul 2026"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/nycu-taiwan/collaborations","linkText":"NYCU-Taiwan collaborations"},{"kicker":"Taiwan · 22 August","kicker_zh":"台灣 · 8 月 22 日","title":"TGEM, the fourth Taiwan iGEM Meetup","title_zh":"TGEM，第四屆台灣 iGEM 聚會","body":"Hosted by Labi-Taiwan at the Boya Building, National Taiwan University, co-hosted with NTU's Department of Biochemical Science and Technology. Format: a five-minute project overview followed by twenty minutes of questions from professors, principal investigators, industry professionals and advisers, then ten-minute village presentations. Running annually since 2023, founded by Kang Chiao International School Linkou — Labi-Taiwan's own predecessor, which competed as Taipei-KCISLK V1 to V3. Named 2026 participants include NTHU Taiwan, Claremont CA, AEI Prep-Taiwan and KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei, whose wiki records the full judging transcript and the four engineering changes it forced. Labi-Taiwan won the peer-voted iGEMers Prize in the High School section.","body_zh":"由 Labi-Taiwan 在台灣大學博雅教學館主辦，與台大生化科技學系合辦。形式為五分鐘專案概述，接著二十分鐘由教授、計畫主持人、業界專業人士與指導老師提問，之後是十分鐘的 village 簡報。自 2023 年起每年舉辦，由康橋國際學校林口校區創立——也就是 Labi-Taiwan 自己的前身，曾以 Taipei-KCISLK V1 至 V3 參賽。2026 年具名的參與隊伍包括 NTHU Taiwan、Claremont CA、AEI Prep-Taiwan 與 KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei，後者的 wiki 完整記錄了評審問答，以及因此促成的四項工程修正。Labi-Taiwan 拿下高中組由各隊互投的 iGEMers Prize。","chips":["4th edition","NTU Boya Building","22 Aug 2026","iGEMers Prize host"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/labi-taiwan/education?tab=tgem","linkText":"Labi-Taiwan on TGEM"},{"kicker":"The null result","kicker_zh":"零結果","title":"Nobody answered Uni-Padua","title_zh":"沒有人回覆 Uni-Padua","body":"On 9 August 2026 Uni-Padua-IT published an open call offering to codon-optimise any team's sequence for its chassis with ReTIsigner and send the result back, pushed through social media and directly to other iGEM teams. They received no replies, and they say so on the wiki. They went on to win Best Software Tool and Best Wiki in the Undergraduate section anyway. Read alongside the fact that not one of the 106 decorated teams ran an inter-lab measurement ring, the conclusion is that 2026's network carried people and slides but almost no reagents, constructs or measurements.","body_zh":"2026 年 8 月 9 日，Uni-Padua-IT 發出公開邀請，提議用 ReTIsigner 替任何隊伍針對其宿主做密碼子最佳化並把結果寄回，透過社群媒體與直接聯繫其他 iGEM 隊伍兩種管道發布。他們沒有收到任何回覆，並把這件事寫在 wiki 上。即便如此，他們仍拿下大專組 Best Software Tool 與 Best Wiki。把這件事和「106 支得獎隊伍中沒有任何一支跑過跨實驗室量測環」放在一起看，結論是：2026 年的網路輸送了人和投影片，卻幾乎沒有輸送試劑、構築體或量測數據。","chips":["0 replies","9 Aug 2026","0 inter-lab rings / 106"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/uni-padua-it/software","linkText":"Uni-Padua-IT software page"},{"kicker":"The one co-produced artefact","kicker_zh":"唯一的共同產出","title":"KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei × HKSSC","title_zh":"KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei × HKSSC","body":"Two virtual planning sessions, 20 August and 19 September. They split the central dogma: KCIS built a sequential LEGO track for transcription and gene regulation, HKSSC built an mRNA translation model with slotted E, P and A sites. Prototypes were exchanged as photo and video logs through a shared Google Drive, then each team deployed to its own audience — HKSSC for general science teaching in Hong Kong, KCIS rebuilding HKSSC's flat felt framework as a 3D tactile box with pipe-cleaner tRNA and Styrofoam amino acids for seven students at the Taipei School for the Visually Impaired. KCIS reports the limits too: N = 7, no pre-test, 4 of 7 found the tactile markers helpful. This is the only Taiwan-linked collaboration in 2026 that produced a physical object two teams can both hand on.","body_zh":"兩次線上規劃會議，8 月 20 日與 9 月 19 日。兩隊把中心法則一分為二：KCIS 做出一條依序推進的樂高軌道，呈現轉錄與基因調控；HKSSC 做出帶有 E、P、A 位點凹槽的 mRNA 轉譯模型。原型以照片與影片記錄，透過共用的 Google Drive 交換，然後各自投入自己的受眾——HKSSC 用於香港校內的一般科學教學，KCIS 則把 HKSSC 的平面不織布框架重做成立體觸覺盒，以毛根代表 tRNA、保麗龍球代表胺基酸，給台北啟明學校的七名學生使用。KCIS 也寫出了限制：N = 7、沒有前測、七人中有四人覺得觸覺標記有幫助。這是 2026 年唯一一項與台灣有關、並產出兩隊都能繼續傳下去的實體成果的合作。","chips":["2 planning calls","shared Drive","N = 7 pupils","Taipei × Hong Kong"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/kcis-xiugang-taipei/collaboration","linkText":"KCIS-Xiugang collaboration page"},{"kicker":"The hubs","kicker_zh":"樞紐","title":"HUST-China: fifteen teams, one forum, one peer prize","title_zh":"HUST-China：十五支隊伍、一場論壇、一座同儕獎","body":"On 12 July 2026 HUST-China independently hosted the First Central-China iGEM Forum at the Qiming College Maker Space, replicating the Jamboree's own structure — opening speeches, keynotes, a LiveStage block, judge comment sessions and poster booths — for fifteen online and offline teams, of which fourteen presented and received targeted commentary. They then wrote a full entry into JLU-FBH's 17-team myth-busting handbook and specialised content into BUCT's air-to-protein publication, mutually reviewed and published on BUCT's wiki. They won the peer-voted iGEMers Prize. The other 2026 iGEMers Prize, in the High School section, went to Labi-Taiwan, which runs TGEM. Two for two: the prize other teams vote for went to the two biggest community builders.","body_zh":"2026 年 7 月 12 日，HUST-China 獨力在啟明學院創客空間舉辦第一屆華中 iGEM 論壇，刻意複製 Jamboree 本身的架構——開幕致詞、主題演講、LiveStage 時段、評審評論環節與海報攤位——共 15 支線上與線下隊伍參與，其中 14 支依序報告並收到具體評論。之後他們為 JLU-FBH 統整的 17 隊破除迷思手冊獨立撰寫了一則完整條目，也為 BUCT 的「空氣變蛋白」科普出版品提供專業內容，經互審後刊在 BUCT 的 wiki 上。他們拿下各隊互投的 iGEMers Prize。2026 年另一座 iGEMers Prize 在高中組，得主是營運 TGEM 的 Labi-Taiwan。兩座全中：由其他隊伍投票的獎項，落在兩個最大的社群建設者身上。","chips":["15 teams","12 Jul 2026","17-team handbook","iGEMers Prize"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/hust-china/collaboration","linkText":"HUST-China collaboration"},{"kicker":"The connectors win nothing","kicker_zh":"連結者什麼也沒拿到","title":"Bielefeld-CeBiTec, JLU-FBH, Lund, Okinawa","title_zh":"Bielefeld-CeBiTec、JLU-FBH、Lund、Okinawa","body":"The teams that carried the 2026 network were not rewarded for it. Bielefeld-CeBiTec (6221) co-ran the BFH European Meet-Up in Hamburg on 15–17 May and the Community Blackboard that roughly 37 teams passed through: Gold plus one Safety and Security nomination. JLU-FBH (6056), chief editor of the handbook 17-plus teams wrote into: Gold, nothing else. BUCT (6055), co-producer with HUST-China: Gold, nothing else. NAU-CHINA (6419), which ran the nationwide ICII initiative that HUST explicitly copied: Gold and one part nomination. Lund (6160), whose podcast The Sequence featured about twelve teams including NYCU-Taiwan: Silver. Okinawa (6155), the one Japanese team that joined Taiwan's meet-up: no medal at all. Verified team by team against api.igem.org.","body_zh":"撐起 2026 年這張網的隊伍並沒有因此得到回報。Bielefeld-CeBiTec（6221）與人合辦 5 月 15 至 17 日在 Hamburg 的 BFH European Meet-Up，以及大約 37 隊經手的 Community Blackboard：金牌加一項 Safety and Security 入圍。JLU-FBH（6056），17 支以上隊伍投稿的那本手冊的主編：金牌，沒有別的。BUCT（6055），與 HUST-China 共同產出：金牌，沒有別的。NAU-CHINA（6419），推動全國性 ICII 計畫、而 HUST 明言借用其邏輯：金牌加一項零件入圍。Lund（6160），其播客 The Sequence 收錄約十二支隊伍、包含 NYCU-Taiwan：銀牌。Okinawa（6155），唯一參加台灣聚會的日本隊伍：完全沒有獎牌。以上逐隊比對 api.igem.org 查證。","chips":["~37 teams","Gold only","Silver","no medal"],"link":"https://api.igem.org/v1/teams/6221/awards","linkText":"iGEM API awards"},{"kicker":"GEMS-Taiwan · 6072","kicker_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan · 6072","title":"Zero edges, three wins","title_zh":"零連結，三項大獎","body":"GEMS-Taiwan has no /collaborations page and no /partnership page — both return 404 — and no other iGEM team is named anywhere on its wiki. Its one listed partner team, Geospatial Analysis, is an internal sub-team. It appears on no other Taiwanese team's collaboration page: not NYCU-Taiwan's, not NCKU-Tainan's, not KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei's, and it is not among the teams Labi-Taiwan names at TGEM. It still took High School Top 10 with wins in Measurement, Hardware and Integrated Human Practices. State that plainly: in 2026 collaboration did not buy placing, and GEMS is the proof. The case for building a network is not the medal — it is that GEMS currently has nowhere to send a construct and nobody to check its numbers.","body_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 沒有 /collaborations 頁，也沒有 /partnership 頁——兩者都回傳 404——整個 wiki 上也沒有具名提到任何其他 iGEM 隊伍。它唯一列出的夥伴隊伍 Geospatial Analysis 是隊內分組。它沒有出現在任何其他台灣隊伍的合作頁上：NYCU-Taiwan 沒有、NCKU-Tainan 沒有、KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei 沒有，也不在 Labi-Taiwan 的 TGEM 具名隊伍之列。它仍然拿下高中組 Top 10，以及最佳量測、最佳硬體與最佳整合式人類實踐三項大獎。這件事要講白：2026 年合作並沒有換來名次，GEMS 就是證明。建立網路的理由不是獎牌——而是 GEMS 現在沒有地方可以寄出一個構築體，也沒有人可以幫它驗證數字。","chips":["0 partner teams","404 on /collaborations","Top 10","3 wins"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/","linkText":"GEMS-Taiwan wiki"}],"table":{"head":["Event","Host","Date","Who came","GEMS there?"],"head_zh":["活動","主辦","日期","誰出席","GEMS 有去嗎？"],"rows":[["2026 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up","NYCU-Taiwan (6306)","27 Jul, Bo-Ai Campus, Hsinchu","53 people; NYCU-Taiwan, HIA-Taiwan, NCKU-Tainan, VIS, WIST + Okinawa online","No"],["TGEM 2026, 4th Taiwan iGEM Meetup","Labi-Taiwan (6511) with NTU Dept of Biochemical Science and Technology","22 Aug, Boya Building, NTU","NTHU Taiwan, Claremont CA, AEI Prep-Taiwan, KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei named","No"],["Grand APiC, 1st Asia-Pacific Synthetic Biology Youth Conference","SUSTech and the University of Hong Kong","16-19 Aug","HUST-China; Peking won Best Project; HKSSC and HKU-HongKong sit in the APiC / iGBA community","No"],["Japan iGEM meet-up","Hiroo Gakuen (HG-Tokyo, 6352)","2026","ASIJ-Tokyo, UTokyo, TUS, Waseda, Keio, Oakridge, HG","No"],["First Central-China iGEM Forum (CCiF)","HUST-China (6284)","12 Jul, Qiming College Maker Space","15 teams online and offline; 14 presented","No"],["Mini-Jamboree (online)","TAU-Israel (6196)","8 Oct","8 teams: NCKU-Tainan, NTHU, CAU-China, Cell Forge, iGEM-UA Alicante, UFRGS-Brazil, AIS-China + host","No"],["Cross-team communication session","Bist-China (6263)","2026","ZJU-China, ZJUT-China, HiZJU-China, HangzhouFourteenAP, OTIA-Hangzhou, WUXI-DSAS, iZJU-China, ZZU-China","No"],["Five-school joint biosafety manual","HBUT-China (6330)","2026","ZJU-China, BNU-China, JLU-FBH, ZJUT-China","No"],["BFH European Meet-Up, 3rd edition","Bielefeld, Frankfurt and Hamburg","15-17 May, Hamburg","Uni-Padua-IT, KIT, ETH-Zurich, Muenster-University and others; Community Blackboard drew ~37 teams including NYCU-Taiwan","No"],["NCKU-Tainan's bilateral run","NCKU-Tainan (6379)","7 Mar - 20 Sep","Mingdao (mentorship), WIST (wet-lab and dry-lab session, 17 Sep), CCU-Taiwan (19 Sep), HIA-Taiwan (20 Sep)","No"]],"rows_zh":[["2026 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up","NYCU-Taiwan (6306)","7 月 27 日，新竹博愛校區","53 人；NYCU-Taiwan、HIA-Taiwan、NCKU-Tainan、VIS、WIST，Okinawa 線上","沒有"],["TGEM 2026，第四屆台灣 iGEM 聚會","Labi-Taiwan (6511) 與台大生化科技學系","8 月 22 日，台大博雅教學館","具名者：NTHU Taiwan、Claremont CA、AEI Prep-Taiwan、KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei","沒有"],["Grand APiC，第一屆亞太合成生物學青年大會","SUSTech 與香港大學","8 月 16 至 19 日","HUST-China；Peking 獲 Best Project；HKSSC 與 HKU-HongKong 屬於 APiC / iGBA 社群","沒有"],["日本 iGEM 聚會","Hiroo Gakuen（HG-Tokyo, 6352）","2026 年","ASIJ-Tokyo、UTokyo、TUS、Waseda、Keio、Oakridge、HG","沒有"],["第一屆華中 iGEM 論壇（CCiF）","HUST-China (6284)","7 月 12 日，啟明學院創客空間","15 支線上與線下隊伍；14 支報告","沒有"],["Mini-Jamboree（線上）","TAU-Israel (6196)","10 月 8 日","8 支隊伍：NCKU-Tainan、NTHU、CAU-China、Cell Forge、iGEM-UA Alicante、UFRGS-Brazil、AIS-China 加主辦","沒有"],["跨隊交流場次","Bist-China (6263)","2026 年","ZJU-China、ZJUT-China、HiZJU-China、HangzhouFourteenAP、OTIA-Hangzhou、WUXI-DSAS、iZJU-China、ZZU-China","沒有"],["五校聯合生物安全手冊","HBUT-China (6330)","2026 年","ZJU-China、BNU-China、JLU-FBH、ZJUT-China","沒有"],["BFH European Meet-Up 第三屆","Bielefeld、Frankfurt 與 Hamburg","5 月 15 至 17 日，Hamburg","Uni-Padua-IT、KIT、ETH-Zurich、Muenster-University 等；Community Blackboard 吸引約 37 支隊伍，含 NYCU-Taiwan","沒有"],["NCKU-Tainan 的雙邊系列","NCKU-Tainan (6379)","3 月 7 日至 9 月 20 日","Mingdao（指導）、WIST（濕式與乾式實驗交流，9 月 17 日）、CCU-Taiwan（9 月 19 日）、HIA-Taiwan（9 月 20 日）","沒有"]]},"checklist":["March 2027 — the GEMS human practices lead emails Labi-Taiwan and the NTU Department of Biochemical Science and Technology to register for TGEM 2027. TGEM has run every August since 2023 and is held in Taipei, where GEMS already is; the 2026 edition judged teams with a five-minute pitch plus twenty minutes of questions from professors and industry. Ask for a slot in the high-school division and offer, in the same email, to run a thirty-minute measurement clinic using the Best Measurement work.","April 2027 — email NYCU-Taiwan. They published their meet-up preparation SOPs, registration form templates and event schedules explicitly for future organisers to adapt, and wrote on their own wiki that next time they want a collaboration interest form rather than a poster. Take them at their word: offer to co-host the 2027 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up in Taipei, or to run the measurement session at theirs.","May 2027 — propose the inter-lab measurement ring nobody ran in 2026. Write to four named teams at once: NCKU-Tainan 6379 (Best Hardware nominee, the US$54-161 CAPTURE-Screen fluorescence reader, and already the busiest technical partner in Taiwan), NTHU 6460 (four-channel frequency-tagged reader with digital lock-in detection), Labi-Taiwan 6511 (Best Measurement nominee, portable electrochemical reader) and Mingdao 6105, the only Taiwanese team that has already re-characterised another team's part at new conditions. The offer is concrete: GEMS ships one calibrated reference construct plus its photometer protocol, each team measures it on its own instrument, and the between-lab spread is published jointly.","May 2027 — before any team says yes, put the ring protocol on the GEMS wiki as a dated, versioned page with the calibration curve, the acceptance criteria and the raw-data template. Uni-Padua-IT's open call failed with nothing attached; an offer that arrives with a finished protocol and a shipping plan is a different object.","June 2027 — copy the KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei and HKSSC method for the cross-border attempt, because it is the only one in the 2026 Taiwanese record that produced a shared artefact: two scheduled planning calls six weeks apart, an agreed split of the work, prototypes exchanged through a shared drive, then each team adapting to its own audience. Approach HKSSC 6053 (High School Top 10, Best New Basic Part winner, already in the APiC and iGBA communities) or ASIJ-Tokyo 6338, which ran activities with eight teams across eight countries and already has a Taiwanese tie.","July 2027 — write to Okinawa 6155 and HG-Tokyo 6352. Okinawa joined Taiwan's meet-up online after NYCU flew there, and won no medal in 2026; HG-Tokyo hosts the Japanese meet-up that UTokyo, TUS, Waseda, Keio, Oakridge and ASIJ attend. Both are reachable, and both have an incentive GEMS can serve.","August 2027 — apply to Grand APiC. The first Asia-Pacific Synthetic Biology Youth Conference ran 16-19 August 2026 at SUSTech and the University of Hong Kong; Peking took Best Project there and HKSSC and HKU-HongKong sit inside the APiC and iGBA community. It is the regional umbrella a Taiwanese high-school research centre can enter without an invitation from any one team.","Throughout — build /collaborations as a page with dates, named counterparts and outputs, not a gallery. And adopt a reciprocity rule: every exchange gets a one-paragraph record on both wikis, agreed before the call ends. In 2026 NCKU-Tainan, ASIJ-Tokyo and NYCU-Taiwan each wrote up partners whose own wikis stayed silent; the partner who writes it up keeps the credit and the reusable artefact."],"checklist_zh":["2027 年 3 月——GEMS 的人類實踐負責人寄信給 Labi-Taiwan 與台大生化科技學系，報名 TGEM 2027。TGEM 自 2023 年起每年八月舉辦，地點在台北，GEMS 本來就在台北；2026 年的形式是五分鐘簡報加二十分鐘由教授與業界提問。爭取高中組的名額，並在同一封信裡提議用 Best Measurement 的成果開一場三十分鐘的量測工作坊。","2027 年 4 月——寄信給 NYCU-Taiwan。他們公開了聚會的籌備 SOP、報名表單範本與活動議程，明言供未來主辦者沿用，也在自己的 wiki 上寫下次想要的是一份合作意向表單而不是一張海報。就照他們說的做：提議在台北共同主辦 2027 年的 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up，或在他們的場次裡負責量測單元。","2027 年 5 月——提出 2026 年沒有任何人做過的跨實驗室量測環。同時寫給四支具名隊伍：NCKU-Tainan 6379（Best Hardware 入圍、US$54-161 的 CAPTURE-Screen 螢光判讀器，也是台灣記錄上最忙碌的技術夥伴）、NTHU 6460（四通道頻率標記判讀器，採數位鎖相偵測）、Labi-Taiwan 6511（Best Measurement 入圍、可攜式電化學判讀器），以及 Mingdao 6105，台灣唯一已經在新條件下重新表徵過別隊零件的隊伍。提案要具體：GEMS 寄出一個經校正的參考構築體與光度計操作流程，各隊在自己的儀器上量測，實驗室之間的差異共同發表。","2027 年 5 月——在任何一隊答應之前，先把量測環的流程放上 GEMS wiki，做成有日期、有版本的頁面，附校正曲線、接受標準與原始資料範本。Uni-Padua-IT 的公開邀請失敗時什麼也沒附；一份帶著完成的流程與寄送計畫送到的邀請，是完全不同的東西。","2027 年 6 月——跨境嘗試就照 KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei 與 HKSSC 的做法複製，因為那是 2026 年台灣記錄中唯一產出共同成果的方法：兩次相隔六週的既定線上規劃會議、講好的分工、透過共用雲端硬碟交換原型，然後各自針對自己的受眾改編。對象可以是 HKSSC 6053（高中組 Top 10、Best New Basic Part 得主，已在 APiC 與 iGBA 社群內），或 ASIJ-Tokyo 6338，他們與八個國家的八支隊伍合辦活動，而且已經有一條通往台灣的線。","2027 年 7 月——寫信給 Okinawa 6155 與 HG-Tokyo 6352。Okinawa 是在 NYCU 親自飛去之後才線上參加台灣聚會的，2026 年沒有拿到任何獎牌；HG-Tokyo 主辦 UTokyo、TUS、Waseda、Keio、Oakridge 與 ASIJ 參加的日本聚會。兩者都連得上，也都有 GEMS 能回應的需求。","2027 年 8 月——報名 Grand APiC。第一屆亞太合成生物學青年大會於 2026 年 8 月 16 至 19 日在 SUSTech 與香港大學舉行；Peking 在該場拿下 Best Project，HKSSC 與 HKU-HongKong 都在 APiC 與 iGBA 社群裡。這是台灣的高中研究中心不需要任何單一隊伍邀請就能進入的區域傘狀組織。","全程——把 /collaborations 做成一個有日期、有具名對象、有產出的頁面，不是相簿。並且建立互惠規則：每一次交流，在會議結束前就講好雙方 wiki 各留一段記錄。2026 年 NCKU-Tainan、ASIJ-Tokyo 與 NYCU-Taiwan 都寫下了夥伴，而那些夥伴自己的 wiki 卻一片沉默；寫下來的那一方，留住了功勞，也留住了那個可重複使用的成果。"],"method":"The first pass was on disk: all 106 researched team files in research/teams/ were grepped for collaboration signals (collaborat, meet-up, meetup, partner, exchange, inter-lab, interlab, conference, mentor, jointly, shared, co-hosted, iGEM team, other teams), returning hits in 74 files, and every good.partners[] entry naming an iGEM team or meet-up was extracted separately. This cannot see a collaboration a team did but did not write up, and it demonstrably misses some: NCKU-Tainan's file contains no collaboration signal at all, yet its wiki carries five dated exchanges. The classification behind the correlation (S = substantive co-production, n = 48; A = attendance or visibility only, n = 21; N = none documented, n = 37) is therefore a documentation proxy, not a census of behaviour, and the Fisher exact tests reported are two-sided on those counts. The roster and every award cited were taken from iGEM's public API — api.igem.org/v1/teams?year=2026 for all 463 registrations across 24 pages, and api.igem.org/v1/teams/<id>/awards for individual teams including Bielefeld-CeBiTec 6221, JLU-FBH 6056, BUCT 6055, NAU-CHINA 6419, Lund 6160, Okinawa 6155 and Claremont CA 6317 — not from any hand-written list. Wiki verification ran over /collaborations, /collaboration, /partnership, /partnerships, /collaborations-and-partnerships, /collaboration-partnership and /public-outreach-and-collaboration for 131 slugs: 568 of 917 returned 404, and many of the rest are client-rendered single-page apps that return HTTP 200 for any route, so the browser was used for Labi-Taiwan, CCU-Taiwan and Uni-Padua-IT while NYCU-Taiwan, NCKU-Tainan, KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei, Squirrel-Beijing and others were read directly. GEMS-Taiwan's absence was checked positively: /collaborations, /collaboration and /partnership all return 404, and its human-practices, education and contribution pages name no other iGEM team. Reciprocity was spot-checked in both directions and three one-sided claims are reported as findings. Pages were read on 19 November 2026.","method_zh":"第一輪在本機進行：對 research/teams/ 下全部 106 份隊伍研究檔案做合作訊號的 grep（collaborat、meet-up、meetup、partner、exchange、inter-lab、interlab、conference、mentor、jointly、shared、co-hosted、iGEM team、other teams），在 74 份檔案中找到命中，並另外抽出所有具名提及 iGEM 隊伍或聚會的 good.partners[] 條目。這種做法看不到一支隊伍做了卻沒寫下來的合作，而且確實有漏：NCKU-Tainan 的檔案完全沒有合作訊號，但它的 wiki 上有五場標了日期的交流。因此，相關性分析背後的分類（S = 實質共同產出，n = 48；A = 僅出席或露臉，n = 21；N = 沒有記錄，n = 37）是一個「記錄」的代理指標，不是行為普查；所報的 Fisher 精確檢定為雙尾。名單與所有引用的獎項都取自 iGEM 的公開 API——api.igem.org/v1/teams?year=2026 取得分 24 頁的全部 463 筆報名，以及 api.igem.org/v1/teams/<id>/awards 取得個別隊伍的獎項，包括 Bielefeld-CeBiTec 6221、JLU-FBH 6056、BUCT 6055、NAU-CHINA 6419、Lund 6160、Okinawa 6155 與 Claremont CA 6317——而不是任何手寫清單。Wiki 查證涵蓋 131 個隊伍網址的 /collaborations、/collaboration、/partnership、/partnerships、/collaborations-and-partnerships、/collaboration-partnership 與 /public-outreach-and-collaboration：917 個網址中有 568 個回傳 404，其餘不少是用戶端渲染的單頁應用，任何路徑都回傳 HTTP 200，因此 Labi-Taiwan、CCU-Taiwan 與 Uni-Padua-IT 改用瀏覽器讀取，而 NYCU-Taiwan、NCKU-Tainan、KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei、Squirrel-Beijing 等則直接讀取。GEMS-Taiwan 的缺席是正面查證過的：/collaborations、/collaboration 與 /partnership 全部回傳 404，而其 human-practices、education 與 contribution 頁面都沒有具名提到任何其他 iGEM 隊伍。互惠性做了雙向抽查，三項單方面宣稱以發現的形式寫入。頁面讀取日期為 2026 年 11 月 19 日。"},{"id":"real-world","tab":"good","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"The commercial work that was worth reading argued against itself","title_zh":"值得一讀的商業分析，都在反駁自己","lede":"Across the 2026 field, the teams with credible real-world plans are the ones that published a model showing their own product losing.","lede_zh":"綜觀 2026 年，真實世界計畫最可信的團隊，都公開了一個顯示自家產品輸掉的模型。","body":"Almost every iGEM team produces a business model canvas. Very few produce a number that could have gone against them. The difference is the whole of what separates a credible 2026 commercial section from a template.\n\n**Worldshaper-Shanghai** published a recomputable net-present-value model and reported the result honestly: their own enzyme gives a **negative NPV**. They did not bury it, soften it, or quietly change the discount rate. **BGI-College** did the same with arithmetic instead of finance — a break-even calculation comparing 6.70 against 4.0 mol H₂ per mol glucose disproved the team's own premise, and forced a redesign around byproduct valorisation. **DTU-Denmark** ran a prospective life-cycle assessment in SimaPro with ReCiPe 2016 H and found its enzymatic route emits 2.1 kg CO₂-eq/kg against 1.4 for solvolysis and 0.9 for pyrolysis, with cement co-processing beating them on almost every indicator — then converted each losing indicator into a named engineering target. **Madrid-UCM** published an ISO 14040/44 openLCA result that currently rules against its own technology.\n\n**Stockholm** went furthest. Its safety advisory board killed the open-water release the project was built around, so the team dismantled the venture, retreated to a contained membrane bioreactor on a smaller industrial stream, and made the deliverable **reusable safety infrastructure** instead: an STPA hazard analysis, a nine-system wastewater containment guidebook, and a measurement-uncertainty toolkit. Giving up the product and shipping the method is a result, and it was recognised with the Safety and Security Award.\n\nSet against that, the template is easy to spot once you know the tell: **the cost side is real and the revenue side is fantasy**. ZJU-China itemises equipment at CNY 7.45 million, media, IPTG and labour, and publishes a downloadable cost sheet — genuinely good work — then assumes **100% capture of its serviceable obtainable market** to reach a USD 427 million NPV. The discipline applied to the inputs evaporates at the outputs.\n\nThe high-school tier is not behind here, and in places it is ahead. **SUIS-SFLS** built the only full financial model in the high-school set: capital expenditure of CNY 6.8 and 11.65 million across two scenarios, CNY 71 and 163.5 per litre, 34% against 15.9% margins, break-even years, and the spreadsheets published as downloadable PDFs, on a dual NMPA and ISO 13485 regulatory track. **ICJFLS** works bottom-up from unit economics — RMB 0.8 per dose against RMB 199 retail — with a 745-response survey and a named CDMO. **NFLSHS-CHINA** has a filed and accepted patent on a CsCCD2 mutant, two physical minimum viable products with formula tables, and labels its partnerships as prospective rather than implying they are signed.\n\nThe second thing the credible teams do is **name the stage of each claim**. Baltimore runs Venture Creation Labs OKRs with numeric gates and IRB-approved trilingual surveys, and says plainly that its letters of intent and grants are targets rather than commitments. McGill has a full techno-economic analysis — $11.83 to $20.58 per kg of rare earth oxide, an Ashram project NPV of +USD 51 million, seven sensitivity analyses — an accelerator place, a venture-capital mentor, two letters of support and secured tailings samples, and states that it is not yet incorporated. Nobody is penalised for an early-stage venture. Teams are penalised, correctly, for presenting an aspiration in the grammar of an achievement.\n\nAnd a reminder that not every project should become a company. **HBUT-China**, **WHU-China**, **Squirrel-Beijing** and **BASIS-China** have no venture at all. Their deliverable is infrastructure other teams can use: 34 parts in four independently reusable modules with measurement parts built in and honest terminator read-through annotations; a five-layer characterisation of Neo-IL-2 including surface plasmon resonance and high-passage stability; a tunable bile-acid kill switch with a measured 0.1–0.2 mM threshold compared against real sewage and soil concentrations, plus a published five-step framework for characterising kill switches. That is a real-world contribution with a longer half-life than most business plans.","body_zh":"幾乎每一支 iGEM 團隊都會生出一張商業模式畫布，但很少有團隊生出一個「有可能對自己不利」的數字。而這個差別，就是 2026 年可信的商業章節與樣板之間的全部距離。\n\n**Worldshaper-Shanghai** 公開了一個可重新計算的淨現值模型，並誠實報告結果：他們自己的酵素得出**負的 NPV**。他們沒有把它藏起來、淡化，也沒有偷偷調整折現率。**BGI-College** 做了同樣的事，只是用算術而非財務——一個比較 6.70 與 4.0 mol H₂／mol 葡萄糖的損益兩平計算，推翻了團隊自己的前提，迫使他們圍繞副產物加值重新設計。**DTU-Denmark** 以 SimaPro 搭配 ReCiPe 2016 H 做了前瞻性生命週期評估，發現自家的酵素路線排放 2.1 kg CO₂-eq/kg，而溶劑解為 1.4、熱解為 0.9，水泥共處理在幾乎每一項指標上都勝過他們——然後把每一項輸掉的指標轉化為一個具名的工程目標。**Madrid-UCM** 則公開了一份 ISO 14040/44 的 openLCA 結果，而該結果目前判定對他們自己的技術不利。\n\n**Stockholm** 走得最遠。他們的安全諮詢委員會否決了整個專案賴以成立的開放水域釋放，於是團隊拆掉了這個創業構想，退回到處理較小工業廢流的密閉式膜生物反應器，並把產出改成**可重複使用的安全基礎設施**：一份 STPA 危害分析、一本涵蓋九種系統的廢水圍堵指南，以及一套量測不確定度工具包。放棄產品、交付方法，本身就是一種成果，而它拿下了安全與保安獎。\n\n對照之下，樣板一旦知道徵兆就很好認：**成本端是真的，營收端是幻想**。ZJU-China 列出 7,450 萬人民幣的設備、培養基、IPTG 與人力，還公開可下載的成本表——這是扎實的工作——接著假設**100% 拿下其可服務可獲得市場**，得出 4.27 億美元的 NPV。用在投入端的紀律，到了產出端就蒸發了。\n\n高中組在這件事上並不落後，有些地方甚至領先。**SUIS-SFLS** 做出高中組唯一一份完整的財務模型：兩種情境下 680 萬與 1,165 萬人民幣的資本支出、每公升 71 元與 163.5 元、34% 對 15.9% 的毛利率、損益兩平年份，試算表以可下載 PDF 公開，並走 NMPA 與 ISO 13485 雙軌法規路徑。**ICJFLS** 從單位經濟由下而上推算——每劑 0.8 人民幣對零售價 199 元——搭配 745 份問卷與一家具名的 CDMO。**NFLSHS-CHINA** 則有一件已提出並受理的 CsCCD2 突變體專利、兩個附配方表的實體最小可行產品，而且把合作關係標示為「潛在」，不暗示已經簽約。\n\n可信團隊做的第二件事，是**標明每一項主張所處的階段**。Baltimore 以 Venture Creation Labs 的 OKR 搭配量化關卡運作，做了經 IRB 核准的三語問卷，並直說他們的意向書與補助都只是目標，不是承諾。McGill 有完整的技術經濟分析——每公斤稀土氧化物 11.83 至 20.58 美元、Ashram 專案淨現值 +5,100 萬美元、七項敏感度分析——有加速器席位、創投導師、兩封支持信與已取得的尾礦樣本，並載明尚未完成公司設立。沒有人會因為創業處於早期而被扣分；被扣分的——而且理所當然——是用「已完成」的文法去陳述一個「想達成」的願望。\n\n最後提醒：不是每一個專案都該變成公司。**HBUT-China**、**WHU-China**、**Squirrel-Beijing** 與 **BASIS-China** 根本沒有創業規劃。他們的產出是其他團隊可以使用的基礎設施：34 個分屬四個可獨立重用模組的元件，內建量測用元件，並誠實註記終止子讀通問題；Neo-IL-2 的五層次表徵，含表面電漿共振與高代次穩定性；一個可調控的膽酸自殺開關，量測到 0.1–0.2 mM 的閾值並與真實污水及土壤濃度對照，外加一套已發表的自殺開關五步驟表徵框架。這是一種真實世界的貢獻，而且半衰期比多數商業計畫書都長。","cards":[{"kicker":"The strongest move","title":"Publish the model that says no","title_zh":"公開那個說「不」的模型","body":"Worldshaper-Shanghai's recomputable NPV model finds their own enzyme gives a negative NPV, and says so. DTU-Denmark's prospective LCA finds cement co-processing beats their enzymatic route on almost every indicator, then turns each losing indicator into an engineering target. Madrid-UCM's ISO 14040/44 assessment currently rules against its own technology. A model that could only ever have agreed with you is not evidence.","body_zh":"Worldshaper-Shanghai 可重算的 NPV 模型得出自家酵素為負 NPV，而他們照實寫出來。DTU-Denmark 的前瞻性 LCA 發現水泥共處理在幾乎每項指標上都勝過他們的酵素路線，於是把每一項輸掉的指標轉成工程目標。Madrid-UCM 的 ISO 14040/44 評估目前判定對自家技術不利。一個只可能同意你的模型，不是證據。","chips":["negative NPV, published","LCA that rules against you"],"kicker_zh":"最強的一步"},{"kicker":"The tell","title":"Real costs, fantasy revenue","title_zh":"真實的成本，幻想的營收","body":"ZJU-China itemises CNY 7.45 million of equipment, media, IPTG and labour and publishes a downloadable cost sheet — then assumes 100% capture of its serviceable obtainable market to reach a USD 427 million NPV. This is the most common failure mode in iGEM commercial sections: rigour on the inputs, where the team has data, and none on the outputs, where it does not.","body_zh":"ZJU-China 逐項列出 7,450 萬人民幣的設備、培養基、IPTG 與人力，還公開可下載的成本表——接著假設 100% 拿下可服務可獲得市場，得出 4.27 億美元的 NPV。這是 iGEM 商業章節最常見的失敗模式：在團隊有資料的投入端講究嚴謹，在沒有資料的產出端完全放棄。","chips":["100% SOM capture"],"kicker_zh":"破綻"},{"kicker":"The result that looks like a failure","title":"Stockholm dismantled its own venture","title_zh":"Stockholm 拆掉了自己的創業計畫","body":"A safety advisory board killed the open-water release the project was built on. Rather than argue, the team retreated to a contained membrane bioreactor on a smaller stream and shipped reusable safety infrastructure instead — an STPA hazard analysis, a nine-system wastewater containment guidebook, a measurement-uncertainty toolkit. It won the Safety and Security Award. Giving up the product and publishing the method is a result.","body_zh":"安全諮詢委員會否決了這個專案賴以成立的開放水域釋放。團隊沒有爭辯，而是退回到處理較小廢流的密閉式膜生物反應器，改為交付可重複使用的安全基礎設施——STPA 危害分析、涵蓋九種系統的廢水圍堵指南、量測不確定度工具包。它拿下了安全與保安獎。放棄產品、公開方法，本身就是成果。","chips":["Safety and Security Award"],"kicker_zh":"看起來像失敗的成果"},{"kicker":"High school, ahead","title":"SUIS-SFLS built the only full financial model in its tier","title_zh":"SUIS-SFLS 做出該組唯一一份完整財務模型","body":"Capital expenditure of CNY 6.8 and 11.65 million across two scenarios, CNY 71 and 163.5 per litre, 34% against 15.9% margins, break-even years, spreadsheets published as downloadable PDFs, on a dual NMPA and ISO 13485 track. ICJFLS works bottom-up from RMB 0.8 per dose against RMB 199 retail with a named CDMO. The census found high-school teams do more techno-economic analysis than undergraduates; this is what that looks like up close.","body_zh":"兩種情境下 680 萬與 1,165 萬人民幣的資本支出、每公升 71 元與 163.5 元、34% 對 15.9% 的毛利率、損益兩平年份，試算表以可下載 PDF 公開，並走 NMPA 與 ISO 13485 雙軌。ICJFLS 則由下而上從每劑 0.8 人民幣對零售價 199 元推算，並列出具名的 CDMO。技術普查發現高中隊伍做的技術經濟分析比大學部還多；放大來看就是這個樣子。","chips":["capex, margins, break-even","NMPA + ISO 13485"],"kicker_zh":"高中組，領先"},{"kicker":"The habit","title":"Name the stage of every claim","title_zh":"標明每一項主張所處的階段","body":"Baltimore says plainly that its letters of intent and grants are targets, not commitments. McGill has a full techno-economic analysis, an accelerator place, a VC mentor, two letters of support and secured tailings samples — and states it is not yet incorporated. NFLSHS-CHINA labels its partnerships prospective. Nobody is penalised for being early. Teams are penalised for writing an aspiration in the grammar of an achievement.","body_zh":"Baltimore 直說他們的意向書與補助都只是目標，不是承諾。McGill 有完整的技術經濟分析、加速器席位、創投導師、兩封支持信與已取得的尾礦樣本——並載明尚未完成公司設立。NFLSHS-CHINA 把合作關係標示為潛在。沒有人會因為處於早期而被扣分；被扣分的是用「已完成」的文法去寫一個「想達成」的願望。","chips":["early is fine","overclaiming is not"],"kicker_zh":"習慣"},{"kicker":"For GEMS","title":"Not every project should become a company","title_zh":"不是每個專案都該變成公司","body":"HBUT-China, WHU-China, Squirrel-Beijing and BASIS-China have no venture at all. They shipped infrastructure instead — 34 parts in four reusable modules with measurement parts built in, a five-layer Neo-IL-2 characterisation, a tunable kill switch with a measured 0.1–0.2 mM threshold checked against real sewage concentrations, and a published five-step framework for characterising kill switches. For an institution building a reputation, that has a longer half-life than a business plan.","body_zh":"HBUT-China、WHU-China、Squirrel-Beijing 與 BASIS-China 完全沒有創業規劃。他們交付的是基礎設施——34 個分屬四個可重用模組、內建量測元件的零件；Neo-IL-2 的五層次表徵；一個量測到 0.1–0.2 mM 閾值、並與真實污水濃度對照的可調控自殺開關；以及一套已發表的自殺開關五步驟表徵框架。對一個正在建立聲譽的機構而言，這些東西的半衰期比商業計畫書長得多。","chips":["parts outlive plans"],"kicker_zh":"給 GEMS"}],"method":"Drawn from the realWorld fields of the team files in this report, each researched from the team's own 2026 wiki. Financial figures are the teams' own and are not independently audited; where a team's assumptions looked unsupported that is noted as our reading, not as a finding of error. Teams that published a model unfavourable to themselves are over-represented here because that is exactly what the analysis is about — it is not a claim that most 2026 teams did so.","method_zh":"資料取自本報告團隊檔案中的 realWorld 欄位，每一份都來自該隊自己的 2026 wiki。財務數字為各隊自報且未經獨立查核；凡判斷某隊假設缺乏支撐之處，均屬我們的閱讀判斷，而非認定其有誤。公開了對自己不利之模型的團隊在此被過度呈現，因為那正是本篇分析的主題——這並不表示 2026 年多數團隊都這麼做。","kicker_zh":"原創分析","order":34},{"id":"software-afterlife","tab":"drylab","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"Does award-winning iGEM software survive the Jamboree?","title_zh":"得獎的 iGEM 軟體撐得過 Jamboree 嗎？","lede":"Of 21 software tools released by award-winning iGEM 2026 teams, 8 are live and usable by a stranger today, 11 are source-only, and 2 have already gone dark.","lede_zh":"2026 年 iGEM 得獎隊伍釋出的 21 個軟體工具中，今天有 8 個還在線上、陌生人可以直接使用，11 個只有原始碼，2 個已經消失。","body":"**Eight of twenty-one.** That is the honest base rate for award-winning iGEM 2026 software that a stranger can open and use today, four weeks after the Jamboree. Eleven more are source-only: the code is public, populated and often genuinely good, but using it means cloning a repository and running Docker. Two are already dead — Vilnius-Lithuania's Ladder Detector now answers \"This service has been suspended by its owner\" at ladder-detector.onrender.com, and TAU-Israel's CERNAL fails to resolve at both cernal.app and cernal.duckdns.org, the two addresses its own wiki advertises.\n\nThe striking thing is that nothing is a stub. Every repository checked was populated with real code, a README and a licence. iGEM's mandatory GitLab deposit has solved the empty-repo problem completely. What it has not solved, and cannot, is hosting: the competition requires you to publish source, and publishing source is where most teams stop.\n\nThe live ones have one habit in common, and it is not budget. **They bought a domain and pointed it at a running backend before the wiki freeze, then wrote the wiki around a URL rather than around an install command.** NJU-China's Atlas sits on starase-atlas.org, XJTLU-Software's AMPilot on ampilotlab.com, Toronto's PETadex on petadex.net, Stanford's RADAR-Scout on Vercel. Two of the eight are high-school teams running real inference in public: GHCIS's ARGUS answers `{\"status\":\"ready\"}` at argus.ucuv.dpdns.org, and HK-Joint-School's PyroForge reports `models_ready: true, esm_ready: true` — an ESM protein model loaded and serving, from a school team.\n\nThe source-only group is not lazy; it is mostly careful. ETH-Zurich's deCISion ships 28 CI-tested checks, a Docker build and an MIT licence. UMA Malaga's Diana has a 10 GB reproducible Docker stack and a BIOLOGICAL_REPORT.md mapping each biological step to code. Uni-Padua-IT's ReTIsigner is a thoughtful fork of a published tool, Apache 2.0, one `docker run` from working. These teams decided, often explicitly and for defensible reasons — cost, patient data, a 4 GB index — that local execution was the right call. The cost is simply that nobody will ever casually try them.\n\nTwo teams published a live URL that is not the tool, and both said so honestly. UMA Malaga's diana-grna-designer-7723f5.igem.wiki opens with \"Saved results, not the live tool... The pages cannot analyse a variant you type.\" GU Frankfurt's HUSH page says \"This page shows its web app in action\" and then presents a clickable mockup of screenshots. Judges reward the appearance of a deployed tool, so the gap between a demo and a deployment is exactly where a link check gets fooled.\n\nOutside use is the bleakest column. Across every GitLab repository examined the star count is zero, the fork count is zero, and the last commit falls in the October freeze window — with one exception, DKU's pepticraft-2, touched on 5 November. Uni-Padua-IT published an open call on 9 August offering to codon-optimise any team's sequence, received no replies, and reported that on their wiki. The only genuine external-adoption signal found anywhere was on Stanford's SynBase, which displays \"837 learners\" — and that is a teaching platform, not a research tool.\n\nOne more caution for anyone citing datasets as deliverables. Toronto's PETadex front end is live and excellent, but the 23.8 GB Zenodo deposit its wiki cites, doi:10.5281/zenodo.23457986, returns 404, and a Zenodo search for \"petadex\" returns zero records. The web app survived; the archival half of the release did not.\n\nFor GEMS the lesson is narrow and cheap. Shipping a tool outsiders use is achievable — eight teams did it, including two high schools — but it is a hosting decision, not a coding decision, and it has to be made months before the wiki freeze. The teams that got there treated the public URL as the deliverable and the repository as the backup. The ones that did not now own excellent code that nobody will run.","body_zh":"**21 個裡有 8 個。**這就是 2026 年 iGEM 得獎軟體誠實的基礎比率：Jamboree 結束四週後，陌生人今天還打得開、用得動的只有這麼多。另外 11 個只有原始碼：程式公開、內容完整，而且常常真的寫得不錯，但要用它就得把儲存庫 clone 下來再跑 Docker。兩個已經死了——Vilnius-Lithuania 的 Ladder Detector 現在在 ladder-detector.onrender.com 回應「This service has been suspended by its owner」，TAU-Israel 的 CERNAL 在 cernal.app 和 cernal.duckdns.org 都無法解析，而這兩個網址正是它自己的 wiki 上公告的。\n\n值得注意的是，沒有一個是空殼。每一個檢查過的儲存庫都有真正的程式碼、一份 README 和一份授權條款。iGEM 強制要求上傳 GitLab，已經徹底解決了空儲存庫的問題。它沒有解決、也無法解決的是代管：競賽要求你公開原始碼，而公開原始碼就是多數隊伍停下來的地方。\n\n還活著的那些有一個共同習慣，而且不是預算。**他們在 wiki 凍結之前就買好網域、指向一個正在運行的後端，然後把 wiki 寫成繞著一個網址，而不是繞著一行安裝指令。**NJU-China 的 Atlas 放在 starase-atlas.org，XJTLU-Software 的 AMPilot 在 ampilotlab.com，Toronto 的 PETadex 在 petadex.net，Stanford 的 RADAR-Scout 在 Vercel 上。八個裡有兩個是高中隊伍，而且在公開環境跑真正的推論：GHCIS 的 ARGUS 在 argus.ucuv.dpdns.org 回應 `{\"status\":\"ready\"}`，HK-Joint-School 的 PyroForge 回報 `models_ready: true, esm_ready: true`——一個 ESM 蛋白質模型載入並持續提供服務，而這來自一支高中隊伍。\n\n只有原始碼的這一群並不是懶，多半是謹慎。ETH-Zurich 的 deCISion 附上 28 項經 CI 測試的檢查、一套 Docker 建置和 MIT 授權。UMA Malaga 的 Diana 有一套 10 GB 的可重現 Docker 環境，以及一份把每個生物步驟對應到程式碼的 BIOLOGICAL_REPORT.md。Uni-Padua-IT 的 ReTIsigner 是對一個已發表工具用心的分支，採 Apache 2.0，一行 `docker run` 就能動。這些隊伍判斷在本機執行才是對的選擇，而且往往講得很明白、理由也站得住腳——成本、病人資料、一個 4 GB 的索引。代價就只是：永遠不會有人隨手試一下。\n\n有兩支隊伍公布了一個不是工具本身的線上網址，而且兩支都誠實說了。UMA Malaga 的 diana-grna-designer-7723f5.igem.wiki 一開頭就寫「Saved results, not the live tool... The pages cannot analyse a variant you type.」GU Frankfurt 的 HUSH 頁面說「This page shows its web app in action」，接著呈現一份由截圖組成、可以點擊的介面示意稿。評審會獎勵「看起來已經部署」這件事，所以示範與部署之間的落差，正是連結檢查被騙的地方。\n\n外部使用是最慘的一欄。所有檢視過的 GitLab 儲存庫，star 數是零，fork 數是零，最後一次 commit 都落在十月的凍結期內——只有一個例外，DKU 的 pepticraft-2 在 11 月 5 日被動過。Uni-Padua-IT 在 8 月 9 日公開徵求，願意幫任何隊伍做密碼子最佳化，結果沒有收到任何回覆，並且把這件事寫在自己的 wiki 上。在任何地方找到的唯一真實外部採用訊號，是 Stanford 的 SynBase 顯示的「837 learners」——而那是一個教學平台，不是研究工具。\n\n給任何把資料集當成交付成果來引用的人一個提醒。Toronto 的 PETadex 前端還在線上，而且做得很好，但它的 wiki 引用的那份 23.8 GB Zenodo 存放紀錄 doi:10.5281/zenodo.23457986 回傳 404，在 Zenodo 搜尋「petadex」也得到零筆紀錄。網頁應用活了下來；這次釋出中負責封存的那一半沒有。\n\n對 GEMS 來說，這個教訓既狹窄又便宜。做出外人會用的工具是辦得到的——八支隊伍做到了，其中包括兩支高中隊伍——但這是代管的決定，不是寫程式的決定，而且必須在 wiki 凍結前好幾個月就做。做到的隊伍把公開網址當成交付成果，把儲存庫當成備份。沒做到的，現在擁有一堆優秀但沒人會執行的程式碼。","cards":[{"kicker":"Best in class","title":"AMPilot — the only tool with a working public API","title_zh":"AMPilot——唯一有可用公開 API 的工具","body":"XJTLU-Software's antimicrobial-peptide workbench at ampilotlab.com opens in guest mode with no account, and its /api/v1 routes are documented in a published OpenAPI 3.1 spec. A live call to /api/v1/corpus/search returned real literature evidence with provenance, licence and retrieval date attached — no key, no sign-up. The spec states the API is deterministic, stateless and calls no language model, which is what makes it safe for someone else to build on. It is the clearest example this year of a team designing for a second user rather than a judge.","body_zh":"XJTLU-Software 的抗菌肽工作台在 ampilotlab.com 以訪客模式開啟，不需要帳號，它的 /api/v1 路徑都寫在一份公開的 OpenAPI 3.1 規格裡。實際呼叫 /api/v1/corpus/search 回傳了真正的文獻證據，並附上來源、授權條款和取用日期——不用金鑰、不用註冊。規格中載明這個 API 是確定性的、無狀態的，而且不呼叫任何語言模型，這正是別人可以安心在上面開發的原因。這是今年最清楚的一個例子：一支隊伍是為第二個使用者而設計，不是為評審而設計。","chips":["alive","XJTLU-Software","public API","guest mode","OpenAPI 3.1"],"kicker_zh":"同類最佳"},{"kicker":"Proof it is not a budget problem","title":"Two high-school teams out-shipped most universities","title_zh":"兩支高中隊伍交付的成果勝過多數大學隊伍","body":"GHCIS's ARGUS runs a real backend at argus.ucuv.dpdns.org — its /api/ready endpoint answers with JSON, not a static shell — alongside a Docker and a native Node deploy path, role-based access and SQLite persistence. HK-Joint-School's PyroForge serves protein thermostability prediction at pyroforge.26650078.xyz with /health reporting ESM models loaded and ready. Both URLs are reachable right now. Neither team had a university budget; they had a cheap domain and a decision to host.","body_zh":"GHCIS 的 ARGUS 在 argus.ucuv.dpdns.org 跑著一個真正的後端——它的 /api/ready 端點回應的是 JSON，不是靜態空殼——還附上 Docker 和原生 Node 兩條部署路徑、角色式存取控制和 SQLite 持久化儲存。HK-Joint-School 的 PyroForge 在 pyroforge.26650078.xyz 提供蛋白質熱穩定性預測，/health 回報 ESM 模型已載入並就緒。兩個網址現在都連得上。兩支隊伍都沒有大學的預算；他們有的是一個便宜的網域，和一個要架站的決定。","chips":["alive","GHCIS","HK-Joint-School","high school","real backend"],"kicker_zh":"證明這不是預算問題"},{"kicker":"The cautionary tale","title":"Vilnius deployed, then switched it off","title_zh":"Vilnius 部署了，然後把它關掉","body":"Ladder Detector automates gel-image annotation, a genuinely unglamorous and genuinely useful job, and Vilnius-Lithuania did the right thing by deploying it publicly. The URL on their wiki, ladder-detector.onrender.com, now returns HTTP 503 and the text \"This service has been suspended by its owner.\" The Apache-2.0 source is intact on GitLab and still runs via docker compose, so the work is not lost — but every citation of that wiki link now points at a dead page. A free hosting tier is a deadline, not a deployment.","body_zh":"Ladder Detector 把膠體影像的標註自動化，這是一件真的不華麗、也真的有用的工作，而 Vilnius-Lithuania 做了對的事：把它公開部署出去。他們 wiki 上的網址 ladder-detector.onrender.com 現在回傳 HTTP 503 和「This service has been suspended by its owner.」這段文字。Apache-2.0 的原始碼在 GitLab 上完好無缺，用 docker compose 依然跑得起來，所以成果沒有消失——但現在每一次引用那個 wiki 連結，指向的都是一個死掉的頁面。免費代管方案是一個期限，不是一次部署。","chips":["gone","Vilnius-Lithuania","503 suspended","source survives"],"kicker_zh":"前車之鑑"},{"kicker":"Honest about the gap","title":"Diana and HUSH publish a URL that is not the tool","title_zh":"Diana 和 HUSH 公布的網址不是工具本身","body":"UMA Malaga's live site opens with a disclaimer: \"Saved results, not the live tool... The pages cannot analyse a variant you type.\" It publishes unedited CLI output with the commit hash, Docker image digest and tool versions recorded — excellent reproducibility practice, but not a service. GU Frankfurt's HUSH page likewise says it \"shows its web app in action\" and then walks through a mockup of screenshots. Both are more honest than most, and both are exactly why a 200 response proves nothing until you read the page.","body_zh":"UMA Malaga 的線上網站一開頭就有免責聲明：「Saved results, not the live tool... The pages cannot analyse a variant you type.」它公開未經修剪的 CLI 輸出，並記下 commit 雜湊值、Docker 映像摘要和工具版本——這是極佳的可重現性實務，但不是一個服務。GU Frankfurt 的 HUSH 頁面同樣寫著它「shows its web app in action」，然後帶你走過一份由截圖組成的介面示意稿。兩者都比大多數隊伍誠實，而兩者也正好說明了為什麼在你讀過頁面之前，一個 200 回應什麼都證明不了。","chips":["source-only","UMA Malaga","GU Frankfurt","demo not deployment"],"kicker_zh":"誠實面對落差"},{"kicker":"Good code, no front door","title":"ETH-Zurich's deCISion is the best source-only release","title_zh":"ETH-Zurich 的 deCISion 是最好的純原始碼釋出","body":"The Best Software winner for Overgrad ships MIT-licensed with a web interface, a JSON API, a CLI, 28 automated tests on every push through GitLab CI, a Docker build, a CITATION.cff and a demo video. It exports FASTA, GenBank and SBOL3 and takes any .pdb or .cif structure, so it would work on someone else's data without modification. The only address on the wiki is localhost:4173. Everything needed to deploy it exists in the repository; nobody deployed it.","body_zh":"這個研究生組的最佳軟體得主以 MIT 授權釋出，附有網頁介面、JSON API、CLI、每次推送都透過 GitLab CI 執行的 28 項自動化測試、一套 Docker 建置、一份 CITATION.cff 和一支示範影片。它可以輸出 FASTA、GenBank 和 SBOL3，也接受任何 .pdb 或 .cif 結構，所以不用改動就能用在別人的資料上。但 wiki 上唯一的位址是 localhost:4173。部署所需要的一切都在儲存庫裡；沒有人去部署它。","chips":["source-only","ETH-Zurich","MIT","CI + Docker","localhost only"],"kicker_zh":"程式很好，沒有入口"},{"kicker":"Check the whole release","title":"Toronto's app is live; its dataset DOI is not","title_zh":"Toronto 的應用還活著，它的資料集 DOI 沒有","body":"PETadex at petadex.net is one of the strongest tools of the year: a sharded DIAMOND search over a 298.7M-sequence corpus, with worked examples loaded and ready to run, nothing to install. But the wiki cites a 23.8 GB Zenodo deposit at doi:10.5281/zenodo.23457986, and that DOI returns 404 — a Zenodo API search for \"petadex\" finds zero records. The interactive half survived and the archival half did not, which is the opposite of what long-term preservation is supposed to deliver.","body_zh":"petadex.net 上的 PETadex 是今年最強的工具之一：對一個 2.987 億條序列的語料做分片 DIAMOND 搜尋，範例已經載好可以直接跑，什麼都不用安裝。但 wiki 引用了一份 23.8 GB 的 Zenodo 存放紀錄 doi:10.5281/zenodo.23457986，而那個 DOI 回傳 404——用 Zenodo API 搜尋「petadex」找到零筆紀錄。互動的那一半活了下來，封存的那一半沒有，這和長期保存本該達成的目標正好相反。","chips":["alive","Toronto","petadex.net","Zenodo DOI 404"],"kicker_zh":"檢查整個釋出"}],"table":{"head":["Tool","Team","Status","Live URL / repo","Reusable on other data?"],"head_zh":["工具","隊伍","狀態","線上網址／儲存庫","可用於其他資料？"],"rows":[["AMPilot","XJTLU-Software","alive","https://ampilotlab.com","yes"],["ARGUS","GHCIS","alive","https://argus.ucuv.dpdns.org/client/","yes"],["Atlas COMPASS + EDGE","NJU-China","alive","https://www.starase-atlas.org/","partly"],["PETadex sequence search","Toronto","alive","https://petadex.net/search","yes"],["PyroForge","HK-Joint-School","alive","https://pyroforge.26650078.xyz/","yes"],["PeptiCraft","DKU","alive","https://pepticraft.pages.dev","partly"],["RADAR-Scout","Stanford University","alive","https://radar-scout.vercel.app/","partly"],["SynBase","Stanford University","alive","https://synbase.web.app/home.html","n/a (curriculum)"],["deCISion","ETH-Zurich","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/eth-zurich/decision","yes"],["OpenSplitProtein","ETH-Zurich","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/eth-zurich/opensplitprotein","yes"],["ReTIsigner","Uni-Padua-IT","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/uni-padua-it/retisigner-svelte","yes"],["RK4 solver","UPF-Barcelona","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/upf-barcelona/upf-software","yes"],["iGEMforge","UPF-Barcelona","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/upf-barcelona/upf-software","partly"],["NetFlux","MIT-MAHE","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/mit-mahe/netflux","yes"],["Diana gRNA designer","UMA Malaga","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/uma-malaga/diana-grna-designer","yes"],["HUSH","GU Frankfurt","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/gu-frankfurt/hush","yes"],["PRINCE","Lambert-GA","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/lambert-ga/prince-webapp","yes"],["catmaOS","XJTLU-China","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/xjtlu-china/software","partly"],["Bioreactor digital twin","GEMS-Taiwan","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/gems-taiwan/digital-twin","no"],["Ladder Detector","Vilnius-Lithuania","gone","ladder-detector.onrender.com (503 suspended)","yes, if self-hosted"],["CERNAL","TAU-Israel","gone","cernal.app + cernal.duckdns.org (both unresolvable)","partly, if self-hosted"],["Electrospinner (no software)","Cornell","n/a","CAD, BOM and manuals only","n/a"],["Bioreactor stack (no software)","KAUST-KSA","n/a","gitlab.igem.org/2026/kaust-ksa","n/a"]],"rows_zh":[["AMPilot","XJTLU-Software","存活","https://ampilotlab.com","是"],["ARGUS","GHCIS","存活","https://argus.ucuv.dpdns.org/client/","是"],["Atlas COMPASS + EDGE","NJU-China","存活","https://www.starase-atlas.org/","部分"],["PETadex 序列搜尋","Toronto","存活","https://petadex.net/search","是"],["PyroForge","HK-Joint-School","存活","https://pyroforge.26650078.xyz/","是"],["PeptiCraft","DKU","存活","https://pepticraft.pages.dev","部分"],["RADAR-Scout","Stanford University","存活","https://radar-scout.vercel.app/","部分"],["SynBase","Stanford University","存活","https://synbase.web.app/home.html","不適用（教學課程）"],["deCISion","ETH-Zurich","僅原始碼","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/eth-zurich/decision","是"],["OpenSplitProtein","ETH-Zurich","僅原始碼","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/eth-zurich/opensplitprotein","是"],["ReTIsigner","Uni-Padua-IT","僅原始碼","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/uni-padua-it/retisigner-svelte","是"],["RK4 求解器","UPF-Barcelona","僅原始碼","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/upf-barcelona/upf-software","是"],["iGEMforge","UPF-Barcelona","僅原始碼","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/upf-barcelona/upf-software","部分"],["NetFlux","MIT-MAHE","僅原始碼","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/mit-mahe/netflux","是"],["Diana gRNA 設計工具","UMA Malaga","僅原始碼","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/uma-malaga/diana-grna-designer","是"],["HUSH","GU Frankfurt","僅原始碼","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/gu-frankfurt/hush","是"],["PRINCE","Lambert-GA","僅原始碼","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/lambert-ga/prince-webapp","是"],["catmaOS","XJTLU-China","僅原始碼","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/xjtlu-china/software","部分"],["生物反應器數位孿生","GEMS-Taiwan","僅原始碼","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/gems-taiwan/digital-twin","否"],["Ladder Detector","Vilnius-Lithuania","已消失","ladder-detector.onrender.com（503 已停用）","是，若自行架設"],["CERNAL","TAU-Israel","已消失","cernal.app + cernal.duckdns.org（兩者都無法解析）","部分，若自行架設"],["靜電紡絲機（無軟體）","Cornell","不適用","只有 CAD、BOM 和操作手冊","不適用"],["生物反應器系統（無軟體）","KAUST-KSA","不適用","gitlab.igem.org/2026/kaust-ksa","不適用"]]},"checklist":["Buy a domain and deploy the tool publicly before the wiki freeze, not after it — every tool that is alive today was hosted on freeze day.","Put a clickable URL at the top of the software page; if the only address on the page is localhost, assume nobody outside the team will ever run it.","Let strangers in without an account — guest mode or a no-key API. CERNAL gated behind a lab login is dead; AMPilot's keyless API still answers.","Pay for hosting that outlives the free tier, and check the URL again a month after the Jamboree. Vilnius's deployment lasted weeks.","Expose a documented HTTP API with an OpenAPI spec alongside the UI, so the tool can be a step in someone else's pipeline rather than a destination.","Ship a health endpoint that returns real JSON, so anyone — including a judge or a reviewer — can prove the backend is running and not a static shell.","Accept standard inputs (FASTA, GenBank, SBML, .pdb/.cif) and export standard outputs (SBOL, GenBank, CSV); hard-wiring the tool to your own chassis caps its audience at your team.","Never present a mockup or saved output as the running tool — and if you do publish saved results, label them as plainly as UMA Malaga did.","Verify every archival DOI resolves before you cite it; Toronto's 23.8 GB Zenodo deposit 404s while the web app it supports stays up.","Recruit one outside user and record what they did. Across all 21 tools the only external-adoption number found anywhere was SynBase's 837 learners; stars and forks were zero everywhere."],"checklist_zh":["在 wiki 凍結之前就買下網域、把工具公開部署出去，不要等凍結之後——今天還活著的每一個工具，在凍結當天都已經上線代管。","把可以點擊的網址放在軟體頁面最上方；如果頁面上唯一的位址是 localhost，就假設團隊之外永遠不會有人執行它。","讓陌生人不用帳號就能進來——訪客模式，或是不需要金鑰的 API。擋在實驗室登入後面的 CERNAL 已經死了；AMPilot 不用金鑰的 API 現在還會回應。","付錢買能撐過免費方案的代管，並在 Jamboree 之後一個月再檢查一次網址。Vilnius 的部署只撐了幾週。","在使用者介面之外，再提供一個有 OpenAPI 規格、文件化的 HTTP API，讓這個工具能成為別人流程中的一步，而不只是一個終點。","提供一個會回傳真正 JSON 的健康檢查端點，讓任何人——包括評審或審查者——都能證明後端真的在跑，不是靜態空殼。","接受標準輸入（FASTA、GenBank、SBML、.pdb/.cif），並輸出標準格式（SBOL、GenBank、CSV）；把工具綁死在自己的底盤菌株上，等於把使用者上限設成自己這支隊伍。","絕不要把介面示意稿或存檔輸出當成正在運行的工具呈現——而如果你真的要公布存檔結果，就像 UMA Malaga 那樣清楚標示。","在引用任何封存 DOI 之前，先確認它解析得出來；Toronto 那份 23.8 GB 的 Zenodo 存放紀錄回傳 404，而它支撐的網頁應用還活著。","找一位團隊外的使用者，並記錄他做了什麼。21 個工具中，在任何地方找到的唯一外部採用數字是 SynBase 的 837 位學習者；star 和 fork 數到處都是零。"],"method":"Starting from the 2026 Best Software winners and nominees, the Best Software & AI winners and nominees, and the Best Model and Best Hardware winners, every tool's wiki software page was read (via curl where server-rendered, via the browser pane for client-rendered SPAs), every GitLab and GitHub repository was queried through the GitLab API for file tree, licence, stars, forks and last-commit date, and every candidate deployment was first checked with curl and then opened in a browser and read, because a 200 from an SPA catch-all route proves nothing — starase-atlas.org returns its index page for any /api path, so apparent API endpoints had to be inspected by content. Where a backend health endpoint existed it was called directly (ARGUS /api/ready, PyroForge /health, AMPilot /api/v1/corpus/search, which returned real data). A link check cannot tell you whether the science is correct, whether the tool gives sensible answers on data it has not seen, whether the maintainers intend to keep paying for hosting, or whether anyone is actually using it — zero stars and zero forks mean no public signal, not necessarily no users. Cornell and KAUST-KSA released no standalone software and are listed but excluded from the base rate; TAU-Israel, HK-Joint-School, DKU and XJTLU-Software had no local research file, so their tools were identified from their wikis directly.","method_zh":"起點是 2026 年最佳軟體的得主與入圍者、最佳軟體與 AI 的得主與入圍者，以及最佳模型與最佳硬體的得主：每一個工具的 wiki 軟體頁面都讀過（伺服器端渲染的用 curl，客戶端渲染的單頁應用則用瀏覽器面板），每一個 GitLab 和 GitHub 儲存庫都透過 GitLab API 查詢檔案樹、授權條款、star 數、fork 數和最後一次 commit 的日期，而每一個可能的部署都先用 curl 檢查、再在瀏覽器中開啟並實際閱讀，因為單頁應用萬用路由回傳的 200 什麼都證明不了——starase-atlas.org 對任何 /api 路徑都回傳它的首頁，所以看起來像 API 端點的東西必須逐一檢查內容。有後端健康檢查端點的就直接呼叫（ARGUS 的 /api/ready、PyroForge 的 /health、AMPilot 的 /api/v1/corpus/search，後者回傳了真實資料）。連結檢查無法告訴你科學是否正確、工具在沒見過的資料上是否給出合理答案、維護者是否打算繼續付代管費用，或是否真的有人在用它——零 star 和零 fork 代表沒有公開訊號，不一定代表沒有使用者。Cornell 和 KAUST-KSA 沒有釋出獨立軟體，列入表格但不計入基礎比率；TAU-Israel、HK-Joint-School、DKU 和 XJTLU-Software 沒有本地的研究檔案，他們的工具是直接從 wiki 辨識出來的。","baseRate":{"checked":21,"alive":8,"sourceOnly":11,"stub":0,"gone":2},"kicker_zh":"原創分析","order":34},{"id":"dataviz","tab":"drylab","kicker":"Original analysis","kicker_zh":"原創分析","title":"How the best teams made complex data honest, not just pretty","title_zh":"最好的團隊如何讓複雜的資料變得誠實，而不只是好看","lede":"The visualisation work that stood out in 2026 was not the most beautiful. It was the work that made it impossible to misread the data.","lede_zh":"2026 年最突出的視覺化作品不是最漂亮的，而是讓資料「無法被誤讀」的那些。","body":"Almost every 2026 wiki has charts. The ones worth studying share a single instinct: **they build the reader's doubt into the picture**.\n\nThe clearest example is **GEMS-Taiwan**'s provenance colour-coding. Its dose ledger is drawn as one top-to-bottom chain, from 1.67 mL on a 10 cm plate down to US$3,800 of capital per hectare, with a rail running down the left that is green while every row still rests on a measurement and **turns amber at the rice canopy correction** — so a reader sees exactly where measurement stops and modelling begins. Every model input is tabulated with a provenance column. **TU Delft** does the same thing in a different register, labelling every cell of its decision matrix Factual, Inferred, Estimated or Speculative, with a legend stating that the tag records the evidence and not the judgement. **BOKU-Vienna** attaches a parameter-provenance table to its interactive widget. **XJTLU-China** runs an evidence-coverage track underneath its priority profiles, so a high score sitting on thin evidence cannot be mistaken for a finding.\n\nThe second instinct is **a state that refuses to be misread**. **DKU**'s safety panel resolves to four verdicts rather than three — clear, exceeded, borderline, and *not assessed* — precisely so an unmeasured gate can never be read as a passed one; 198 of its 496 constructs carry no immunogenicity measurement, and the interface says so rather than showing a zero. It goes further: because the MHC class I predictor accepts only 5-15 residue peptides and returns zero outside that window, a stored zero is explicitly not presented as evidence of low immunogenicity. **GHCIS** ships the same idea in its colour classifier, with an explicit \"unresolved, and must not be treated as Negative\" state. **UMA Malaga** conveys status by shape and text rather than colour alone.\n\nThe third is **telling the reader how to read it**. BOKU-Vienna puts an explicit \"How to read this graph\" panel beside each one. XJTLU-China numbers eighteen model figures so they read as a single argument rather than a gallery, aligning six normalised feature tracks above a composite score so you can see which feature drove a peak.\n\nThe fourth is **captions that carry the whole experiment**. **Mingdao**'s figures are plain, and that is the point — each names the instrument (a BioTek Synergy H1 plate reader; a FORA G31 glucose meter, range 20-600 mg/dL), the buffer, the temperature, the replicate count and the error measure, links its own raw CSV by filename, and where error bars are too small to see, *the caption says so* and points at the table of values.\n\nThe fifth is **showing the absences**. **DTU-Denmark**'s interactive stakeholder map colour-codes each pin by engagement status so that non-responses stay visible, and the team names the organisations that never replied. **BNDS-China** prints a caveat directly on its influence map stating that appearing on it does not mean an interview took place.\n\nAnd a note on accessibility, because the wiki analysis found that late alt-text compliance sweeps correlate with nothing. **BAID-China** shows what doing it properly looks like instead: every chart on the wiki redrawn in the eight-colour Okabe-Ito colour-blind-safe palette, chosen for luminance separation so the figures survive greyscale, with a published colour-blindness simulation verifying that elements stay distinguishable under red-green, blue-yellow and total colour-blindness. That is a design decision taken at the start, not a checkbox at the end.\n\nInteractivity, finally, earns its place only when it lets the reader change something. **UPF-Barcelona**'s RK4 solver gives every parameter a live slider that takes effect *during* the running simulation. BOKU-Vienna's trade-off widget moves a vitamin flux against growth rate with the team's own measured points overlaid. DTU-Denmark's process-flow diagram zooms from a five-route overview into the enzymatic routes with every parameter printed on the box - acid molarity, temperature, residence time, enzyme loading, number of reuses. An animation that only plays is decoration; a control that changes the answer is an argument.","body_zh":"幾乎每一個 2026 年的 wiki 都有圖表。值得研究的那些共享同一種直覺：**他們把讀者的懷疑畫進圖裡**。\n\n最清楚的例子是 **GEMS-Taiwan** 的來源色標。他們的劑量帳本畫成一條由上而下的單一鏈條，從 10 公分培養皿上的 1.67 毫升，一路到每公頃 3,800 美元的資本支出，左側有一條軌道：只要每一列仍然立基於量測，它就是綠色，而**在水稻冠層修正那一列轉為琥珀色**——讀者因此能一眼看出量測在哪裡結束、模擬從哪裡開始。每一項模型輸入都附有來源欄位。**TU Delft** 用另一種形式做同樣的事：決策矩陣的每一格都標註為 Factual、Inferred、Estimated 或 Speculative，並附圖例說明「這個標籤記錄的是證據，不是判斷」。**BOKU-Vienna** 為互動元件附上參數來源表。**XJTLU-China** 則在優先度曲線下方加一條證據覆蓋軌，讓「高分但證據稀薄」不會被誤讀成發現。\n\n第二種直覺是**一個拒絕被誤讀的狀態**。**DKU** 的安全面板有四種判定而非三種——clear、exceeded、borderline，以及 *not assessed*——正是為了讓「未量測」永遠不會被讀成「通過」；496 個構築中有 198 個沒有免疫原性量測資料，介面就直接這麼說，而不是顯示一個 0。他們還更進一步：由於 MHC class I 預測器只接受 5-15 個胺基酸的胜肽，超出範圍一律回傳 0，因此系統明確聲明「儲存的 0 不代表低免疫原性」。**GHCIS** 在顏色判讀器中實作了同樣的概念，設有明確的「無法判定，且不得視為陰性」狀態。**UMA Malaga** 則以形狀與文字、而非單靠顏色來傳達狀態。\n\n第三種是**告訴讀者該怎麼讀**。BOKU-Vienna 在每張圖旁邊放一個明確的「如何閱讀這張圖」面板。XJTLU-China 把十八張模型圖編號，使它們讀起來像一條完整論證而不是圖庫，並把六條標準化特徵軌對齊疊在綜合分數之上，讓人看得出是哪一項特徵推高了峰值。\n\n第四種是**讓圖說承載整個實驗**。**Mingdao** 的圖很樸素，而這正是重點——每張圖都標明儀器（BioTek Synergy H1 盤式判讀儀；FORA G31 血糖儀，量測範圍 20-600 mg/dL）、緩衝液、溫度、重複次數與誤差量度，並以檔名連結自己的原始 CSV；當誤差棒小到看不見時，*圖說會直接寫出來*，並指向數值表。\n\n第五種是**把「缺席」顯示出來**。**DTU-Denmark** 的互動式利害關係人地圖依接觸狀態為每個圖釘上色，讓未回覆者保持可見，團隊還點名了從未回信的機構。**BNDS-China** 則把警語直接印在影響力地圖上：出現在圖上並不代表訪談真的發生過。\n\n最後談無障礙，因為 wiki 分析發現「最後才補的替代文字」與得獎毫無相關。**BAID-China** 示範了真正做對是什麼樣子：wiki 上每一張圖都以八色 Okabe-Ito 色盲友善色票重繪，選色依據是亮度差異足以在灰階下仍可辨識，並公開了一份色盲模擬圖，驗證元素在紅綠、藍黃與全色盲模擬下仍可區分。那是一開始就做的設計決定，不是最後補打的勾。\n\n最後，互動性只有在「讓讀者能改變某個東西」時才站得住腳。**UPF-Barcelona** 的 RK4 solver 為每個參數配上即時滑桿，而且在模擬*執行中*就會生效。BOKU-Vienna 的權衡元件讓維生素通量對生長速率移動，並疊上團隊自己量到的點。DTU-Denmark 的流程圖可從五條路線的總覽放大到酵素路線，每個方塊上都印著參數——酸莫耳濃度、溫度、停留時間、酵素添加量、重複使用次數。只會播放的動畫是裝飾；能改變答案的控制項才是論證。","cards":[{"kicker":"The device worth stealing","kicker_zh":"值得借用的裝置","title":"Colour the rail where measurement stops","title_zh":"在量測終止之處替軌道換色","body":"GEMS-Taiwan draws its dose ledger as one chain from 1.67 mL on a plate to US$3,800 per hectare, with a rail down the left that is green while each row rests on a measurement and turns amber at the rice canopy correction. Anyone can see where the evidence ends. TU Delft does the same with Factual / Inferred / Estimated / Speculative tags on every cell of its decision matrix.","body_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 把劑量帳本畫成一條鏈：從培養皿上的 1.67 毫升到每公頃 3,800 美元，左側軌道在每列仍立基於量測時保持綠色，到水稻冠層修正那一列轉為琥珀色。任何人都看得出證據在哪裡結束。TU Delft 用另一種方式做同一件事：在決策矩陣的每一格標上 Factual / Inferred / Estimated / Speculative。","chips":["provenance made visible"]},{"kicker":"The device worth stealing","kicker_zh":"值得借用的裝置","title":"Give \"not assessed\" its own state","title_zh":"給「未評估」一個自己的狀態","body":"DKU's safety panel resolves to clear, exceeded, borderline and not assessed — four verdicts, so an unmeasured gate can never read as a passed one. 198 of its 496 constructs have no immunogenicity measurement and the interface says so instead of showing a zero. GHCIS ships the same idea as \"unresolved, and must not be treated as Negative\".","body_zh":"DKU 的安全面板有四種判定：clear、exceeded、borderline、not assessed——四種，因此「未量測」永遠不會被讀成「通過」。496 個構築中有 198 個沒有免疫原性量測，介面就直接說明，而不是顯示 0。GHCIS 以「無法判定，且不得視為陰性」實作了同樣的概念。","chips":["198 of 496 say so"]},{"kicker":"The device worth stealing","kicker_zh":"值得借用的裝置","title":"Put the whole experiment in the caption","title_zh":"把整個實驗寫進圖說","body":"Mingdao's figures are plain and rigorous. Each names the instrument, the buffer, the temperature, the replicate count and the error measure, and links its own raw CSV by filename. Where the error bars are too small to see, the caption says so and points at the table of values. A figure a reader can audit beats a figure a reader can admire.","body_zh":"Mingdao 的圖樸素而嚴謹。每張圖都標明儀器、緩衝液、溫度、重複次數與誤差量度，並以檔名連結自己的原始 CSV。當誤差棒小到看不見，圖說會直接寫明並指向數值表。一張讀者能稽核的圖，勝過一張讀者只能讚嘆的圖。","chips":["instrument · buffer · n · error","raw CSV linked"]},{"kicker":"The device worth stealing","kicker_zh":"值得借用的裝置","title":"Show who did not reply","title_zh":"把沒有回覆的人也畫出來","body":"DTU-Denmark colour-codes every pin on its stakeholder map by engagement status, so non-responses stay visible, and names the organisations that never answered. BNDS-China prints the caveat on its influence map that appearing there does not mean an interview happened. A map with no gaps is a map that has been tidied.","body_zh":"DTU-Denmark 依接觸狀態為利害關係人地圖上的每個圖釘上色，讓未回覆者保持可見，並點名從未回信的機構。BNDS-China 則把警語印在影響力地圖上：出現在圖上不代表訪談真的發生過。一張沒有空缺的地圖，是一張被整理過的地圖。","chips":["non-responses stay visible"]},{"kicker":"Accessibility, done early","kicker_zh":"及早處理的無障礙","title":"BAID-China redrew every chart in a colour-blind-safe palette","title_zh":"BAID-China 用色盲友善色票重繪了每一張圖","body":"The eight-colour Okabe-Ito palette, chosen for luminance separation so the figures survive greyscale, with a published colour-blindness simulation verifying that elements stay distinguishable under red-green, blue-yellow and total colour-blindness. The wiki analysis found late alt-text sweeps correlate with nothing; this is the alternative — a decision taken at the start.","body_zh":"採用八色 Okabe-Ito 色票，選色依據是亮度差異足以讓圖在灰階下仍可辨識，並公開色盲模擬圖驗證元素在紅綠、藍黃與全色盲模擬下仍可區分。wiki 分析發現最後才補的替代文字與得獎毫無相關；這就是替代方案——一個在一開始就做的決定。","chips":["Okabe-Ito","simulation published"]},{"kicker":"For GEMS","kicker_zh":"給 GEMS","title":"Interactivity only counts if the reader can change the answer","title_zh":"互動只有在讀者能改變答案時才算數","body":"UPF-Barcelona gives every parameter a live slider that takes effect during the running simulation. BOKU-Vienna moves vitamin flux against growth rate with the team's own measured points overlaid and a \"How to read this graph\" panel beside it. DTU prints every parameter on the box of a zoomable process diagram. An animation that only plays is decoration.","body_zh":"UPF-Barcelona 為每個參數配上即時滑桿，而且在模擬執行中就會生效。BOKU-Vienna 讓維生素通量對生長速率移動，疊上團隊自己量到的點，旁邊還附「如何閱讀這張圖」面板。DTU 在可縮放流程圖的每個方塊上都印出參數。只會播放的動畫是裝飾。","chips":["sliders during the run","How to read this graph"]}],"method":"Drawn from the dataviz field of every team file in this report, each researched from the team's own 2026 wiki. Interactive behaviour is as the analysts described it after opening the pages; we have not re-tested every widget here. The examples are chosen because they illustrate a transferable device, not because they are the only teams doing good work. GEMS-Taiwan is the report author's own team and appears on the same terms as the rest.","method_zh":"資料取自本報告每一份團隊檔案的 dataviz 欄位，皆來自各隊自己的 2026 wiki。互動行為依分析員實際開啟頁面後的描述記錄，我們並未在此重新測試每一個元件。所舉案例是因為它們示範了一個可移植的手法而被選出，並非表示只有這些團隊做得好。GEMS-Taiwan 是本報告作者自己的團隊，與其他隊伍適用相同標準。","order":36},{"id":"ihp-by-village","tab":"good","order":36,"kicker":"Original analysis","kicker_zh":"原創分析","title":"The experts-only pattern is not about medicine. It is about who operates the thing.","title_zh":"「只有專家」的現象與醫學無關，而與「誰在操作那個東西」有關","lede":"The obvious hypothesis — that therapeutics teams talk to clinicians because they have to, while agriculture and bioremediation teams get real knowledge from farmers and residents — does not survive the counting. Medical villages closed 6 of 21 loops with a non-expert; land, water and food villages closed 8 of 24. The gap that is real is a different one, and it is wide.","lede_zh":"最直覺的假說——治療類隊伍只能找臨床醫師，而農業與生物復育類隊伍則能從農民和居民身上得到真知識——在實際清點後站不住腳。醫學類村落在 21 個閉合迴路中有 6 個由非專家閉上；土地、水與食物類村落則是 24 個中有 8 個。真正存在的差距是另一條線，而且相當大。","body":"Across the 106 decorated teams on file, 71 closed a stakeholder-to-design loop and 16 of those 71 closed at least one with a non-expert — a farmer, beekeeper, patient, resident, frontline worker, vendor, artisan or volunteer rather than a professor, clinician, regulator, company scientist or official. Sorted by village, the medical/agricultural split the hypothesis predicted is almost flat. **Therapeutics** is 5 of 12, a higher rate than **Bioremediation** at 1 of 8. **Conservation** is 2 of 8 and **Food & Nutrition** 2 of 4. Only **Agriculture**, at 3 of 4, behaves as predicted, and four closed loops cannot carry an inference on their own. Reported honestly: the hypothesis as stated is wrong, and the earlier *ihp-depth* finding that nearly every loop is expert-closed holds inside every large village without exception.\n\nWhat the table does show is a split the hypothesis did not anticipate, and it is not close. The **platform villages** — Foundational Advance, Biomanufacturing, Space, Software & AI, Fashion & Cosmetics — closed 26 loops and 2 of them involved a non-expert. Foundational Advance is 0 of 8, Space 0 of 3, Software & AI 0 of 1, Biomanufacturing 1 of 11. The **applied villages**, medical and agricultural together, closed 45 loops with 14 non-expert among them. Where a project has no identifiable person downstream of it this year, nobody outside the lab closes a loop, and no amount of survey work substitutes: Heidelberg, Marburg, Princeton, ETH-Zurich, Vilnius, William-and-Mary and XJTLU-China are all score-4 teams whose every consequential input came from somebody with a doctorate.\n\nThe structural reason, where the files support one, is not the village but **who physically operates the thing being changed**. Compare the two villages the hypothesis treated as equivalent. An Agriculture or Conservation deployment ends in a hive, a plot or a market stall that a beekeeper, a grower or a vendor runs with their own hands, so the operator *is* the non-expert and the loop closes through them. A Bioremediation deployment ends inside a wastewater plant, a refinery or a biodiesel works, where the operator is a process engineer with a degree — ABOA's loop closed through the Turku plant's process engineer, UOttawa's through a sulfur-recovery engineer of thirty-three years, Madrid-UCM's through Bio-Oils Huelva and Repsol, Wageningen's through Vitens and Aqualab Zuid. The residents the hypothesis imagined are present in those files and they do change something, but they change communication: Madrid-UCM's Inmaculada Alonso, who had watched a reservoir eutrophy for decades, moved the team toward perceptible restoration outcomes and clearer explanation; UZurich's residents below the slopes made ecological cost something to investigate. Twelve of the 71 teams that closed a loop have a documented non-expert input of exactly that kind — real, named, and stopping short of the build. That is the same vocabulary-not-vector result the earlier analysis found, now located precisely: it happens wherever the public lives *near* the deployment instead of *running* it.\n\nThe best non-expert loops are worth naming because they are all the same shape. **Athens** states that two conditions were fixed before any construct was designed — the protein must reach the brood, and it must survive the larval gut — and says plainly that neither would have come from a literature search; beekeeper Peter Kasztelewicz's gentler practice (requeening, partial clean-out) is why delivery moved from spray to feed, and the team published what that cost. **HongKong-JSS** replaced a 14-channel colour sensor with a wavelength-resolved spectrometer because Koo's Farm and wet-market vendors wanted a number, then replaced syringe delivery with pump dosing after users complained about the force needed, measuring the result as a fall from 7.41 to 1.95 per cent coefficient of variation. **Hongwen School** got the handling cost of wet spent grain (70-80 RMB per tonne, driven by leachate, odour and liner) from Master He, a municipal landfill worker of six years, and turned localised processing from a preference into a hard constraint; separately Mr Shen of a Chongming ecological farm said 'I never look at the price per ton — I look at the cost per kilogram of gain', and the feed route became a standardised premix judged on feed conversion ratio. **LYON** removed every living cell from its filter because the public objected, and ruled households out as customers entirely. **QingdaoAcademy** put ultrafiltration desalting and endotoxin limits into its plan because a beauty-salon manager said she would hesitate to trust Qingdao Ulva. **TAU-Israel** is the medical exception that proves the rule: Shir Parchef's eighteen-year wait for an endometriosis diagnosis and Netta Ben Moshe's being told that incapacitating pain was ordinary cramps set the goal as eliminating pathology without systemic hormonal ablation — patients setting a constraint on the mechanism, not on the wording.\n\nTwo cautions against over-reading. First, the non-expert loops cluster not only by operator role but by **what kind of change they produce**: of the 16, ten changed something physical — a sensor, a delivery route, a formulation, a containment architecture — and six changed only deployment scope, target user or a selection criterion. Oxford is in the second group: about twenty chemical-free hobbyists of the Oxfordshire Natural Beekeeping Group argued against the entire premise, and Oxford's response was to narrow the target user to commercial operations and write that they had changed 'not the molecular mechanism of NECTAR, but the problem we believed NECTAR should — and should not — try to solve'. That is honest and it is real, but it is not the same act as changing a part. Second, legibility may be doing some of the work the villages appear to do: a judge can verify that a professor said something, and several teams that did consult non-experts recorded the result as an honest null. **IISER-Kolkata** asked Mr Mohadep Dutta, who has fished the Ganga since he was seven, about a shift in fish sex ratio, and published that he could not see one — evidence the effect needs instrumentation, rather than a loop. **Stanford University**, Grand Prize winner in Therapeutics, looked for keloid patient groups, found almost none, was told by the one that replied to talk to clinicians instead, and states outright that physicians cannot stand in for lived experience. Those two entries are better practice than most of the surveys in the cohort and they close nothing.\n\nFor an agriculture-adjacent team the operational reading is narrow and uncomfortable. The teams worth copying are not the Best IHP winners as a class — **TU Delft**, **UCAS-China** and **GEMS-Taiwan** all won and all had their architecture set by credentialled experts. **GEMS-Taiwan** should be held to its own standard here: sensing moving out of the cell, the hollow-fibre perfusion reactor, the abandonment of proline delivery, the narrowing to heat and salinity, the WB800 strain and the shift from continuous to periodic operation were closed by Prof. Chen Wen-Liang, Dr. Paul Verslues, Dr. Elizabeth Sattely, Prof. Huang Chieh-Chen and CH Biotech. The only non-expert input that reached the design was the natural-farming forum of 5 September, whose argument that a crop protected from every stress never builds tolerance became the specification for the release threshold, and a farmer's question about organic certification, which bounded the market rather than the machine. **Muenster-University**, nominated for Best Agriculture, reached farmers through the WLV agricultural association and changed its education strategy. That is the default outcome for an agriculture team that talks to farmers, and avoiding it takes a deliberate act: put the device in the hand of the person who will hold it, and ask for a number.","body_zh":"在檔案中的 106 支受獎隊伍裡，有 71 支閉合了一條從利害關係人到設計的迴路，而這 71 支中有 16 支至少有一條迴路是由非專家閉上的——農民、養蜂人、病人、居民、第一線工人、攤商、工匠或志工，而不是教授、臨床醫師、主管機關人員、企業科學家或官員。依村落分類之後，假說預測的「醫學 vs 農業」分界幾乎是平的。**Therapeutics** 是 12 中有 5，比例反而高於 **Bioremediation** 的 8 中有 1。**Conservation** 是 8 中有 2，**Food & Nutrition** 是 4 中有 2。只有 **Agriculture** 的 4 中有 3 符合預測，而四條閉合迴路本身撐不起任何推論。誠實地說：這個假說如其所述是錯的，而先前 *ihp-depth* 所說「幾乎每一條迴路都由專家閉上」的結論，在每一個樣本量夠大的村落裡都毫無例外地成立。\n\n這張表真正顯示的，是假說沒有預期到的另一條分界，而且差距不小。**平台型村落**——Foundational Advance、Biomanufacturing、Space、Software & AI、Fashion & Cosmetics——共閉合 26 條迴路，其中只有 2 條牽涉非專家。Foundational Advance 是 8 中有 0，Space 3 中有 0，Software & AI 1 中有 0，Biomanufacturing 11 中有 1。**應用型村落**（醫學與農業合計）閉合了 45 條迴路，其中 14 條有非專家參與。當一個專案在今年還沒有可指認的下游使用者時，實驗室外就沒有人會閉上迴路，而再多的問卷也替代不了：Heidelberg、Marburg、Princeton、ETH-Zurich、Vilnius、William-and-Mary 與 XJTLU-China 全是 4 分隊伍，而他們每一項有後果的輸入都來自擁有博士學位的人。\n\n在檔案支持得了結論的範圍內，結構性原因不是村落，而是**誰用手在操作那個被改動的東西**。拿假說視為同類的兩個村落來比。Agriculture 或 Conservation 的部署最後落在一個蜂箱、一塊田或一個市場攤位上，由養蜂人、農友或攤商親手操作，因此操作者本身*就是*那位非專家，迴路也就經由他們閉合。Bioremediation 的部署則落在污水處理廠、煉油廠或生質柴油廠內部，操作者是有學位的製程工程師——ABOA 的迴路經由 Turku 廠的製程工程師閉合，UOttawa 經由一位有 33 年資歷的硫回收工程師，Madrid-UCM 經由 Bio-Oils Huelva 與 Repsol，Wageningen 經由 Vitens 與 Aqualab Zuid。假說想像的那些居民確實出現在這些檔案裡，也確實改變了某些東西，但他們改變的是溝通：Madrid-UCM 的 Inmaculada Alonso 看著一座水庫優養化數十年，她讓隊伍轉向「看得見的復原成果」與更清楚的說明；UZurich 坡下的居民讓生態代價從預設變成待查事項。在 71 支閉合迴路的隊伍中，有 12 支記錄了正是這一類的非專家輸入——真實、具名，而且止步於設計之前。這就是先前分析所說的「改變用詞、不改變方向」，如今可以被精確定位：它發生在公眾住在部署地*附近*、而不是*操作*它的時候。\n\n最好的那幾條非專家迴路值得點名，因為它們形狀相同。**Athens** 寫明有兩項條件在任何構築設計之前就已固定——蛋白質必須抵達幼蟲巢房，而且必須在幼蟲腸道中存活——並直言這兩點都不會從文獻檢索中得出；養蜂人 Peter Kasztelewicz 較溫和的作法（換王、局部清巢）正是投遞方式從噴灑改為飼餵的原因，而隊伍也公開寫出了這個選擇的代價。**HongKong-JSS** 把 14 通道的顏色感測器換成波長解析的光譜儀，因為 Koo's Farm 與傳統市場攤商要的是一個數字；接著在使用者抱怨推針太費力之後，把針筒加樣改為泵驅動定量加樣，並以變異係數從 7.41% 降到 1.95% 來量測成果。**Hongwen School** 從有六年資歷的市政掩埋場工人 Master He 那裡得到濕啤酒糟的處理成本（每公噸 70-80 人民幣，由滲出水、異味與底層襯墊驅動），並把在地化處理從商業偏好升格為硬性限制；另外，崇明一家生態農場的 Mr Shen 說「我從來不看每噸的價格，我看的是每公斤增重的成本」，於是飼料路線變成一包可直接倒進既有攪拌機的標準化預混料，並以飼料換肉率作為評判標準。**LYON** 因為公眾反對，把濾材裡所有活細胞全部移除，並徹底排除家戶作為客戶。**QingdaoAcademy** 把超濾脫鹽與內毒素上限寫進計畫，因為一位美容沙龍經理說她不敢信任青島的石蓴原料。**TAU-Israel** 則是醫學類中那個反證：Shir Parchef 為子宮內膜異位症的診斷等了 18 年，Netta Ben Moshe 被告知劇烈疼痛只是普通經痛——這些讓隊伍把目標設定為「消除病灶而非掩蓋症狀，且不進行全身性荷爾蒙抑制」。這是病人替機制設下限制，而不是替用詞設下限制。\n\n有兩點要提防過度解讀。第一，這些非專家迴路不只依操作者角色分群，也依**它們造成什麼樣的改變**分群：16 條之中，有 10 條改了某個實體的東西——一顆感測器、一條投遞路徑、一種劑型、一套圍堵架構——另外 6 條只改了部署範圍、目標使用者或選擇判準。Oxford 屬於第二群：Oxfordshire Natural Beekeeping Group 約二十位不用藥的業餘養蜂人，反對的是整個前提；Oxford 的回應是把目標使用者收窄到商業蜂場，並寫下他們改變的「不是 NECTAR 的分子機制，而是我們認為 NECTAR 應該、以及不應該去解決的問題」。這很誠實、也很真實，但它和改掉一個元件並不是同一件事。第二，「可被辨識」這件事，可能正在做一部分看起來像是村落在做的工：評審可以查證一位教授說過什麼，而好幾支確實諮詢過非專家的隊伍，把結果記成了一個誠實的空值。**IISER-Kolkata** 問過七歲起就在恆河捕魚的 Mr Mohadep Dutta 有沒有看到魚類性別比例的變化，並公開記下他看不出來這件事——那是「此效應需要儀器才看得見」的證據，而不是一條迴路。**Stanford University** 身為 Therapeutics 的大獎得主，去找蟹足腫病友團體，幾乎找不到，唯一回覆的基金會叫他們去找臨床醫師，而隊伍直白寫下醫師無法代替親身經驗。這兩筆記錄比全體隊伍中大多數的問卷都更接近好的做法，而它們什麼迴路也沒閉上。\n\n對一支與農業相關的隊伍而言，可操作的結論既狹窄又不舒服。值得複製的不是「最佳整合式人類實踐得獎者」這個類別——**TU Delft**、**UCAS-China** 與 **GEMS-Taiwan** 都得了獎，而三者的架構都由有專業資歷的專家定下。**GEMS-Taiwan** 在這裡應當用同一把尺來量：感測移出細胞之外、中空纖維灌流生物反應器、放棄脯胺酸投遞、把植物測試收窄到高溫與鹽分、WB800 菌株，以及反應器從連續改為週期操作，分別是由 Chen Wen-Liang 教授、Dr. Paul Verslues、Dr. Elizabeth Sattely、Huang Chieh-Chen 教授與 CH Biotech 閉上的。唯一真正進到設計裡的非專家輸入，是 9 月 5 日的自然農法公開論壇——「一株被保護到完全沒有逆境的作物永遠不會建立耐受性」成了釋放閾值的規格依據——以及一位農民關於有機驗證的提問，而那限定的是市場，不是機器。**Muenster-University** 入圍最佳農業專案，透過 WLV 農業協會接觸到農民，然後改了教育策略。對一支去找農民談話的農業隊伍來說，那就是預設結果；要避開它需要一個刻意的動作：把裝置放進那個將要握著它的人手裡，然後向他要一個數字。","cards":[{"kicker":"The result","kicker_zh":"結果","title":"A negative result, stated plainly","title_zh":"一個直說的否定結果","body":"The hypothesis was that the experts-only pattern is worst where the stakes are most medical and best where non-specialists hold decisive practical knowledge. It does not hold. Medical villages (Therapeutics, Diagnostics, Oncology, Infectious Diseases) closed 21 loops with 6 non-expert among them, 29 per cent. Land, water and food villages (Agriculture, Bioremediation, Conservation, Food & Nutrition) closed 24 loops with 8 non-expert, 33 per cent. Four percentage points is not a pattern. Bioremediation, the village singled out for residents near contaminated sites, is the weakest applied village at 1 of 8.","body_zh":"原本的假說是：「只有專家」的現象在醫學風險最高處最嚴重，在非專家握有決定性實務知識之處最輕。這不成立。醫學類村落（Therapeutics、Diagnostics、Oncology、Infectious Diseases）閉合 21 條迴路，其中 6 條由非專家閉上，佔 29%。土地、水與食物類村落（Agriculture、Bioremediation、Conservation、Food & Nutrition）閉合 24 條，其中 8 條，佔 33%。四個百分點不構成一種型態。而被特別點名「污染場址附近居民」的 Bioremediation，反而是應用型村落中最弱的一個：8 中有 1。","chips":["106 teams","71 closed a loop","16 with a non-expert","Hypothesis fails"]},{"kicker":"The split that is real","kicker_zh":"真正存在的分界","title":"Platform villages have nobody downstream","title_zh":"平台型村落的下游沒有人","body":"Foundational Advance 0 of 8, Space 0 of 3, Software & AI 0 of 1, Biomanufacturing 1 of 11, Fashion & Cosmetics 1 of 3. The five platform villages between them closed 26 loops and 2 involved a non-expert, against 14 of 45 across the applied villages. This is not a failure of effort - Heidelberg, Marburg, Princeton and ETH-Zurich ran some of the most traceable chains in the cohort. It is that a tool with no named user this year has no lay stakeholder to be wrong in front of. For a team whose project is a platform, the honest move is Uni-Padua-IT's: take the hardware manual to an instrumentation professor and weaken your own claim.","body_zh":"Foundational Advance 8 中 0、Space 3 中 0、Software & AI 1 中 0、Biomanufacturing 11 中 1、Fashion & Cosmetics 3 中 1。五個平台型村落合計閉合 26 條迴路，只有 2 條牽涉非專家；應用型村落則是 45 條中有 14 條。這不是努力不足——Heidelberg、Marburg、Princeton 與 ETH-Zurich 跑出了全體中最可追溯的幾條鏈。原因是：一個今年還沒有具名使用者的工具，也就沒有一位外行的利害關係人可以在他面前出錯。對專案本身就是平台的隊伍而言，誠實的做法是 Uni-Padua-IT 的做法：把硬體手冊拿去給儀器專業的教授看，然後把自己的主張講弱一點。","chips":["Platform: 2 of 26","Applied: 14 of 45","Not an effort gap"]},{"kicker":"Worked example","kicker_zh":"實例","title":"Two conditions, fixed before any construct was designed","title_zh":"兩項條件，在任何構築設計之前就已固定","body":"Athens writes that the requirements for ApiconIASIS came from beekeeping, not from the team: the protein must reach the brood, and it must survive the larval gut. Neither, they say, would have been prioritised from a literature search, and both now define what counts as success. Beekeeper Peter Kasztelewicz, whose own hive footage is on the wiki, worked by requeening and partial clean-out, and that practice is why delivery moved from spray to feed - the adjuvant surfactants harm bees, and separately the person holding the sprayer inhales it, so protective equipment went into the protocols and not into the product. They then chose a purified non-replicating enzyme over a live phage knowing it is weaker and more expensive.","body_zh":"Athens 寫道，ApiconIASIS 的需求來自養蜂實務，而不是來自隊伍本身：蛋白質必須抵達幼蟲巢房，而且必須在幼蟲腸道中存活。他們說這兩點都不會在文獻檢索中被列為優先，而現在它們定義了什麼叫做成功。養蜂人 Peter Kasztelewicz 的蜂箱影像就放在 wiki 上，他採用換王與局部清巢的作法，而正是這套實務讓投遞方式從噴灑改成飼餵——佐劑中的界面活性劑會傷害蜜蜂，而另一個獨立的風險是拿噴霧器的人會吸入它，所以防護裝備被寫進操作流程、而不是寫進產品。他們接著明知較弱也較貴，仍選擇純化的非複製型酵素而非活噬菌體。","chips":["Athens","Conservation","Beekeeper set success","Spray to feed"]},{"kicker":"Worked example","kicker_zh":"實例","title":"The man who knew what a tonne actually costs","title_zh":"知道一公噸真正成本的那個人","body":"Hongwen School's register of changes is specific, attributed and sometimes negative. Master He, a municipal landfill worker of six years, gave them 60-90 tonnes a month at nearly 80 per cent moisture and handling costs of 70-80 RMB per tonne driven by leachate, odour, liner and labour, persisting not from indifference but from absent local off-takers. The team deleted both of its extreme narratives, fixed 70-80 RMB per tonne as a local baseline, and upgraded localised processing from a business preference to a hard environmental constraint, because a route relying on high-energy drying or long-haul transport would eat its own gains. Separately Mr Shen of a Chongming ecological farm reframed the unit of account - cost per kilogram of gain, not price per tonne - and the feed route became a standardised premix pourable into an existing mixer, judged on feed conversion ratio, diarrhoea rate and mortality.","body_zh":"Hongwen School 的改變清單具體、具名，有時還是負面的。市政掩埋場工人 Master He 有六年資歷，他給出的數字是每月 60-90 公噸、含水率將近 80%，處理成本每公噸 70-80 人民幣，由滲出水、異味、底層襯墊與人力構成；而這個問題持續存在不是因為大家不在乎，而是因為在地沒有接手者。隊伍刪掉了自己兩套極端敘事，把每公噸 70-80 人民幣定為在地基準，並把在地化處理從商業偏好升格為硬性環境限制——因為依賴高耗能乾燥或長程運輸的路線會把自己的效益吃光。另外，崇明一家生態農場的 Mr Shen 重新定義了計價單位：不是每公噸的價格，而是每公斤增重的成本；於是飼料路線變成可直接倒進既有攪拌機的標準化預混料，並以飼料換肉率、腹瀉率與死亡率來評判。","chips":["Hongwen School","Food & Nutrition","Landfill worker","Farm owner"]},{"kicker":"Held to the same standard","kicker_zh":"用同一把尺來量","title":"GEMS-Taiwan's architecture was closed by professors","title_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 的架構是由教授閉上的","body":"GEMS-Taiwan won Best Integrated Human Practices in the high-school section on an agricultural project, and on this measure it sits with the majority rather than the exceptions. Sensing moving out of the cell and the hollow-fibre perfusion reactor came from Prof. Chen Wen-Liang on 10 April; abandoning proline delivery from Dr. Paul Verslues; narrowing to heat and salinity from Dr. Elizabeth Sattely; the WB800 strain and periodic rather than continuous operation from Prof. Huang Chieh-Chen; the costing and regulatory work from CH Biotech. The one non-expert input that reached the design is the natural-farming forum of 5 September, where the argument that a crop protected from every stress never builds tolerance became the specification for the release threshold, and a farmer's question about organic certification that bounded the market rather than the machine. The Ghanaian farmers who supplied the origin question have no documented design consequence.","body_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 以一個農業專案拿下高中組 Best Integrated Human Practices，而在這個指標上，它站在多數那一邊，不是例外那一邊。感測移出細胞之外與中空纖維灌流生物反應器來自 4 月 10 日的 Chen Wen-Liang 教授；放棄脯胺酸投遞來自 Dr. Paul Verslues；把範圍收窄到高溫與鹽分來自 Dr. Elizabeth Sattely；WB800 菌株與反應器改為週期操作來自 Huang Chieh-Chen 教授；成本與法規工作來自 CH Biotech。唯一進到設計裡的非專家輸入，是 9 月 5 日的自然農法論壇——「一株被保護到完全沒有逆境的作物永遠不會建立耐受性」成了釋放閾值的規格依據——以及一位農民關於有機驗證的提問，而那限定的是市場、不是機器。至於提供了最初問題的迦納農民，檔案中沒有記錄任何設計後果。","chips":["GEMS-Taiwan","Agriculture","Best IHP winner","1 non-expert loop"]}],"table":{"head":["Village","Decorated teams","Closed a loop","Closed it with a non-expert"],"head_zh":["村落","受獎隊伍數","閉合了迴路","由非專家閉上"],"rows":[["Therapeutics","16","12 of 16","5 of 12"],["Biomanufacturing","13","11 of 13","1 of 11"],["Bioremediation","13","8 of 13","1 of 8"],["Foundational Advance","13","8 of 13","0 of 8"],["Diagnostics","11","7 of 11","1 of 7"],["Conservation","9","8 of 9","2 of 8"],["Food & Nutrition","8","4 of 8","2 of 4 - cell too small"],["Fashion & Cosmetics","7","3 of 7","1 of 3 - cell too small"],["Agriculture","5","4 of 5","3 of 4 - cell too small"],["Space","4","3 of 4","0 of 3 - cell too small"],["Software & AI","3","1 of 3","0 of 1 - cell too small"],["Infectious Diseases","2","1 of 2","0 of 1 - cell too small"],["Oncology","2","1 of 2","0 of 1 - cell too small"],["Medical villages combined","31","21 of 31","6 of 21"],["Land, water and food combined","35","24 of 35","8 of 24"],["Platform villages combined","40","26 of 40","2 of 26"],["All villages","106","71 of 106","16 of 71"]],"rows_zh":[["治療 Therapeutics","16","16 中有 12","12 中有 5"],["生物製造 Biomanufacturing","13","13 中有 11","11 中有 1"],["生物復育 Bioremediation","13","13 中有 8","8 中有 1"],["基礎推進 Foundational Advance","13","13 中有 8","8 中有 0"],["診斷 Diagnostics","11","11 中有 7","7 中有 1"],["保育 Conservation","9","9 中有 8","8 中有 2"],["食品與營養 Food & Nutrition","8","8 中有 4","4 中有 2－樣本過小"],["時尚與美妝 Fashion & Cosmetics","7","7 中有 3","3 中有 1－樣本過小"],["農業 Agriculture","5","5 中有 4","4 中有 3－樣本過小"],["太空 Space","4","4 中有 3","3 中有 0－樣本過小"],["軟體與 AI Software & AI","3","3 中有 1","1 中有 0－樣本過小"],["傳染病 Infectious Diseases","2","2 中有 1","1 中有 0－樣本過小"],["腫瘤 Oncology","2","2 中有 1","1 中有 0－樣本過小"],["醫學類村落合計","31","31 中有 21","21 中有 6"],["土地、水與食物類合計","35","35 中有 24","24 中有 8"],["平台型村落合計","40","40 中有 26","26 中有 2"],["全部村落","106","106 中有 71","71 中有 16"]]},"checklist":["Ask who will physically hold the device or run the process on the day it is used. If that person has a degree in your field, your non-expert loop will not happen by accident.","Make the non-expert ask for a number. HongKong-JSS's sensor swap and Hongwen School's 70-80 RMB per tonne both started as a quantity somebody named out loud.","Fix one or two success conditions from practice before the construct is designed, as Athens did, and write down that they did not come from the literature.","Recruit the people who disagree with the premise. Oxford's twenty chemical-free hobbyists narrowed the target user; GEMS-Taiwan's natural-farming forum set the release threshold.","Record non-expert input that changed nothing, and say so. IISER-Kolkata published a fisher who could not see the effect; Stanford published that it could not find patients. Both are better than a survey that only changed a word.","Check the type of change before claiming a loop: a part number, a concentration, a format, a delivery route or who may buy it counts. A changed word, a new leaflet or a reframed slogan does not."],"checklist_zh":["問清楚：產品真正被使用的那一天，是誰用手拿著裝置、或是誰在操作那套製程。如果那個人在你的領域裡有學位，你的非專家迴路就不會自己發生。","讓非專家開口要一個數字。HongKong-JSS 換感測器、Hongwen School 的每公噸 70-80 人民幣，都是從某個人說出口的量值開始的。","在構築設計之前，就從實務裡定下一到兩項成功條件，像 Athens 那樣，並寫明這些條件不是從文獻來的。","去找那些不同意前提的人。Oxford 那二十位不用藥的業餘養蜂人收窄了目標使用者；GEMS-Taiwan 的自然農法論壇定下了釋放閾值。","把沒有造成任何改變的非專家輸入也記下來，並直說。IISER-Kolkata 公開記下一位看不出效應的漁民；Stanford 公開寫下他們找不到病友。兩者都比一份只改了一個用詞的問卷更好。","宣稱閉合迴路之前，先檢查改變的類型：元件型號、濃度、劑型、投遞路徑，或誰可以購買，這些算數。改掉一個用詞、做一張新傳單、換一句標語，不算。"],"method":"Population: all 106 team files on disk, every one of them a Top 10 or special-prize winner or nominee, so this is the most decorated tenth of iGEM 2026 and not a sample of the competition. Loop scores: the 93 teams scored in the earlier ihp-depth analysis keep that analysis's score unchanged, and 'closed a loop' means its score of 4 - a named stakeholder, a specific thing said, and a change to the build, deployment, readout, safety design or business model. Thirteen files landed after that scoring ran (BASIS-China, BGI-College, Bist-China, Michigan, NCKU-Tainan, NU Boston, Squirrel-Beijing, TU Darmstadt, Tsinghua-T, UBC-Vancouver, UiOslo-Norway, WHU-China, XJTLU-Software); I scored those thirteen myself on the same rubric and seven reached 4, so 71 of 106 against the earlier 64 of 93. Non-expert rule, written before classifying: a person counts as a NON-EXPERT when their standing in the exchange rests on lived experience or hands-on practice rather than on a credential, a research post, a regulatory office or a technical role in a company - farmers, growers, fishers, beekeepers, residents, patients and their families, carers, frontline manual workers, market vendors, shop and salon staff, artisans, consumers, students, volunteers, indigenous community members. EXPERT covers professors and researchers, physicians, dentists, nurses and medical technologists, regulators and officials, company scientists, engineers, technical directors, QA and regulatory-affairs staff, investors and corporate managers, lawyers, ethicists and social scientists, peer iGEM teams and alumni. The hard case the brief names - a farmer with a degree - I resolved toward NON-EXPERT when the person speaks about running their own operation, and toward EXPERT when they are employed to advise other people's operations. Mr Lu of Worldshaper-Shanghai, described as a grower and extension author, is counted non-expert on that rule and is the clearest instance of it; Yusong Shi of GYHS, a doctoral student who is also a stony-coral hobbyist, is counted expert on the same rule, and GYHS's Conservation cell would move if that call reversed. A team counts in the last column if at least one documented loop was closed by a non-expert; ten of the sixteen changed something physical (sensor, delivery route, formulation, containment architecture) and six changed deployment scope, target user or a selection criterion. Twelve further teams have a documented non-expert input that changed only claims, language, education material or success framing, and those are counted as expert-closed, which is the same line the earlier analysis drew. Counting only physical changes gives nine or ten rather than the earlier analysis's 'six or seven in 93'; the difference is thirteen extra files plus formulation and delivery-route changes I counted and it did not, and this is the one place the two analyses differ. Villages: 50 of the 106 files carry no village string, and the high-school section does not have fine-grained villages at all - it competes in four merged clusters, so GEMS-Taiwan's agricultural project sat in the Space / Foundational Advance / Software & AI / Biomanufacturing cluster. I therefore assigned every team to one of the thirteen collegiate villages by where the technology is deployed and who it affects, using the official label from results2026.json where one exists. Several assignments are genuinely arguable - Cornell's smart bandage sits in Fashion & Cosmetics because that is the village it won, QingdaoAcademy and MIT-MAHE could be read as Food rather than Biomanufacturing, Mingdao and TU Darmstadt as Bioremediation rather than Biomanufacturing - and a different reading would move single teams between rows without changing the platform-versus-applied result. What this cannot see: whether a change was made because of the advice or attributed to it afterwards; the wiki behind the file summary, except for Athens and HUST-China, whose pages I read directly to check two borderline calls; whether a loop recorded as expert-closed had an unrecorded non-expert behind it; and whether judges preferred credentialled stakeholders, which is a plausible alternative explanation for the platform-village result that these files cannot settle. Nine of the thirteen village cells have fewer than eight closed loops and are flagged in the table; Agriculture at 3 of 4 is the single most quotable cell and the least load-bearing.","method_zh":"母體：磁碟上全部 106 份隊伍檔案，每一支都是 Top 10 或特別獎的得主或入圍者，因此這是 iGEM 2026 中受獎最多的十分之一，而不是整個競賽的抽樣。迴路評分：先前 ihp-depth 分析已評分的 93 支隊伍沿用該分析的分數不變，而「閉合了迴路」即該分析的 4 分——具名的利害關係人、一句具體說了什麼，以及建構、部署、讀出、安全設計或商業模式上的一項改變。有 13 份檔案是在那次評分之後才到的（BASIS-China、BGI-College、Bist-China、Michigan、NCKU-Tainan、NU Boston、Squirrel-Beijing、TU Darmstadt、Tsinghua-T、UBC-Vancouver、UiOslo-Norway、WHU-China、XJTLU-Software）；這 13 支由我以同一套評分標準自行評分，其中 7 支達到 4 分，因此是 106 中的 71，對應先前的 93 中的 64。非專家判準，在開始分類之前就先寫下：當一個人在這場對話中的立足點來自親身經驗或動手實務，而不是來自資歷、研究職位、主管機關職務或公司裡的技術角色時，即計為**非專家**——農民、種植者、漁民、養蜂人、居民、病人與家屬、照顧者、第一線體力工作者、市場攤商、店員與沙龍人員、工匠、消費者、學生、志工、原住民社群成員。**專家**則涵蓋教授與研究人員、醫師、牙醫、護理師與醫檢師、主管機關人員與官員、企業科學家、工程師、技術總監、品保與法規事務人員、投資人與企業經理人、律師、倫理學者與社會科學家，以及同儕 iGEM 隊伍與校友。委託說明特別點名的難題——有學位的農民——我的處理方式是：當這個人談的是經營自己的場域時計為非專家，當他受雇去指導別人的場域時計為專家。Worldshaper-Shanghai 的 Mr Lu 被描述為「種植者兼推廣作者」，依此規則計為非專家，也是這條規則最清楚的一個案例；GYHS 的 Yusong Shi 是博士生同時也是硬珊瑚玩家，依同一規則計為專家，而若這個判斷反過來，GYHS 所在的 Conservation 欄位數字就會變動。只要有至少一條記載在案的迴路由非專家閉上，該隊伍就計入最後一欄；16 支之中有 10 支改了實體的東西（感測器、投遞路徑、劑型、圍堵架構），另外 6 支改的是部署範圍、目標使用者或選擇判準。另有 12 支隊伍有記載在案的非專家輸入，但只改了主張、用詞、教育素材或成功的框架，這些仍計為由專家閉合，和先前分析劃的是同一條線。若只計實體改變，得到的是 9 到 10 支，而非先前分析所說的「93 中的六或七支」；差異來自多出的 13 份檔案，加上我把劑型與投遞路徑的改變也計入而該分析沒有——這是兩份分析唯一相異之處。村落：106 份檔案中有 50 份沒有村落欄位字串，而高中組根本沒有細分村落，它們是在四個合併的集群中競賽，所以 GEMS-Taiwan 的農業專案被放在 Space / Foundational Advance / Software & AI / Biomanufacturing 這個集群裡。因此我依「技術部署在哪裡、影響到誰」，把每一支隊伍指派到十三個大專組村落之一，有官方標籤者（來自 results2026.json）即採用官方標籤。有幾個指派確實可以爭論——Cornell 的智慧敷料放在 Fashion & Cosmetics，是因為那是它得獎的村落；QingdaoAcademy 與 MIT-MAHE 也可讀成 Food 而非 Biomanufacturing；Mingdao 與 TU Darmstadt 可讀成 Bioremediation 而非 Biomanufacturing——不同讀法會讓個別隊伍在列與列之間移動，但不會改變「平台型 vs 應用型」這個結果。這份分析看不到的：一項改變究竟是因為那個建議而做，還是事後才歸因於它；檔案摘要背後的 wiki，除了 Athens 與 HUST-China 這兩個邊界案例的頁面我直接讀過以外；一條被記為由專家閉合的迴路背後，是否有未被記錄的非專家；以及評審是否偏好有資歷的利害關係人——這是平台型村落結果的一個合理替代解釋，而這些檔案無法裁決。十三個村落欄位中有九個的閉合迴路少於八條，已在表中標示；Agriculture 的 4 中有 3 是最好引用、也最撐不住重量的一格。"},{"tab":"overview","kicker":"How to read this","title":"Two questions, thirty teams","title_zh":"兩個問題，三十支團隊","lede":"This report asks the same two questions of every team it looks at.","lede_zh":"本報告對每一支團隊都問同樣的兩個問題。","body":"The first question is computational. Where does a project stop being wet biology and start being a model, a pipeline, a dataset, a piece of software? What did that layer actually decide — did it change an experiment, or was it decoration added after the fact? The teams that win are increasingly the ones where the answer is \"it changed the experiment\".\n\nThe second question is social. Who outside the team touched this project, and what did they change about it? A list of meetings is not integrated human practices. A design that is visibly different because somebody outside the lab said something is.\n\nEverything else here — the trend tabs, the roadmap — exists to answer a third question that only GEMS Research can answer: given what 2026 looked like, what should a growing research institution in Taiwan be building in 2027 and beyond?","body_zh":"第一個問題關於運算。一個專案在哪裡不再只是濕實驗生物學，而開始成為模型、管線、資料集或軟體？這一層究竟決定了什麼——它改變了實驗，還是事後補上的裝飾？越來越多得獎團隊的答案是「它改變了實驗」。\n\n第二個問題關於社會。團隊之外有誰接觸過這個專案，而他們改變了什麼？列一串會議紀錄不是整合式人類實踐；因為實驗室外的某個人說了什麼，而讓設計明顯不同，才是。\n\n其餘的部分——趨勢頁、路線圖——都是為了回答第三個只有 GEMS Research 能回答的問題：看過 2026 年的樣貌之後，一個在台灣成長中的研究機構，在 2027 年以後應該建造什麼？"},{"tab":"roadmap","kicker":"Premise","title":"Why the dry lab is the roadmap","title_zh":"為什麼乾實驗室就是路線圖","lede":"GEMS Research is becoming an institution, not a team. Institutions are defined by what they can still do after the current students graduate.","lede_zh":"GEMS Research 正在從一支團隊成為一個機構。機構的定義，在於現在這批學生畢業之後，它還能做什麼。","body":"A wet lab is bounded by its benches, its reagents budget and the hours its students are physically present. A dry lab is bounded by what its people know and what they have written down. That asymmetry is the whole argument: computational capability compounds across years in a way that pipetting skill does not, because a model, a pipeline or a calibrated measurement protocol survives the student who built it.\n\nThis is also where the field has moved. Protein design, metabolic modelling and measurement standardisation are no longer the specialist corner of a project — in 2026 they are frequently the project. The teams on the 2026 podium did not win because they ran more gels.\n\nSo the roadmap below is deliberately about capability, not about any single 2027 project idea. Pick a phase and start.","body_zh":"濕實驗室受限於實驗檯、試劑預算，以及學生實際在場的時數。乾實驗室則受限於人員所知，以及他們寫下了什麼。這個不對稱就是整個論點：運算能力會跨年度累積，而移液技巧不會——因為一個模型、一條管線或一份校正過的量測流程，會比建造它的那位學生留得更久。\n\n這也是整個領域移動的方向。蛋白質設計、代謝建模與量測標準化不再是專案裡的專家角落；在 2026 年，它們經常就是專案本身。站上 2026 頒獎台的團隊，不是因為多跑了幾道膠。\n\n因此以下的路線圖刻意談能力，而不是任何單一的 2027 專案構想。挑一個階段，開始做。"},{"tab":"roadmap","kicker":"The convergence","title":"Two independent analyses, one answer","title_zh":"兩份獨立分析，同一個答案","lede":"The academic trend review and the industry trend review were run separately, from different sources, with no knowledge of each other. They landed on the same white space.","lede_zh":"學術趨勢分析與產業趨勢分析分開進行、來源不同、彼此互不知情。它們指向了同一塊空白地帶。","body":"From the literature side: light has matured from a laboratory curiosity into a real-time actuator for closed-loop control of fermentation, with reported titre gains around 60% in a 1 L photobioreactor — and optogenetics in **Bacillus subtilis** is a twelve-paper literature in the whole of PubMed.\n\nFrom the industry side, reached by an entirely different route: optogenetics is becoming the control and cleaning layer of bioprocessing, because light lets you retrofit an existing steel fermenter instead of building a new one. That makes it the cheapest route past the capital-expenditure wall that is currently the binding constraint on biomanufacturing.\n\nGEMS Research already stands in that gap. ReLEAF was a CcaS/CcaR optogenetic circuit in *Bacillus subtilis* driving a bioreactor, and it won Best Measurement and Best Hardware at high-school level for exactly the instrumentation this line needs. The competition project is over; the research line it opened is not.\n\nThere is a second, blunter finding underneath this. Taiwan's state-backed biotechnology push is a manufacturing play — contract development and manufacturing, GMP capacity — with no visible synthetic-biology **design** layer, while Singapore and Israel are explicitly funding exactly that layer. A small institution cannot out-build a CDMO. It can occupy the design position that nobody in Taiwan currently holds.","body_zh":"從文獻端看：光已經從實驗室的新奇玩意，成熟為可即時操控發酵的閉迴路致動器，1 公升光生物反應器中回報約 60% 的效價提升——而**枯草桿菌（Bacillus subtilis）**的光遺傳學，在整個 PubMed 中只有十二篇文獻。\n\n從產業端看，循著完全不同的路徑：光正在成為生物製程的控制與清潔層，因為光讓你可以改裝既有的不鏽鋼發酵槽，而不必蓋一座新的。這使它成為繞過資本支出高牆最便宜的路徑——而資本支出正是當前生物製造的關鍵瓶頸。\n\nGEMS Research 已經站在這個缺口上。ReLEAF 本來就是在*枯草桿菌*中以 CcaS/CcaR 光遺傳電路驅動生物反應器，並且正是憑著這條路線所需要的儀器化能力，在高中組拿下最佳量測與最佳硬體。競賽專案結束了，它打開的研究路線沒有。\n\n底下還有第二個更直白的發現。台灣由國家支持的生技推動是製造導向的——委託開發製造、GMP 產能——看不到合成生物學的**設計**層；而新加坡與以色列正明確地投資的，正是這一層。一個小型機構無法在產能上贏過 CDMO，但它可以佔住台灣目前沒有人佔住的設計位置。"}],"roadmap":[{"title":"Phase 1 · Make the current work reproducible","title_zh":"階段一 · 讓現有工作可重現","when":"0–3 months","when_zh":"0–3 個月","lede":"Before building anything new, make what already exists survivable by the next cohort.","lede_zh":"在建造新東西之前，先讓既有成果能被下一屆接手。","items":["**Put every analysis in version control.** One GEMS Research GitHub organisation, one repository per project, with the raw data, the notebook and the figure-generating script in the same place. If a figure cannot be regenerated from the repository, it does not count as a result.","**Write down the measurement protocols.** Calibration standards, units, replicate counts, how uncertainty was computed. The 2026 Best Measurement teams all did this; it is the cheapest credibility a dry lab can buy.","**Tag the provenance of every number.** The most copyable device in the whole 2026 field: TU Delft labels every cell of its decision matrix Factual, Inferred, Estimated or Speculative, with a legend saying the tag records the evidence and not the judgement; GEMS-Taiwan's own dose ledger runs a rail that turns from green to amber exactly where measurement stops and modelling begins. Make it the house format for every table and figure. It costs a column and it is the fastest way to be believed.","**Standardise the environment.** One `environment.yml` or `requirements.txt` per project, Python 3.12+, pinned versions. A student should be able to clone and run in under ten minutes.","**Archive the 2026 ReLEAF dry lab properly** — the OD600 signal processing, the optogenetic circuit model, the hardware firmware — as the first entry in the institutional record.","**Write the one-page biosecurity and ordering policy.** The US National Policy for Nucleic Acid Synthesis Screening (November 2026) now ties federal funding to buying synthetic DNA only from certified providers that screen orders of 50+ nucleotides. Mirror it: certified suppliers only, a documented internal review of any sequence design, an explicit scope statement excluding pathogen and toxin sequences, signed by every student before their first order. It costs an afternoon and it is the first thing a serious partner asks about."],"items_zh":["**把所有分析放進版本控制。** 一個 GEMS Research GitHub organisation，一個專案一個 repository，原始資料、notebook 與產生圖表的腳本放在同一處。若一張圖無法從 repository 重新產生，它就不算結果。","**寫下量測流程。** 校正標準品、單位、重複次數、不確定度如何計算。2026 年所有最佳量測獎團隊都做到了這點；這是乾實驗室能買到最便宜的可信度。","**為每一個數字標註來源。** 這是整個 2026 年最值得照抄的裝置：TU Delft 在決策矩陣的每一格標上 Factual、Inferred、Estimated 或 Speculative，並附圖例說明「標籤記錄的是證據，不是判斷」；GEMS-Taiwan 自己的劑量帳本則有一條軌道，正好在量測結束、模擬開始之處由綠轉琥珀。把它訂為所有表格與圖的統一格式。它只花一個欄位，卻是最快讓人相信你的方法。","**統一環境。** 每個專案一份 `environment.yml` 或 `requirements.txt`，Python 3.12 以上，版本鎖定。學生應該能在十分鐘內 clone 下來就跑起來。","**妥善歸檔 2026 ReLEAF 的乾實驗室成果** —— OD600 訊號處理、光遺傳電路模型、硬體韌體 —— 作為機構紀錄的第一筆。","**寫下一頁的生物安全與訂購政策。** 美國《核酸合成篩查國家政策》（2026 年 11 月）已將聯邦經費與「只向通過認證、且會篩查 50 個核苷酸以上訂單的供應商購買合成 DNA」綁在一起。比照辦理：僅限認證供應商、任何序列設計都要有書面內部審查、明確排除病原與毒素序列，並由每位學生在第一次下單前簽署。這只需要一個下午，而且是認真的合作對象第一個會問的事。"],"outcome":"A new student can reproduce any 2026 figure from the repository alone, without asking anybody.","outcome_zh":"新進學生只靠 repository 就能重現 2026 年的任何一張圖，不需要問任何人。"},{"title":"Phase 2 · Build the core modelling skill","title_zh":"階段二 · 建立核心建模能力","when":"3–9 months","when_zh":"3–9 個月","lede":"Two tracks, taught deliberately, with a real deliverable at the end of each.","lede_zh":"兩條軌道，刻意教學，每條都有真實的產出。","items":["**Track A — dynamical systems.** ODE models of genetic circuits, parameter fitting to the team's own data, sensitivity analysis, identifiability. Tools: Python with SciPy and lmfit, Tellurium/COPASI for the SBML side. Deliverable: a circuit model fitted to real GEMS time-course data, with confidence intervals on every parameter.","**Track B — structural and sequence modelling.** Structure prediction is now free infrastructure: the open models (Boltz-2, Chai-1, OpenFold3, ColabFold) match or beat the gated flagship, so folding a protein is a commodity step, not a project. Put one shared GPU box or a modest cloud budget behind an internal queue, make \"fold it, then read the confidence metrics\" compulsory in every project, and teach the hard part — knowing when pLDDT and PAE are lying to you. Deliverable: a designed or selected variant with a documented computational rationale, taken to the bench.","**Teach the four controls, and make them compulsory.** This is where the 53%-against-23% finding becomes a syllabus. Split calibration from validation before fitting anything. Cluster near-duplicate sequences and split whole clusters across folds, so a model cannot memorise a near-copy. Run a label-shuffle control that must collapse to chance. Run an ablation that strips the information you claim to be using. Eton-College-UK did all four at high-school level with logistic regression and a scoring matrix; the controls, not the model, are what made it credible.","**Teach uncertainty before teaching models.** Error propagation, replicate design, what a fit actually claims. Most student models fail here, not at the mathematics.","**Run a weekly dry-lab clinic.** One hour, somebody presents a figure, everyone else attacks it. This is how modelling taste transmits between cohorts."],"items_zh":["**軌道 A —— 動力系統。** 基因電路的 ODE 模型、以自身資料擬合參數、敏感度分析、可辨識性。工具：Python 搭配 SciPy 與 lmfit，SBML 端使用 Tellurium/COPASI。產出：一個以 GEMS 真實時間序列資料擬合的電路模型，每個參數都附信賴區間。","**軌道 B —— 結構與序列建模。** 結構預測現在已是免費的基礎設施：開源模型（Boltz-2、Chai-1、OpenFold3、ColabFold）已可匹敵甚至超越封閉的旗艦模型，因此「把蛋白質折出來」是一個標準步驟，而不是一個專案。配置一台共用 GPU 主機或一筆適度的雲端預算，架一個內部排程佇列，規定每個專案都必須「先折、再讀信心指標」，並教真正困難的部分——判斷 pLDDT 與 PAE 什麼時候在騙你。產出：一個經過設計或篩選的變體，附上完整的運算理由，並實際進到實驗檯。","**教那四項對照，並列為必做。** 這就是「53% 對 23%」這個發現落地成課綱的地方。在擬合任何東西之前先把校正組與驗證組分開。把近似重複的序列分群，並讓整群落在同一個 fold，使模型無法記住近似副本。跑標籤洗牌對照，其表現必須塌回隨機水準。跑一個消融測試，剝除你宣稱正在使用的那項資訊。Eton-College-UK 在高中階段用 logistic regression 與計分矩陣就做完了這四項；讓結果可信的是那些對照，不是模型。","**先教不確定度，再教模型。** 誤差傳遞、重複設計、一次擬合究竟主張了什麼。多數學生模型敗在這裡，而不是數學。","**每週一次乾實驗室診療會。** 一小時，一個人報一張圖，其他人負責挑戰它。建模的品味就是這樣在屆與屆之間傳下去的。"],"outcome":"Two or three students who can independently build, fit and defend a model with its controls — and who can teach the next two or three.","outcome_zh":"有兩三位學生能獨立建立、擬合模型並連同對照一起為它辯護——而且能教會下兩三位。"},{"title":"Phase 3 · Ship one tool the outside world uses","title_zh":"階段三 · 做出一個外界真的會用的工具","when":"9–18 months","when_zh":"9–18 個月","lede":"The difference between a competition team and a research centre is whether anybody outside uses what you built.","lede_zh":"競賽團隊與研究中心的差別，在於外界有沒有人用你做的東西。","items":["**Commit to the Bacillus optogenetics line.** Both trend reviews independently pointed here. Port and properly characterise a CcaS/CcaR or LOV-based light-inducible cassette in *B. subtilis* with full dose-response, dynamic range and growth-stage characterisation. In a twelve-paper literature that is on its own a publishable contribution, and it is the natural continuation of ReLEAF rather than a fresh start.","**Pick one narrow, real problem** that GEMS has genuine data on — the strongest candidate is the optogenetic induction and OD600 measurement work from ReLEAF, where GEMS already has instrumentation, data and a Best Measurement award behind it.","**Buy the domain and host it before the freeze.** This is the single habit that separated the award-winning iGEM 2026 software that is still usable today from the software that is not. Of 21 award-winning tools checked, 8 are live; every one of those was hosted on freeze day, and every source-only tool's wiki lists localhost as its only address. It is a hosting decision made months early, not a coding or budget one — two high-school teams out-shipped most of the universities on exactly this. Write the documentation around a URL, not an install command.","**Build it as a deployed web tool, not a notebook.** Documented, licensed, with example data, a DOI, and a URL anybody can open. Teams that only publish source code get used by nobody.","**Design for other people's data from day one.** Input format, validation, error messages. This is the single most common failure in iGEM software.","**Expect nobody to come.** Across every award-winning 2026 repository checked, stars and forks were zero, and the only external-adoption figure found anywhere was Stanford's SynBase reporting 837 learners. Uni-Padua-IT publicly offered to optimise any team's sequence and got no replies, and said so on their wiki. Publishing is necessary and not sufficient: the three outside users below have to be recruited by hand.","**Get three outside users and write down what broke.** Other Taiwanese schools, a university lab, a 2027 iGEM team. Their complaints are the roadmap for version two."],"items_zh":["**確立枯草桿菌光遺傳學這條路線。** 兩份趨勢分析各自獨立地指向這裡。在 *B. subtilis* 中移植並完整表徵一組 CcaS/CcaR 或 LOV 型的光誘導卡匣，做出完整的劑量反應、動態範圍與生長期表徵。在一個只有十二篇文獻的領域裡，光是這件事本身就足以發表，而且這是 ReLEAF 的自然延伸，不是重新開始。","**挑一個狹窄而真實的問題**，而且 GEMS 手上有真正的資料——最強的候選是 ReLEAF 的光遺傳誘導與 OD600 量測工作，GEMS 已經有儀器、有資料，背後還有一座最佳量測獎。","**在 wiki 凍結前就把網域買好、把服務架起來。** 這是唯一一個把「今天還能用」的 iGEM 2026 得獎軟體，和「今天不能用」的區分開來的習慣。在檢查的 21 個得獎工具中，有 8 個仍然在線；這 8 個無一例外在凍結當日就已經上線，而所有只有原始碼的工具，其 wiki 上唯一的位址都是 localhost。這是一個提前好幾個月做的「要不要架站」決定，不是寫程式或預算的決定——有兩支高中隊伍正是靠這一點，交付得比多數大學還好。文件要圍繞一個網址來寫，而不是圍繞一行安裝指令。","**把它做成已部署的網頁工具，而不是 notebook。** 有文件、有授權、有範例資料、有 DOI，以及任何人都能打開的網址。只釋出原始碼的團隊，沒有人會用。","**從第一天就為別人的資料設計。** 輸入格式、驗證、錯誤訊息。這是 iGEM 軟體最常見的單一失敗原因。","**不要期待有人會自己找上門。** 在檢查過的每一個 2026 得獎 repository 中，star 與 fork 都是零，而唯一能找到的外部採用數字，是 Stanford 的 SynBase 回報的 837 位學習者。Uni-Padua-IT 公開表示願意為任何團隊最佳化序列，結果沒有人回應，而他們把這件事寫在 wiki 上。釋出是必要條件而非充分條件：下面那三位外部使用者，必須一個一個親手去找。","**找到三位外部使用者，並記錄哪裡壞了。** 其他台灣學校、一間大學實驗室、一支 2027 iGEM 團隊。他們的抱怨就是第二版的路線圖。"],"outcome":"A tool with a URL, a licence, documentation and users who are not GEMS students.","outcome_zh":"一個有網址、有授權、有文件，而且使用者不是 GEMS 學生的工具。"},{"title":"Phase 4 · Become a place other people come to","title_zh":"階段四 · 成為別人會來的地方","when":"18 months +","when_zh":"18 個月以上","lede":"Institutional standing comes from being useful to people who owe you nothing.","lede_zh":"機構地位來自於：對那些不欠你任何東西的人仍然有用。","items":["**Run a dry-lab school for Taiwanese iGEM and high-school teams.** Modelling, measurement, reproducibility. Teaching forces the material to become transmissible, and it builds the network that later supplies collaborators.","**Approach the three Taiwanese teams the analysis identified by name.** NTHU Taiwan (team 6416, Hsinchu) is a separate NTHU entry running engineered *Bacillus subtilis* in a moving-bed reactor — the closest technical match to GEMS on the island, and the natural partner for a joint *B. subtilis* measurement standard. CCU-Taiwan (6408, Chiayi) worked on rice, the same crop as ReLEAF, so a shared Taiwan rice-stress dataset with a published benchmark is a one-season project. Labi-Taiwan (6511) won the peer-voted iGEMers Prize and is the obvious co-teacher for a Taiwan high-school dry-lab school.","**Start a collaboration page, because GEMS does not have one.** The Taiwan analysis found GEMS-Taiwan appears on no other Taiwanese team's collaboration page and has none of its own, while NYCU-Taiwan's meet-up on 27 July drew 53 people from five teams. Being findable is a prerequisite for everything else in this phase.","**Publish.** A methods paper, a preprint, or a well-documented dataset. One citable artefact per year changes how every later conversation starts.","**Keep a standing partnership with a university lab and a non-academic stakeholder** — a farm, a clinic, a municipal body. The stakeholder relationship is what makes human practices real rather than performed, and it is the thing competition teams cannot build in nine months.","**Maintain the trend watch.** This report should be regenerated at least twice a year; the academic and industry tabs are built to be re-run."],"items_zh":["**為台灣的 iGEM 與高中團隊辦一所乾實驗室學校。** 建模、量測、可重現性。教學會逼迫內容變得可傳遞，也建立起日後提供合作者的人脈網絡。","**直接聯繫分析點名的三支台灣團隊。** NTHU Taiwan（隊伍 6416，新竹）是清大另一支獨立隊伍，在移動床反應器中培養工程化的*枯草桿菌*——全島與 GEMS 技術上最接近的一支，也是共同建立 *B. subtilis* 量測標準的天然夥伴。CCU-Taiwan（6408，嘉義）做的是水稻，與 ReLEAF 同一作物，因此「共享台灣稻作逆境資料集並公開基準」是一季之內可完成的專案。Labi-Taiwan（6511）拿下同儕票選的 iGEMers Prize，是共同開辦台灣高中乾實驗室學校最明顯的人選。","**開一個 collaboration 頁面，因為 GEMS 根本沒有。** 台灣分析發現 GEMS-Taiwan 沒有出現在任何其他台灣團隊的合作頁面上，自己也沒有一個；而 NYCU-Taiwan 在 7 月 27 日的聚會吸引了來自五支隊伍的 53 人。能被找到，是這個階段其他每一件事的前提。","**發表。** 一篇方法論文、一份預印本，或一套文件完整的資料集。每年一個可被引用的產物，會改變此後每一次對話的起點。","**與一間大學實驗室和一個非學術利害關係人維持長期夥伴關係** —— 一座農場、一間診所、一個地方機關。利害關係人關係是讓人類實踐成為真實而非表演的關鍵，也是競賽團隊在九個月內建立不起來的東西。","**持續追蹤趨勢。** 這份報告每年至少重新生成兩次；學術與產業頁就是為了可重跑而設計的。"],"outcome":"GEMS Research is cited, invited and asked for help by people who were never GEMS students.","outcome_zh":"GEMS Research 被從未是 GEMS 學生的人引用、邀請並尋求協助。"}]};
